window.KB_BODY[38]={"50-018-017":"<h3>Specifications</h3><h4>Lubricating Oil Pressure, Main Oil Rifle (15W-40 oil at 107°C [225°F]):</h4><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Minimum at rated rpm</th><th>465 kPa [67.5 psi]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Maximum at rated rpm</th><th>552 kPa [80 psi]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Minimum at idle rpm</th><th>172 kPa [25 psi]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><h4>Oil Pump - Pumping Capacity</h4><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Maximum at Rated Speed (1900 rpm)</th><th>1420 liters/min [375 gal/min]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><h4>Lubricating Oil Temperature</h4><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Maximum</th><th>120°C [248°F]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><h4>Eliminator Oil Capacity - Engine Operation</h4><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Maximum</th><th>20 liters [5.2 gal]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><h4>Sump Configuration - System Capacity</h4><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Center Sump - Low Level</th><th>242.5 liters [64 gal]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Center Sump - High Level</th><th>280 liters [74 gal]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Rear Sump - Low Level</th><th>242.5 liters [64 gal]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Rear Sump - High Level</th><th>280 liters [74 gal]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>","56-000-001":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><p>Industrial and Power Generation</p><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Coolant is toxic. Keep away from small children and pets. If not reused, dispose of in accordance with local environmental regulations.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not remove the pressure cap from a hot engine. Wait until the coolant temperature is below 50°C [120°F] before removing the pressure cap. Heated coolant spray or steam can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of personal injury, avoid direct contact of hot oil with your skin.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Some state and federal agencies have determined that used engine oil can be carcinogenic and cause reproductive toxicity. Avoid inhalation of vapors, ingestion, and prolonged contact with used engine oil. If not reused dispose of in accordance with local environmental regulations.</p></div></div><ul><li>Attach a tag to all hoses, lines, linkages, and electrical connections, as they are removed, to identify location and aid the installation process.</li><li>Disconnect the battery cables.</li><li>Drain the engine coolant. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-018-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-018</a> (Cooling System) in Section 8.</li><li>Drain the lubricating oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-037</a> (Lubricating Oil System) in Section 7.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/fp8hola.png\" alt=\"fp8hola.png\"></figure><p>QSK60 Marine Applications</p><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Coolant is toxic. Keep away from small children and pets. If not reused, dispose of in accordance with local environmental regulations.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not remove the pressure cap from a hot engine. Wait until the coolant temperature is below 50°C [120°F] before removing the pressure cap. Heated coolant spray or steam can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of personal injury, avoid direct contact of hot oil with your skin.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Some state and federal agencies have determined that used engine oil can be carcinogenic and cause reproductive toxicity. Avoid inhalation of vapors, ingestion, and prolonged contact with used engine oil. If not reused dispose of in accordance with local environmental regulations.</p></div></div><ul><li>Attach a tag to all hoses, lines, linkages, and electrical connections, as they are removed, to identify location and aid the installation process.</li><li>Disconnect the battery cables.</li><li>Drain the engine coolant. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-018-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-018</a> (Cooling System) in Section 8.</li><li>Drain the lubricating oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-037</a> (Lubricating Oil System) in Section 7.</li><li>Remove aftercooler heat shields. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-010-129-tr\">Refer to Procedure 010-129</a> (Aftercooler Heat Shield) in Section 10.</li><li>Remove the turbocharger heat shields. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-010-076-tr\">Refer to Procedure 010-076</a> (Turbocharger Heat Shield) in Section 10.</li><li>Remove the turbocharger inlet connections. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-010-130-tr\">Refer to Procedure 010-130</a> (Turbocharger Inlet Connections) in Section 10.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><p>Disconnect the starter cable, engine ground straps, cab or chassis to engine hoses, tubing, electrical wires, and hydraulic lines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/13200042.png\" alt=\"13200042.png\"></figure><p>Disconnect the intake and exhaust system pipes.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/oi400hc.png\" alt=\"oi400hc.png\"></figure><p>Disconnect the drive units from the flywheel housing and flywheel.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/tr400wa.png\" alt=\"tr400wa.png\"></figure><p>Disconnect the OEM wiring harness from the ECM.</p><ul><li>For QSK45 engines, refer to the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, QSK19, QSK23, QSK45, QSK60, and QSK78 Engines, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666113\">3666113</a>.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19400309.png\" alt=\"19400309.png\"></figure><h4>with Electronically Actuated Injector</h4><ul><li>For QSK60 engines, refer to the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, QSK38, QSK50 and QSK60 (CM850 Modular Common Rail System), Bulletin 4021533.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19601401.png\" alt=\"19601401.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If a liquid refrigerant system (air conditioning) is used, wear eye and face protection, and wrap a cloth around the fittings before removing. Liquid refrigerant can cause serious eye and skin injuries.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To protect the environment, liquid refrigerant systems must be properly emptied and filled using equipment that prevents the release of refrigerant gas into the atmosphere. Federal law requires capturing and recycling the refrigerant.</p></div></div><p>Remove air conditioning lines if needed.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/oi800qb.png\" alt=\"oi800qb.png\"></figure><p>Remove all chassis components necessary to remove the engine from the equipment.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00600043.png\" alt=\"00600043.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Inspect the engine lifting brackets for damage or cracks. Do not attempt to lift the engine if any cracks or damage are visible. Using damaged lifting equipment can cause serious personal injury and/or property damage.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The QSK45 and QSK60 series engines can weigh as much as 9980 kg [22,000 lb]. Use a properly rated hoist and engine lifting fixture, Part Number 3163264, to lift the engine. Rigging and lifting must be done by trained, experienced personnel.</p></div></div><p>The engine lifting fixtures, Part Number 3163264, are designed to lift the engine <b>only</b>. Any additional components attached (including to the drive end, non-drive end and/or chassis) <b>must</b> be removed.</p><p>For engine weights, <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-018-015-tr\">Refer to Procedure 018-015</a> (Specifications, General Engine) in Section V.</p><p>Inspect the engine lifting brackets for cracks.</p><p>The engine lifting equipment is designed to lift the engine safely.</p><p>The lifting fixture, Part Number 3163264, is designed to lift a maximum of 11,340 kg [25,000 lb].</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00600042.png\" alt=\"00600042.png\"></figure><p>Use a properly rated hoist and lifting fixture to support the weight of the engine. Remove the front and rear engine support capscrews.</p><p>Use a properly rated hoist and engine lifting fixture, Part Number 3163264, to remove the engine.</p><p>The lifting force <b>must</b> be in a straight vertical line with the lifting brackets in both directions.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00600040.png\" alt=\"00600040.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The oil sump or cover plate will not support the weight of the engine. The engine will fall and personal injury can result.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Use a stand or skid that contacts the engine mounts. The stand must hold the weight of the engine and provide permanent support to prevent the engine from falling.</p></div></div><p>Place the engine on the stand.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ew4suha.png\" alt=\"ew4suha.png\"></figure><p>Cover all engine openings to prevent dirt and debris from entering the engine.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/tb4otla.png\" alt=\"tb4otla.png\"></figure><p>Remove all remaining accessories and brackets that will be used on the replacement engine.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ew400hc.png\" alt=\"ew400hc.png\"></figure>","56-000-002":"<h3>Install</h3><p>Industrial and Power Generation</p><p>Install all accessories and brackets that were removed from the engine.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ew400hc.png\" alt=\"ew400hc.png\"></figure><p>The engine lifting fixtures, Part Number 3163264, are designed to lift the engine <b>only</b>. Any additional components attached (including to the drive end, non-drive end and/or chassis) <b>must</b> be removed.</p><p>Use the following procedure to determine engine weights, <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-018-015-tr\">Refer to Procedure 018-015 in Section V.</a></p><p>The engine lifting equipment is designed to lift the engine safely. Do <b>not</b> lift the engine and drivetrain as an assembly.</p><p>The lifting fixture, Part Number 3163264, is designed to lift a maximum of 11,340 kg [25,000 lb].</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00600042.png\" alt=\"00600042.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Inspect the engine lifting brackets for damage or cracks. Do not attempt to lift the engine if any cracks or damage are visible. Using damaged lifting equipment can cause serious personal injury and/or property damage.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The QSK45 and QSK60 series engines can weigh as much as 9980 kg [22,000 lb]. Use a properly rated hoist and engine lifting fixture, Part Number 3163264, to lift the engine. Rigging and lifting must be done by trained, experienced personnel.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make sure all lines, hoses, and tubes are in good condition, properly routed, and fastened to prevent damage.</p></div></div><p>Use a properly rated hoist and engine lifting fixture, Part Number 3163264, to install the engine.</p><p>The lifting force <b>must</b> be in a straight vertical line with the lifting brackets in both directions.</p><p>Align the engine in the chassis, and tighten the engine mounting capscrews. Refer to the OEM&#x27;s torque specifications.</p><p>Connect all engine and chassis-mounted accessories that were removed.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00600040.png\" alt=\"00600040.png\"></figure><p>With the engine installed check the crankshaft end clearance to make sure it is still within specification. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-007-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-007 in Section 1.</a></p><p>Remove an accessible hand hole cover. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-035 in Section 1</a> The crankshaft can be moved forwards and backwards by using a pry bar on the crankshaft webs through the hand hole cover opening. The end clearance can be measured through the hand hole cover opening on a crankshaft counterweight or on the front damper.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not use a pry bar on the damper to move the crankshaft. Doing so may cause damage to the damper.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The oil pan is shown removed from the engine for illustration purposes.</p></div></div><p>Once the end clearance is confirmed to be within specification replace the hand hole cover. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-035 in Section 1</a>. If the end clearance is out of specification, check for misalignment with the attached drive units.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb1beja.png\" alt=\"mb1beja.png\"></figure><p>Connect the OEM wiring harness to the ECM.</p><ul><li>For QSK45 engines, refer to the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, QSK Fuel System, QSK19, QSK23, QSK45, QSK60, and QSK78 Engines, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666113\">3666113</a>.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19400309.png\" alt=\"19400309.png\"></figure><h4>Electronically Actuated Injector</h4><ul><li>For QSK60 engines, refer to the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, QSK38, QSK50 and QSK60 (CM850 Modular Common Rail System), Bulletin 4021533.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19601401.png\" alt=\"19601401.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To prevent the possibility of engine damage the engine must be prelubricated by pumping pressurized oil through the system prior to starting the engine.</p></div></div><p>Fill the engine with clean 15W-40 lubricating oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-037 in Section 7.</a></p><p>Determine the actual capacity by oil pan part number. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-018-017\">Refer to Procedure 018-017 in Section V.</a></p><p>Industrial engines are equipped with prelubrication devices from the factory. Engines other than industrial often do <b>not</b> have a prelubrication option. Follow the instructions below for the remote prelubrication process.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/pl4hohb.png\" alt=\"pl4hohb.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The lubricating oil system must be primed before operating the engine after rebuild to avoid internal component damage.</p></div></div><p>Use a pump capable of supplying 205-kPa [30-psi] continuous pressure. Connect the pump to the front of the oil filter head.</p><p>Use a supply of clean oil. Turn the pump to the ON position. Check the engine oil pressure gauge. When the gauge indicates oil pressure, begin monitoring the oil level in the oil pan.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/pl4hoha.png\" alt=\"pl4hoha.png\"></figure><p>Fill the cooling system with fully formulated coolant. Information is found in the Operation and Maintenance Manual, QSK45 and QSK60 Engines, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666260\">3666260</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-018-018\">Refer to Procedure 018-018 in Section 8.</a></p><p>Refer to the OEM&#x27;s specifications for radiator and system capacity.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08200020.png\" alt=\"08200020.png\"></figure><p>Perform a final inspection to make sure all hoses, wires, linkages, and components have been properly installed and tightened.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ew4cosa.png\" alt=\"ew4cosa.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not remove the pressure cap from a hot engine. Wait until the coolant temperature is below 50°C [120°F] before removing the pressure cap. Heated coolant spray or steam can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Operate the engine at low idle for 2 to 3 minutes.</p><p>Stop the engine and wait 5 to 7 minutes for the oil to drain to the oil pan. Check the oil and coolant levels.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/oi800dd.png\" alt=\"oi800dd.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><p>Industrial and Power Generation</p><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not remove the pressure cap from a hot engine. Wait until the coolant temperature is below 50°C [120°F] before removing the pressure cap. Heated coolant spray or steam can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><ul><li>Perform a final inspection to make sure all hoses, wires, linkages, and components have been properly installed and tightened.</li><li>Operate the engine at low idle for 2 to 3 minutes. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-014-006-tr\">Refer to Procedure 014-006 in Section 14.</a></li><li>Stop the engine and wait 5 to 7 minutes for the oil to drain to the oil pan. Check the oil and coolant levels.</li><li>Add oil or coolant to obtain the correct level if necessary. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-018-018\">Refer to Procedure 018-018 in Section 8.</a> <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-018-017\">Refer to Procedure 018-017 in Section V.</a></li><li>Operate the engine for 8 to 10 minutes to check for proper operation, unusual noises, and coolant, fuel, or lubricating oil leaks. Repair all leaks and component problems. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-014-006-tr\">Refer to Procedure 014-006 in Section 14.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><p>QSK60 Marine Applications</p><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not remove the pressure cap from a hot engine. Wait until the coolant temperature is below 50°C [120°F] before removing the pressure cap. Heated coolant spray or steam can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><ul><li>Install the turbocharger inlet connections. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-010-130-tr\">Refer to Procedure 010-130 in Section 10.</a></li><li>Install the turbocharger heat shields. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-010-076-tr\">Refer to Procedure 010-076 in Section 10.</a></li><li>Install the aftercooler heat shield. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-010-129-tr\">Refer to Procedure 010-129 in Section 10.</a></li><li>Perform a final inspection to make sure all hoses, wires, linkages, and components have been properly installed and tightened.</li><li>Operate the engine at low idle for 2 to 3 minutes. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-014-006-tr\">Refer to Procedure 014-006 in Section 14.</a></li><li>Stop the engine and wait 5 to 7 minutes for the oil to drain to the oil pan. Check the oil and coolant levels.</li><li>Add oil or coolant to obtain the correct level if necessary. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-018-018\">Refer to Procedure 018-018 in Section 8.</a> <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-018-017\">Refer to Procedure 018-017 in Section V.</a></li><li>Operate the engine for 8 to 10 minutes to check for proper operation, unusual noises, and coolant, fuel, or lubricating oil leaks. Repair all leaks and component problems. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-014-006-tr\">Refer to Procedure 014-006 in Section 14.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-000-014":"<h3>General Information</h3><p>The following recommendations are to prepare the engine for winter storage. <b>Not</b> all recommendations will apply to all applications. <b>Always</b> follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendation on components <b>not</b> manufactured by Cummins Inc.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/05600069.png\" alt=\"05600069.png\"></figure><p>Marine Applications</p><p>Fill the tank with good quality ASTM number 2D climatized diesel fuel.</p><p>Change the fuel filter. Refer to Section 4.</p><p>Change the boat fuel-water separator element. Refer to Section 3.</p><p>Change the engine lubricating oil and filters. Refer to Section 4.</p><p>Treat the fuel with diesel conditioner or algaecide to prevent the growth of algae in the fuel tank.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/05900717.png\" alt=\"05900717.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not run the engine with the sea water valve closed. This can damage the sea water pump and the engine. It is good practice to disable the engine or to place a tag at the helm(s) when the sea water valve is closed.</p></div></div><p>If the vessel is stored in the water, close the sea water valve on the vessel hull.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08600044.png\" alt=\"08600044.png\"></figure><p>Drain the sea water system.</p><p>Remove the drain plug on the marine gear cooler.</p><p>Remove the zinc anodes from the heat exchanger and the aftercooler. Refer to Section 4.</p><p>Remove the drain plug from the air box side of the sea water aftercooler, if equipped.</p><p>Remove the engine sea water hoses to drain sea water from the engine.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08900214.png\" alt=\"08900214.png\"></figure><p>Remove the inlet and outlet hoses from the heat exchanger.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08900215.png\" alt=\"08900215.png\"></figure><p>Remove the inlet and outlet hoses from the sea water pump.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08900216.png\" alt=\"08900216.png\"></figure><p>There are two different types of pumps. Use the appropriate procedure for the type of pump used.</p><p>Remove and inspect the sea water pump impeller. Refer to the manufacturer&#x27;s instructions.</p><p>If the sea water pump impeller is damaged or <b>not</b> reusable, do <b>not</b> install a new sea water pump impeller until the vessel is ready to be used.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08900217.png\" alt=\"08900217.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not expose the sea water pump impeller to sunlight, fluorescent lighting, or any source of ultra-violet light for an extended period of time. This will cause damage the sea water pump impeller.</p></div></div><p>The sea water pump impeller <b>must</b> be lubricated with glycerin or a nonpetroleum-based lubricant such as silicon spray.</p><p>Store the sea water pump impeller for the season in a polyethylene bag in a location void of sunlight, fluorescent light, or any other source of ultraviolet light.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08900218.png\" alt=\"08900218.png\"></figure><p>Install the zinc anodes in the heat exchanger and aftercooler. Refer to Section 4.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08900219.png\" alt=\"08900219.png\"></figure><p>Loosen the heat exchanger sea water outlet clamps (1 and 2).</p><p>Rotate the sea water outlet connection to a vertical position (3).</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08900220.png\" alt=\"08900220.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Coolant is toxic. Keep away from children and pets. If not reused, dispose of in accordance with local environmental regulations.</p></div></div><p>Place a container under the heat exchanger sea water inlet.</p><p>Pour the coolant, a 50/50 mixture of antifreeze and water, through the heat exchanger.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> allow excess coolant to drain into the bilge.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08900221.png\" alt=\"08900221.png\"></figure><p>Rotate and connect the sea water outlet connection to the exhaust elbow (1).</p><p>Tighten the hose clamps (2).</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>5 n•m [44 in-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08900222.png\" alt=\"08900222.png\"></figure><p>Empty the sea water stainer. Refer to Section 3.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08900223.png\" alt=\"08900223.png\"></figure><p>Perform the recommended maintenance procedures on the marine gear. Refer to the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations and specifications.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08900224.png\" alt=\"08900224.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><p>Disconnect and remove the battery. Refer to the manufacturer&#x27;s instructions.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ee8comk.png\" alt=\"ee8comk.png\"></figure>","56-000-999":"<h3>General Information</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Lifting the QSK45 or the QSK60 engine improperly can cause equipment damage, severe personnel injury, or death. Lifting must be completed by trained, experienced technicians in accordance with instructions in this manual.</p></div></div><p>The procedures required to replace an engine will vary with different engine models, the type of equipment, optional equipment, and the shop facilities. Use the following procedures as a guide.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>All removal and replacement steps do <b>not</b> apply to all types of equipment. Complete <b>only</b> the steps that apply to the equipment involved. Use the OEM&#x27;s recommendations and precautions for the removal and installation of chassis components needed to gain access to the engine.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00600040.png\" alt=\"00600040.png\"></figure>","56-001-001":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><ul><li>Remove the alternator drive pulley. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-009-010-tr\">Refer to Procedure 009-010 in Section 9.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><p>Remove the three hex head capscrews.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600041.png\" alt=\"01600041.png\"></figure><p>Remove the seal assembly from the gear cover and shaft.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If a washer is fitted behind the seal (applicable to engines built between January and June 2001), discard this washer, along with the old accessory drive seal.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600042.png\" alt=\"01600042.png\"></figure><h3>Machine</h3><p>If reusing the old pulley, machine 2.1 mm [0.08 in] from the length of the pulley and update the part number accordingly.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600217.png\" alt=\"01600217.png\"></figure><p>The illustration displays the pulley assembly:</p><ol><li>Shaft</li><li>Washer</li><li>Seal</li><li>Machined-off area of pulley (old pulley <b>only</b>)</li><li>Pulley</li></ol><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600224.png\" alt=\"01600224.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><p>The right-bank drive pulley does <b>not</b> require the mounting spacer provided in the drive seal service kit. Discard the spacer for the right-bank repair procedure.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600042.png\" alt=\"01600042.png\"></figure><p>Install the washer onto the shaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600221.png\" alt=\"01600221.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Care <b>must</b> be taken <b>not</b> to allow the wear sleeve to separate from the seal during handling.</p></div></div><p>Install the alternator drive seal.</p><p>Align the mounting holes, and insert the three capscrews.</p><p>Make sure to tighten the mounting capscrews evenly.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>10 n•m [89 in-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600041.png\" alt=\"01600041.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><ul><li>Install the alternator drive pulley. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-009-010-tr\">Refer to Procedure 009-010 in Section 9.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-001-003-shopas":"<h3>Install</h3><p>Separate the rotational and stationary part of the seal.</p><p>Locate the stationary part of the seal on the end of the seal installation tool, Part Number 5573257.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00r01581.png\" alt=\"00r01581.png\"></figure><p>Put the spacer on the shaft.</p><p>Slide the tool on to the end of the shaft.</p><p>Tap the end of the installation tool with a mallet to push the stationary part of the seal into the gear housing.</p><p>The spacer <b>must</b> be installed, or the seal will <b>not</b> locate correctly.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00r01582.png\" alt=\"00r01582.png\"></figure><p>Place the rotational part of the seal on top of the pulley shaft.</p><p>Use seal installation tool, Part Number 5573258 to install the seal on to the pulley with the aid of a mallet.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If you are moving from an older style seal that utilizes three bolts for installation to the new seal a new design pulley <b>must</b> also be purchased.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00r01583.png\" alt=\"00r01583.png\"></figure>","56-001-003-shopds":"<h3>Remove</h3><p>The rotational part of the seal is removed from the shaft and gear housing when removing the pulley. This <b>must</b> be removed from the pulley and discarded.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00r01579.png\" alt=\"00r01579.png\"></figure><p>Remove and discard the stationary part of the seal assembly from the gear cover and shaft.</p><p>Remove the spacer from the end of the shaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00r01580.png\" alt=\"00r01580.png\"></figure>","56-001-003-tr":"<h3>Select Service Tools</h3><h4>Recommended Cummins® Service Tools</h4><ul><li>Seal installation tool, Part Number 5573257</li><li>Seal installation tool, Part Number 5573258</li></ul><h4>Additional Service Items</h4><ul><li>No additional service items required.</li></ul><h3>General Information</h3><p>This procedure is to remove and install the press fit style accessory drive seal. There is an older seal which uses three capscrews for installation which is <b>not</b> discussed in this procedure.</p><h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><ul><li>Remove the accessory drive pulley. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-009-004-tr\">Refer to Procedure 009-004 in Section 9.</a></li></ul><h3>Remove</h3><p>The rotational part of the seal is removed from the shaft and gear housing when removing the pulley. This <b>must</b> be removed from the pulley and discarded.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00r01579.png\" alt=\"00r01579.png\"></figure><p>Remove and discard the stationary part of the seal assembly from the gear cover and shaft.</p><p>Remove the spacer from the end of the shaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00r01580.png\" alt=\"00r01580.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><p>Separate the rotational and stationary part of the seal.</p><p>Locate the stationary part of the seal on the end of the seal installation tool, Part Number 5573257.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00r01581.png\" alt=\"00r01581.png\"></figure><p>Put the spacer on the shaft.</p><p>Slide the tool on to the end of the shaft.</p><p>Tap the end of the installation tool with a mallet to push the stationary part of the seal into the gear housing.</p><p>The spacer <b>must</b> be installed, or the seal will <b>not</b> locate correctly.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00r01582.png\" alt=\"00r01582.png\"></figure><p>Place the rotational part of the seal on top of the pulley shaft.</p><p>Use seal installation tool, Part Number 5573258 to install the seal on to the pulley with the aid of a mallet.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If you are moving from an older style seal that utilizes three bolts for installation to the new seal a new design pulley <b>must</b> also be purchased.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/00r01583.png\" alt=\"00r01583.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><ul><li>Install the accessory drive pulley. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-009-004-tr\">Refer to Procedure 009-004 in Section 9.</a></li></ul>","56-001-005-tr":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Some state and federal agencies have determined that used engine oil can be carcinogenic and cause reproductive toxicity. Avoid inhalation of vapors, ingestion, and prolonged contact with used engine oil. If not reused dispose of in accordance with local environmental regulations</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Drain the lubricating oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-037 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the lubricating oil pan. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-025-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-025 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the lubricating oil pan adapter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-027-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-027 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the oil suction tube and transfer tube. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-035 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the block stiffener plate. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-089-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-089 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Remove the oil pump, if necessary. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-031 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the piston cooling nozzles. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-046-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-046 in Section 1.</a></li></ul><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Use the following procedure for more information on connecting rod types. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-014\">Refer to Procedure 001-014 in Section 1.</a></p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><p>Use the barring mechanism to rotate the engine crankshaft to position a connecting rod at bottom dead center for maximum accessibility when loosening the connecting rod capscrews.</p><p>Bar the engine to the desired position.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600125.png\" alt=\"01600125.png\"></figure><p>The connecting rods <b>must</b> have the cylinder number and bank marked on both the connecting rod and the connecting rod cap on the inboard side. Check the connecting rods for the correct markings. Use a steel stamp to mark any connecting rod that is <b>not</b> correctly marked.</p><p>Loosen the capscrews until there is 6 mm [0.25 in] of clearance between the rod cap and the capscrew head.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600066.png\" alt=\"01600066.png\"></figure><p>Use a mallet to tap the connecting rod capscrews until the connecting rod cap and rod separate.</p><p>Remove the capscrews and the cap.</p><p>Mark the cylinder number, right (R) or left (L) bank, and the letter “L” in the flat surface of the bearing tangs.</p><p>Use an awl to mark the bearing position in the tang area.</p><p>Remove the lower rod bearing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600067.png\" alt=\"01600067.png\"></figure><p>Push the connecting rod up far enough to allow the upper bearing shell to be removed. Push the rod away from the crankshaft.</p><p>Remove the bearing shell, and mark the cylinder number, right (R) or left (L) bank, and the letter “U” on the flat surface of the bearing tangs.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600068.png\" alt=\"01600068.png\"></figure><p>The bearings <b>must</b> be marked for location as they are removed for future identification. Each bearing <b>must</b> be installed in its original location if the bearing is installed again.</p><p>Use a scribe or ball point pen to mark the bearing location in the tang area.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx1bema.png\" alt=\"cx1bema.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use solvent to clean the bearings.</p><p>Dry with compressed air.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8beea.png\" alt=\"cx8beea.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the bearing face on the front and back for:</p><ul><li>Nicks</li><li>Cracks</li><li>Burrs</li><li>Scratches (deep enough to be felt with a fingernail)</li><li>Scrapes</li><li>Gouges</li><li>Embedded particles</li><li>Fretting</li><li>Pitting</li><li>Flaking</li><li>Corrosion</li><li>Lock tang damage.</li></ul><p>If any damage is found, the bearing <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx2besa.png\" alt=\"cx2besa.png\"></figure><p>Normal bearing wear produces a smooth finish which will wear into the copper lining. Exposed copper does <b>not always</b> indicate worn bearings. Reference the Parts Reuse Guidelines, Bulletin 3810303.</p><p>If large areas of copper lining are visible in the bearings before the engine has accumulated 3000 hours, inspect the engine for contamination from fine dirt particles and correct the problem.</p><p>For more detailed information of bearing damage, reference the Analysis and Prevention of Bearing Failures Manual, Bulletin 3810387</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8beba.png\" alt=\"cx8beba.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><p>Use a clean, lint-free paper towel or cloth to clean the rod bore, the cap, and the crankshaft rod journal.</p><p>Inspect the crankshaft rod journals for damage.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600069.png\" alt=\"01600069.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of engine damage, do not lubricate the back of the bearing shells.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The illustration shows the piston and connecting rod removed from the block for clarity.</p></div></div><p>Used bearings <b>must</b> be installed in the same location from which they were removed.</p><p>Install the upper bearing shell in the connecting rod with the tang of the bearing in the slot of the rod.</p><p>Lubricate the bearing shell with Lubriplate™ 105, Part Number 3163086.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600070.png\" alt=\"01600070.png\"></figure><p>Install the lower bearing shell in the rod cap. Make sure the tang of the bearing shell is in the slot of the rod cap, and the end of the bearing is even with the surface of the rod cap.</p><p>Lubricate the bearing shell with Lubriplate™ 105, Part Number 3163086.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600071.png\" alt=\"01600071.png\"></figure><p>Lubricate the connecting rod capscrew head flanges with clean gear oil Society of Automotive Engineers (SAE) W140).</p><p>Lubricate the capscrew threads with clean engine oil (SAE 15W-40).</p><p>Install the capscrews in the rod caps.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600072.png\" alt=\"01600072.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The connecting rods and connecting rod caps are not interchangeable. The rods and the caps are machined as an assembly. The cylinder number on the rod and cap must be the same. Failure will result if the parts are mixed.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The side of the connecting rod cap with the cylinder number marking (bearing tang side) must be inboard on the engine. Failure will result if the parts are not installed correctly.</p></div></div><p>Install the connecting rod cap.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600073.png\" alt=\"01600073.png\"></figure><p>Tighten the capscrews alternately and evenly to pull the cap over the dowel pins. Use the following steps and sequence to tighten the capscrews.</p><p>Use the sequence of 1, 2, 3, 4, on each connecting rod when tightening the connecting rod capscrews, as illustrated.</p><p>Use the following procedures for the connecting rod capscrew tightening specifications:</p><ul><li>Refer to Procedure 001-054 in Section 1.</li><li><a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-045-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-045 in Section 1.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600133.png\" alt=\"01600133.png\"></figure><p>Check the side clearance between the rod and the crankshaft. Move the rods as far as they will go toward the crankshaft web. Measure the side clearance with a feeler gauge.</p><p>Refer to Procedure 001-054 in Section 1.</p><p>Both rods <b>must</b> move freely from side-to-side.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx600da.png\" alt=\"cx600da.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Install the lubricating oil pump, if removed. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-031 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the lubricating oil transfer and suction tubes and brackets. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-035 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the block stiffener plate. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-089-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-089 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Install the lubricating oil pan adapter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-027-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-027 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the lubricating oil pan. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-025-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-025 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install new oil filters. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-013-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-013 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Fill the engine with clean engine oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-037 in Section 7.</a></li><li>On engines <b>not</b> using the PRELUB™ system, the engine <b>must</b> be manually prelubricated before operation. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-063-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-063 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Operate the engine until the coolant temperature reaches 70°C [158°F].</li><li>Check for coolant and oil leaks.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-001-006":"<h3>General Information</h3><p>The upper bearings contain an oil hole. The lower bearings do <b>not</b> have an oil hole. Both bearings are marked on the backside indicating location (upper or lower) and size (standard or oversize]). The amount that the bearing is oversize is indicated in U.S. customary inches.</p><p>Use the same size bearing, standard 0.254 mm [0.010 in], 0.508 mm [0.020 in], or 0.762 mm [0.030 in] that was removed.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600076.png\" alt=\"01600076.png\"></figure><p>The crankshaft will be stamped on the end of the number 1 counterweight to indicate whether it has been ground undersize. The amount of material removed from the main journals and the rod journals are both stamped at this location. Thrust bearing size is stamped on a crankshaft counterweight adjacent to the thrust location.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800ga.png\" alt=\"ck800ga.png\"></figure><p>The location numbers of the main bearing caps, beginning at the front, are number one through number 7 on QSK45 engines, and number 1 through number 9 on QSK60 engines.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400122.png\" alt=\"01400122.png\"></figure><h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Some state and federal agencies have determined that used engine oil can be carcinogenic and cause reproductive toxicity. Avoid inhalation of vapors, ingestion, and prolonged contact with used engine oil. If not reused, dispose of in accordance with local environmental regulations.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Disconnect the batteries. See equipment manufacturer service information.</li><li>Drain the lubricating oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-037 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the lubricating oil pan. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-025-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-025 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the oil pan adapter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-027-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-027 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the oil suction and supply tubes and brackets. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-035 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the oil pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-031 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the block stiffener plate. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-089-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-089 in Section 1.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Replace the main bearings one at a time. Personal injury and damage to the crankshaft can result if the crankshaft falls.</p></div></div><p>The main bearing caps <b>must</b> be marked according to their respective positions (number 1 through number 7 for QSK45 engines and number 1 through number 9 for QSK60 engines with number 1 at the front of the engine). Each cap <b>must</b> also have the block number stamped into it. Use a steel stamp to mark any cap <b>not</b> correctly marked.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb6cagb.png\" alt=\"mb6cagb.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Access to some side capscrews involves the removal of other components.</p></div></div><p>Remove the two side capscrews.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600077.png\" alt=\"01600077.png\"></figure><p>Remove the main bearing cap mounting capscrews.</p><p>Remove the cap. Use the main bearing cap puller, Part Number 4919357.</p><p>Align the main bearing cap puller with the main bearing cap.</p><p>Install the fixture to the left and right oil pan rails of the engine block.</p><p>Install the main bearing cap puller clamp plate onto the main bearing cap and tighten the clamp knob.</p><p>Turn the adjusting nut at the top of the fixture with a wrench to lift the main bearing cap.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If the flywheel housing is still in place, the rear main bearing cap will need to be tilted forward slightly for tool access. Use a pry bar or a large screwdriver to tilt the cap forward.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800640.png\" alt=\"22800640.png\"></figure><p>QSK60 engines which do <b>not</b> have the machined ledge on the left bank pan rail inner wall, as shown in the illustration, and have a fully counterweighted crankshaft installed, <b>must</b> have the number 14 and 15 crankshaft counterweights removed in order to remove the number 8 main bearing cap.</p><p>Use the following procedure for the removal and installation of the crankshaft counterweights. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-016 in Section 1.</a></p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>QSK60 cylinder blocks which do <b>not</b> have the machined ledge can have this feature added. Use the following procedure Machine section for the pan rail machining instructions. Refer to Procedure 001-026 in Section 1.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600643.png\" alt=\"01600643.png\"></figure><p>QSK60 engines which do have the machined ledge to the left bank pan rail inner wall and have a fully counterweighted crankshaft installed on the number 8 main bearing cap can be removed without removing any counterweights.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>For removal of the number 8 main bearing cap, with a fully counterweighted crankshaft installed, the number 4 and 5 connecting rod journals <b>must</b> be positioned at bottom dead center (BDC).</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600644.png\" alt=\"01600644.png\"></figure><p>With the main bearing cap clear of the interference pads, extract using service tool, Part Number 4919357, to lift the main bearing cap until the left bank upper interference pad of the main bearing cap (1) passes the cylinder block machined ledge (2). Angle the cap so that the right bank lower interference pad of the main bearing cap (3) passes the upper interference pad of the cylinder block (4).</p><p>Remove the main bearing cap.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The main bearing capscrews <b>must</b> be removed during the process.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>All main bearing cap locations which have the left bank pan rail inner wall machined ledge can have the main bearing cap removed using this method.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600645.png\" alt=\"01600645.png\"></figure><p>Remove the bearing from the cap, and mark the location in the tang for future identification or analysis.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb800ma.png\" alt=\"mb800ma.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If the crankshaft is being removed, the upper main bearing shells do <b>not</b> require removal at this time.</p></div></div><p>To remove the upper main bearing shells, use the main bearing remover, Part Number 3823818.</p><p>Rotate the crankshaft so the tang (1) of the main bearing shell rolls out of the block first.</p><p>Use the barring device to slowly rotate the crankshaft. Continue rotating the crankshaft until the bearing shell is out of the engine block. If the flywheel housing has been removed, the crankshaft can be turned using the crankshaft adapter mounting capscrews.</p><p>Mark the upper main bearing location in the tang area of the bearing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600626.png\" alt=\"01600626.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If bearing replacement was initiated due to damage, check the oil pan for debris. If significant debris is present, remove and disassemble the lubricating oil pump and inspect the bushing for debris damage. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-031 in Section 7.</a></p></div></div><p>Clean the crankshaft journal with a lint-free cloth.</p><p>Inspect the journal for damage.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600324.png\" alt=\"01600324.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of damage to the crankshaft, do not use a scraper or a wire brush on the crankshaft journals.</p></div></div><p>Use a lint-free cloth to clean the crankshaft journal.</p><p>Inspect the crankshaft journal for damage.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks800sa.png\" alt=\"ks800sa.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of bearing damage, do not use a scraper or wire brush on bearing surfaces.</p></div></div><p>Clean the bearings with solvent and dry with compressed air.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb8bega.png\" alt=\"mb8bega.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the main caps, capscrews, and washers for the following damage:</p><ul><li>Pitting</li><li>Cracking</li><li>Thread damage.</li></ul><p>Replace any damaged part.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01a00023.png\" alt=\"01a00023.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the main caps, capscrews, and washers for the following damage:</p><ul><li>Galling under capscrew head or around capscrew hole in the main bearing cap.</li></ul><p>Replace any damaged part.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01k00060.png\" alt=\"01k00060.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the bearings for damage.</p><p>Replace any bearings that have the following damage:</p><ul><li>Nicks</li><li>Cracks</li><li>Burrs</li><li>Scratches (deep enough to be felt with a fingernail)</li><li>Scrapes</li><li>Gouges</li><li>Embedded particles</li><li>Fretting</li><li>Pitting</li><li>Flaking</li><li>Corrosion</li><li>Lock tang damage.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx2besa.png\" alt=\"cx2besa.png\"></figure><p>Normal bearing wear produces a smooth finish, which will wear into the copper lining. Exposed copper does <b>not always</b> indicate worn bearings. Reference the Parts Reuse Guidelines, Bulletin 3810303.</p><p>If large areas of copper lining are visible in the bearings before the engine has accumulated 3000 hours, inspect the engine for contamination from fine dirt particles and correct the problem.</p><p>For more detailed information of bearing damage, reference the Analysis and Prevention of Bearing Failures Manual, Bulletin 3810387.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8beba.png\" alt=\"cx8beba.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of damage to the bearing surfaces, use adequate professional tools and measuring techniques. Use of improper measuring tools or methods may cause local surface damages that can become the initiation point for bearing surface layer failure.</p></div></div><p>Use a ball-end micrometer to measure the bearing thickness at the wear location.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Main Bearing Thickness</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>Standard</td><td>4.317</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.1699</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>4.337</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.1707</td></tr><tr><td>Oversize 0.25 mm [0.010 in]</td><td>4.442</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.1748</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>4.462</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.1756</td></tr><tr><td>Oversize 0.50 mm [0.020 in]</td><td>4.567</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.1798</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>4.587</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.1805</td></tr><tr><td>Oversize 0.75 mm [0.030 in]</td><td>4.692</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.1847</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>4.712</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.1855</td></tr><tr><td>Oversize 1.0 mm [0.039 in]</td><td>4.817</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.1896</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>4.837</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.1904</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb8betb.png\" alt=\"mb8betb.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><p>Used bearings <b>must</b> be installed in their original location.</p><p>Install the upper main bearing shells using the same method that was used for the removal of the shells.</p><p>The bearing tang <b>must</b> fit into the slot in the bearing saddle to secure the bearing in the proper location.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600156.png\" alt=\"01600156.png\"></figure><p>Use a lint-free cloth to clean the lower main bearing cap, lower thrust bearings, and mounting surfaces.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> lubricate the backs of the main bearings.</p><p>Align the tang (1) in the bearing with the slot (2) in the main bearing cap. Install the bearing. The end of the bearing <b>must</b> be even with the main bearing cap mounting surface.</p><p>Lubricate the bearing surface with Lubriplate™ 105, Part Number 3163086.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb8behb.png\" alt=\"mb8behb.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of engine damage, the grooves in the thrust bearings must point toward the crankshaft. The dowels that secure the bearings must not protrude above the bearing.</p></div></div><p>Lubricate the capscrew head and threads with Society of Automotive Engineers (SAE) EP 140W oil. Allow the excess oil to drip off the capscrews before installing them in the block.</p><p>Install the two thrust bearings on the number 6 main bearing cap on QSK45 engines and the number 8 bearing cap on QSK60 engines. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-007-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-007 in Section 1.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00030.png\" alt=\"01s00030.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of engine damage, the numbers on the main bearing caps must be the same as the numbers on the block.</p></div></div><p>Check the number on the main bearing caps. The last digit (1 to 9) of each number indicates the correct location.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb4bdga.png\" alt=\"mb4bdga.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of engine damage, make sure the side of the cap with the bearing tang slot and the bearing locking tang are toward the same side of the block.</p></div></div><p>Place the ring dowels in the capscrew holes.</p><p>The bearing shells <b>must</b> be firmly seated in the cap and the correct capscrew in position. Install the main bearing caps.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> hit the main bearing caps with a hammer. The bearing shells can fall out or be dislodged.</p><p>Keep the cap straight while moving it past the side capscrew holes.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600080.png\" alt=\"01600080.png\"></figure><p>QSK60 engines which do <b>not</b> have the machined ledge to the left bank pan rail inner wall, as shown in the illustration, and have a fully counterweighted crankshaft installed, <b>must</b> have the number 14 and 15 crankshaft counterweights removed in order to install the number 8 main bearing cap.</p><p>Use the following procedure for removal and installation of the crankshaft counterweights. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-016 in Section 1.</a></p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>QSK60 cylinder blocks which do <b>not</b> have the machined ledge can have this feature added. Use the following procedure Machine section for machining the pan rail machining instructions. Refer to Procedure 001-026 in Section 1.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600643.png\" alt=\"01600643.png\"></figure><p>QSK60 engines which do have the machined ledge to the left bank pan rail inner wall, and have a fully counterweighted crankshaft installed, can have the number 8 main bearing cap installed without removing any counterweights.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>For removal of the number 8 main bearing cap with a fully counterweighted crankshaft installed, the number 4 and 5 connecting rod journals <b>must</b> be positioned at BDC.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600644.png\" alt=\"01600644.png\"></figure><p>Angle the main bearing cap so the left bank cap side is lower than the right bank cap side. Allow the left bank upper interference pad of the main bearing cap (1) to sit in to the machined ledge (2). Carefully lower the right bank side of the main bearing cap so the right bank lower interference pad of the main bearing cap (3) passes the upper interference pad of the cylinder block (4).</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The main bearing capscrews <b>must</b> be removed during the process.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600645.png\" alt=\"01600645.png\"></figure><p>Lower the cap into place.</p><p>Continue to install the main bearing caps as in previous steps.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600646.png\" alt=\"01600646.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not rotate the crankshaft until all of the main bearing caps are pulled to the block. Damage will result if the bearings move out of location.</p></div></div><p>Install the capscrews by hand.</p><p>Turn the two capscrews by hand at the same time until each touches the main bearing caps.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb4csha.png\" alt=\"mb4csha.png\"></figure><p>Do <b>not</b> use an impact wrench. The main bearing shells can become dislodged.</p><p>Use two wrenches to turn both capscrews on a main bearing cap at the same time to seat the cap into position.</p><p>Seat all of the main bearing caps before tightening.</p><p>Check to make sure the number 7 cap on QSK45 engines (the number 9 cap on QSK60 engines) is even with the back of the block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb4cshb.png\" alt=\"mb4cshb.png\"></figure><p>Lubricate the side capscrews with clean oil, allowing the excess to run off.</p><p>Turn the capscrews in by hand as far as possible.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600081.png\" alt=\"01600081.png\"></figure><p>QSK45 Engines</p><p>Use the following steps to tighten the capscrews in the sequence shown.</p><p>Tighten the main bearing cap containing the thrust bearings to 50 N•m [37 ft-lb] before tightening to specification.</p><p>Torque Value:</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600632.png\" alt=\"01600632.png\"></figure><p>QSK60 Engines</p><p>Tighten the capscrews in the sequence shown.</p><p>Tighten the main bearing cap containing the thrust bearings to 50 N•m [37 ft-lb] before tightening to specification.</p><p>Torque Value:</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600634.png\" alt=\"01600634.png\"></figure><p>QSK45 and QSK60</p><p>Tighten the right bank main bearing cap side capscrews first.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>305 n•m [225 ft-lb]</p></div></div><p>Tighten the left bank main bearing cap side capscrews after the right bank.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>305 n•m [225 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600128.png\" alt=\"01600128.png\"></figure><p>Turn the crankshaft with the barring mechanism.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The crankshaft will turn freely if the main bearings are installed correctly.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks400da.png\" alt=\"ks400da.png\"></figure><p>Check the crankshaft end clearance. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-007-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-007 in Section 1.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb1beja.png\" alt=\"mb1beja.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Install the block stiffener plate. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-089-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-089 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Install the oil pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-031 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the oil suction and supply tubes and brackets. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-035 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the oil pan adapter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-027-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-027 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the lubricating oil pan. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-025-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-025 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Fill the engine with lubricating oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-037 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Connect the batteries. See equipment manufacturer service information.</li><li>Start and operate the engine to 70°C [158°F] coolant temperature.</li><li>Inspect for coolant and oil leaks.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-001-007-tr":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Some state and federal agencies have determined that used engine oil can be carcinogenic and cause reproductive toxicity. Avoid inhalation of vapors, ingestion, and prolonged contact with used engine oil. If not reused, dispose of in accordance with local environmental regulations.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Disconnect the batteries. See equipment manufacturer service information.</li><li>Drain the engine oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-037 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the lubricating oil pan. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-025-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-025 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the pan adapter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-027-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-027 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the suction tube. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-035 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the transfer tube. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-040-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-040 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the oil pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-031 in Section 7.</a></li></ul><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Record the quantity and location of the shims under the oil pump feet. The same number of shims must be put back in the same location when the oil pump is installed.</p></div></div><ul><li>Remove the stiffener plate. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-089-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-089 in Section 1.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><p>The number 6 main bearing cap on QSK45 engines and the number 8 main beraring cap on QSK60 engines contain two thrust bearings, each on the front and rear of the cap.</p><p>The main bearing cap <b>must</b> be removed for the thrust bearing to be removed.</p><p>Remove the two thrust bearings from the bearing cap, and mark them for position in the notched area.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb1bemb.png\" alt=\"mb1bemb.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p><b>If necessary, slide the crankshaft to the front or to the rear to allow the thrust bearings to be removed.</b></p></div></div><p>Remove the two upper thrust bearings from the block at the appropriate location. Mark the thrust bearings for position.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/bp400ma.png\" alt=\"bp400ma.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compresed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of bearing damage, do not use a scraper or wire brush to clean bearings.</p></div></div><p>Clean the bearings with solvent and dry with compressed air.</p><p>Make sure the bearings are marked for location. The bearing <b>must</b> be installed in the original location if used again.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb8bega.png\" alt=\"mb8bega.png\"></figure><p>Use a micrometer to measure the bearing thickness at the wear location.</p><p>The areas that shine indicate the location where the crankshaft contacts the bearing.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Thrust Bearing Thickness</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>Standard</td><td>7.239</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.285</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>7.315</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.288</td></tr><tr><td>Oversize 0.254 mm [0.010 in]</td><td>7.49</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.295</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>7.57</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.298</td></tr><tr><td>Oversize 0.508 mm [0.020 in]</td><td>7.75</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.305</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>7.82</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.308</td></tr><tr><td>Oversize 0.762 mm [0.030 in]</td><td>8.00</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.315</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>8.08</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.318</td></tr><tr><td>Oversized 1.016 mm [0.040 in]</td><td>8.25</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.325</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>8.33</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.328</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb8bete.png\" alt=\"mb8bete.png\"></figure><p>Check the thrust bearing retaining pin in the main bearing cap for mechanical damage.</p><p>Check the thrust bearing retaining pins protrusion.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Dowel Pin Protrusion</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>4.0</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.157</td></tr><tr><td>5.0</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.197</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the thrust bearing retaining pins are damaged or having incorrect protrusion, they <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01e00323.png\" alt=\"01e00323.png\"></figure><h3>Repair</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If one or more pins are damaged, replace all four pins.</p></div></div><p>Use a pair of cutting dikes and grasp the damaged pin.</p><p>Place a piece of thin wood, or equivalent, between the dikes and main bearing cap, if necessary.</p><p>Pry the damaged pin out of the bearing cap.</p><p>Use compressed air to blow any dirt or material out of the pin hole.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01e00324.png\" alt=\"01e00324.png\"></figure><p>The pin insertion tool can be fabricated locally.</p><p>The tool is to be made from 4340 steel, or equivalent.</p><p>The material will need to be thoroughly hardened to 45-50 HRC.</p><p>Fabricate the pin insertion tool using the following dimensions.</p><p>The overall length of the tool is 160 mm [6.299 in].</p><ol><li>12.5 mm [0.492 in]</li><li>0.5 mm [0.020 in]</li><li>5.2 mm [ 0.205 in]</li><li>5 mm [0.197 in].</li></ol><ol><li>Chamfer should be no greater that 0.4 x 0.2 mm [0.016 x 0.008 in].</li></ol><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01e00325.png\" alt=\"01e00325.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of personal injury or equipment damage, this procedure must only be performed by suitably qualified service technicians.</p></div></div><p>Install the new thrust bearing retaining pins (two on each side) into the main bearing cap to facilitate the installing of the lower thrust bearings.</p><p>To avoid thrust bearing retaining pin damage, use the pin insertion tool and a copper hammer.</p><p>This tool will set the pins to the correct depth of protrusion.</p><p>Check the thrust bearing retaining pin protrusion after installation. Reference the Dowel Pin Protrusion information in the Inspect for Reuse section of this procedure.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01e00326.png\" alt=\"01e00326.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><p>Lubricate the grooved side of the thrust bearings with Lubriplate™ 105, Part Number 3163086.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb1bewb.png\" alt=\"mb1bewb.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The grooves in the thrust bearings must point toward the crankshaft.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p><b>Move the crankshaft to the front or rear so the second thrust bearing can be installed.</b></p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p><b>The upper and lower thrust bearing on the same side of the main bearing cap must be the same thickness.</b></p></div></div><p>Install the upper thrust bearings in the number 6 main bearing cap for the QSK45 and the number 8 main bearing cap for QSK60 engines.</p><p>Slide the lower thrust bearings over the pins into the machined lip of the main bearing caps.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb1behb.png\" alt=\"mb1behb.png\"></figure><p>Install the main bearing cap. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-006\">Refer to Procedure 001-006 in Section 1.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600080.png\" alt=\"01600080.png\"></figure><p>Use a dial indicator, Part Number 3376050, and magnetic base, Part Number 3377399, to measure the crankshaft&#x27;s end clearance.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Crankshaft End Clearance</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.13</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.005</td></tr><tr><td>0.51</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.020</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the clearance is <b>not</b> within specifications, check for foreign material behind the thrust bearings. Oversize thrust bearings are available to adjust the end clearance.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p><b>The upper and lower thrust bearing on the same side of the main bearing cap must be the same thickness.</b></p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb1beja.png\" alt=\"mb1beja.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>It is recommended to recheck the crankshaft end clearance once the engine is installed into an application.</p></div></div><p>Release the tension on the cooling fan drive belt, if installed. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-002-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-002 in Section 8.</a></p><p>Remove an accessible handhole cover. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-035 in Section 1.</a></p><p>Use the barring device to rotate the engine so that the connecting rod journal is opposite the handhole cover opening. If the connecting rods are already in this position when the handhole cover is removed, use the barring device to rotate the crankshaft slightly in the opposite direction to normal rotation. This releases the loading on the gear train.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks400dc.png\" alt=\"ks400dc.png\"></figure><p>Use a pry bar or similar to move the crankshaft backward by prying against the crankshaft web.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do <b>not</b> pry against the connecting rods or the crankshaft counterweights.</p></div></div><p>Set the dial indicator to zero.</p><p>Move the crankshaft in the opposite direction by prying on the crankshaft web.</p><p>Check the reading on the dial indicator to confirm the crankshaft has end clearance that is within the limits shown above.</p><p>If previously loosened, tension the cooling fan drive belt. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-002-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-002 in Section 8.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00036.png\" alt=\"01s00036.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this component.</p></div></div><ul><li>Install the block stiffener plate. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-089-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-089 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Install the oil transfer tube. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-040-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-040 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the oil suction tube. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-035 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the lube oil pump, if removed. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-031 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the oil pan adapter and related components. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-027-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-027 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the oil pan. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-025-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-025 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Fill the engine with clean 15W-40 oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-018-017\">Refer to Procedure 018-017 in Section V.</a></li><li>Connect the batteries. See equipment manufacturer service information.</li><li>Operate the engine to 70°C [158°F] coolant temperature and check for leaks.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-001-008":"<h2><b>Camshaft (<a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-008\">56-001-008</a>)</b></h2><p>This procedure is not yet available at the time of publication.</p><p>Last Modified: 11-Oct-2003</p>","56-001-008-shopas":"<h3>Install</h3><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The right and left camshafts are different. They must be installed in the correct bank. If they are not installed correctly, the engine will be seriously damaged.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The camshafts for the QSK45 and QSK60 are different. The installation procedure, however, is the same.</p></div></div><p>Make sure the correct camshaft is installed. Refer to the CPL for the engine being serviced. If the wrong camshaft is installed, the engine will <b>not</b> perform to specifications.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg6shga.png\" alt=\"cg6shga.png\"></figure><p>Use camshaft tool kit, Part Number 3163195. Install the camshaft installation guides <b>only</b> on the inner base circle of the valve lobes as defined and center the guides on the camshaft. Install all of the guides before removing or installing the camshaft.</p><p>Install the camshaft installation guides, Part Number 3163195, on the valve lobes of the camshaft.</p><p>Install the camshaft pilot onto the rear of the camshaft.</p><p>Use clean engine oil to lubricate the camshaft and camshaft bushings.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600015.png\" alt=\"22600015.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this component.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not damage the camshaft bushings when installing the camshaft. The bushing will fail.</p></div></div><p>Install the camshaft by turning it slightly <b>clockwise</b> and <b>counterclockwise</b> as it is pushed into the block. Keep the guides turned downward to support the camshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg6shha.png\" alt=\"cg6shha.png\"></figure><p>Align the thrust bearing, and install the two capscrews.</p><p>The narrow side of the thrust bearing plate is installed towards the outside of the engine block.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600084.png\" alt=\"01600084.png\"></figure><p>Use a dial indicator, Part Number 3376050, and magnetic base, Part Number 3377399, to measure the camshaft&#x27;s end clearance.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft End Clearance</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.15</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.006</td></tr><tr><td>0.33</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.013</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the clearance is <b>not</b> within specifications, check for foreign material or a piece of gasket between the thrust plate and the block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/if400ta.png\" alt=\"if400ta.png\"></figure>","56-001-008-shopds":"<h3>Remove</h3><p>Remove the two capscrews from the thrust bearing plate through the openings in the camshaft gear.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600084.png\" alt=\"01600084.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Pilots must be used to prevent damage to the camshaft and the bushings.</p></div></div><p>Use camshaft tool kit, Part Number 3163195. Install the c-clips <b>only</b> on the inner base circle of the valve lobes as defined and center the clips on the camshaft. Install all clips before removing or installing the camshaft.</p><p>The c-clip locations can be seen in the chart below.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft Guide Installation Chart</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>QSK 45 Camshaft Lobes</td><td>QSK60 Camshaft Lobes</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Left Bank</td><td>Right Bank</td><td>Left Bank</td><td>Right Bank</td></tr><tr><td>Exhaust - 2, 4, 5, and 6</td><td>Exhaust - 2, 3, and 5</td><td>Exhaust - 4, 6, and 8</td><td>Exhaust - 2, 4, and 7</td></tr><tr><td>Intake - 2 and 5</td><td>Intake - 2, 3, and 5</td><td>Intake - 2, 4, and 8</td><td>Intake - 2, 3, and 4</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Move the camshaft forward enough to enable installation of the camshaft support on the rear of the camshaft.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400019.png\" alt=\"22400019.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of damage to the camshaft or bushings during disassembly, turn the camshaft gently clockwise and counterclockwise slightly while pulling it out.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Rotating the camshaft too far in any direction will cause the camshaft tools to lock up the camshaft.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>One of the pilots <b>must always</b> be on the bottom part of the camshaft bushing.</p></div></div><p>Slightly rotate the camshaft back and forth during removal, if necessary.</p><p>Once the camshaft extends approximately half the length of the camshaft, use a lift strap to support the camshaft and complete the removal.</p><p>Remove the camshaft from the cylinder block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600085.png\" alt=\"01600085.png\"></figure>","56-001-008-tr":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The two cam idler gears, the two camshaft gears, and the crankshaft gear have index marks that are aligned at assembly. Improper alignment will cause extensive engine damage.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Proper support of the engine is required due to the front engine mount being removed. Do <b>not</b> work on, around, or under an improperly supported or suspended engine.</p></div></div><ul><li>Remove the gear cover and all related components. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-031 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Remove the cam follower assemblies from the necessary bank. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-004-001-tr\">Refer to Procedure 004-001 in Section 4.</a></li><li>Remove one injector per bank to allow timing to be checked. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-006-026-tr\">Refer to Procedure 006-026 in Section 6.</a></li><li>Bar the engine over to align the index marks.</li><li>Remove the left-bank camshaft compound-idler gear. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-037 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Remove the accessory drive idler gear.</li></ul><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The right bank camshaft can be removed without removing the right-bank idler gear.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><p>Remove the two capscrews from the thrust bearing plate through the openings in the camshaft gear.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600084.png\" alt=\"01600084.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Pilots must be used to prevent damage to the camshaft and the bushings.</p></div></div><p>Use camshaft tool kit, Part Number 3163195. Install the c-clips <b>only</b> on the inner base circle of the valve lobes as defined and center the clips on the camshaft. Install all clips before removing or installing the camshaft.</p><p>The c-clip locations can be seen in the chart below.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft Guide Installation Chart</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>QSK 45 Camshaft Lobes</td><td>QSK60 Camshaft Lobes</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Left Bank</td><td>Right Bank</td><td>Left Bank</td><td>Right Bank</td></tr><tr><td>Exhaust - 2, 4, 5, and 6</td><td>Exhaust - 2, 3, and 5</td><td>Exhaust - 4, 6, and 8</td><td>Exhaust - 2, 4, and 7</td></tr><tr><td>Intake - 2 and 5</td><td>Intake - 2, 3, and 5</td><td>Intake - 2, 4, and 8</td><td>Intake - 2, 3, and 4</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Move the camshaft forward enough to enable installation of the camshaft support on the rear of the camshaft.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400019.png\" alt=\"22400019.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of damage to the camshaft or bushings during disassembly, turn the camshaft gently clockwise and counterclockwise slightly while pulling it out.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Rotating the camshaft too far in any direction will cause the camshaft tools to lock up the camshaft.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>One of the pilots <b>must always</b> be on the bottom part of the camshaft bushing.</p></div></div><p>Slightly rotate the camshaft back and forth during removal, if necessary.</p><p>Once the camshaft extends approximately half the length of the camshaft, use a lift strap to support the camshaft and complete the removal.</p><p>Remove the camshaft from the cylinder block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600085.png\" alt=\"01600085.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use solvent to clean the camshaft assembly.</p><p>Dry the camshaft with compressed air.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8bdea.png\" alt=\"cg8bdea.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To prevent rust from forming, do not touch the camshaft machined surfaces after the camshaft has been cleaned.</p></div></div><p>Before handling, lubricate the camshaft with clean 15W-40 oil.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8bdba.png\" alt=\"cg8bdba.png\"></figure><p>Check the camshaft lobes and journals for cracks, scratches, or other damage. If the lobes or journals are damaged, the camshaft <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>Cummins Inc. does <b>not</b> recommend repairing camshafts by grinding the valve or injector lobes.</p><p>Marks on the lobes or journals that can <b>not</b> be felt with a fingernail are acceptable.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400057.png\" alt=\"01400057.png\"></figure><p>Using a feeler gauge, measure the camshaft&#x27;s thrust end clearance.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft Thrust End Clearance</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.15</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.006</td></tr><tr><td>0.33</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.013</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the end clearance is <b>not</b> within specifications, the gear <b>must</b> be removed. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-013-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-013 in Section 1.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400342.png\" alt=\"01400342.png\"></figure><p>Measure the diameter of the seven camshaft bushing journals.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft Bushing Journal Diameter</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>104.987</td><td>MIN</td><td>4.133</td></tr><tr><td>105.013</td><td>MAX</td><td>4.134</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the bushing journal diameter is <b>not</b> within specifications, the camshaft <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600159.png\" alt=\"01600159.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lbs]. To prevent serious personal injurty, make sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Place two vee blocks on a flat surface.</p><p>Support the camshaft on the vee blocks at the two journals indicated below.</p><ul><li>QSK45 camshafts: journals 2 and 6</li><li>QSK60 camshafts: journals 2 and 7.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01k00003.png\" alt=\"01k00003.png\"></figure><p>Position a dial indicator so the stem touches the center line of the journal. Rotate the camshaft and measure the total indicator run-out for each journal.</p><p>The dial indicator <b>must</b> be positioned at the centerline of any journal that is measured.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Max Journal Run-out</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.08</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.003</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the camshaft is <b>not</b> within specifications, it <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The max journal run-out applies to each journal.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The two supported journals do <b>not</b> need to be measured.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01e00311.png\" alt=\"01e00311.png\"></figure><h3>Magnetic Crack Inspect</h3><p>The gear and the thrust plate <b>must</b> be removed before performing this task. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-013-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-013 in Section 1.</a></p><p>Use a magnetic particle testing machine.</p><p>Using the head shot method:</p><ul><li>Adjust the machine to 2,000 amps direct current of rectified VAC.</li><li>Use the continuous method. Do <b>not</b> wet more than 1/3 of the camshaft at a time.</li><li>Check the camshaft for cracks.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8bdsc.png\" alt=\"cg8bdsc.png\"></figure><p>When the coil shot method is used, use a coil that is a minimum of 305 mm [12 in] diameter.</p><p>Ampere turn is an electrical current of one ampere flowing through the coil, multiplied by the number of turns in the coil.</p><p>Use a coil with a minimum of 3,600 amps direct current or rectified VAC and a maximum of 4000 amps direct current or rectified VAC.</p><p>Check the camshaft for cracks.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8bdsd.png\" alt=\"cg8bdsd.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><p>An open indication is visible after the wetting operation has been completed. An indication below the surface is <b>not</b> visible after the wetting operation has been completed. An indication below the surface is visible with the use of ultraviolet light.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> use the camshaft if the bearing journals have:</p><h4>Bearing Journal Limits of Acceptance</h4><ul><li>More than four open indications in an axial direction on any one bearing journals.</li><li>More than one half of the open indications extend more than one half of the distance across the bearing journals.</li><li>Open indications in a circumferential direction.</li></ul><p>The camshaft can be used if there are indications below the surface of the bearing journals.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> use the camshaft if the lobes have:</p><h4>Camshaft Lobe Limits of Acceptance - Open Indications</h4><ul><li>Open Indications in a circumferential direction.</li><li>Open Indications in the black or shaded areas (2).</li><li>Open indications that are longer than 6 mm [0.236 in].</li><li>Open indications that are closer than 5 mm [0.197 in] from the edge.</li><li>More than two indications on one of the lobes.</li></ul><h4>Camshaft Lobe Limits of Acceptance - Indications Below the Surface</h4><ul><li>More than two indications in the shaded area (2).</li><li>Below the surface indications in shaded area (2) that are longer than 16 mm [0.630 in].</li><li>More than three indications in the white area (1).</li><li>Below the surface indication in the black area (2) on the injector area.</li><li>More than two indications in the black area on the valve lobe (2).</li><li>Below the surface indications in the black area (2) of the valve lobe that are longer than 3 mm [0.118 in].</li></ul><p>Demagnetize the camshaft.</p><p>Clean the camshaft with solvent.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8bdse.png\" alt=\"cg8bdse.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The right and left camshafts are different. They must be installed in the correct bank. If they are not installed correctly, the engine will be seriously damaged.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The camshafts for the QSK45 and QSK60 are different. The installation procedure, however, is the same.</p></div></div><p>Make sure the correct camshaft is installed. Refer to the CPL for the engine being serviced. If the wrong camshaft is installed, the engine will <b>not</b> perform to specifications.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg6shga.png\" alt=\"cg6shga.png\"></figure><p>Use camshaft tool kit, Part Number 3163195. Install the camshaft installation guides <b>only</b> on the inner base circle of the valve lobes as defined and center the guides on the camshaft. Install all of the guides before removing or installing the camshaft.</p><p>Install the camshaft installation guides, Part Number 3163195, on the valve lobes of the camshaft.</p><p>Install the camshaft pilot onto the rear of the camshaft.</p><p>Use clean engine oil to lubricate the camshaft and camshaft bushings.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600015.png\" alt=\"22600015.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this component.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not damage the camshaft bushings when installing the camshaft. The bushing will fail.</p></div></div><p>Install the camshaft by turning it slightly <b>clockwise</b> and <b>counterclockwise</b> as it is pushed into the block. Keep the guides turned downward to support the camshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg6shha.png\" alt=\"cg6shha.png\"></figure><p>Align the thrust bearing, and install the two capscrews.</p><p>The narrow side of the thrust bearing plate is installed towards the outside of the engine block.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600084.png\" alt=\"01600084.png\"></figure><p>Use a dial indicator, Part Number 3376050, and magnetic base, Part Number 3377399, to measure the camshaft&#x27;s end clearance.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft End Clearance</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.15</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.006</td></tr><tr><td>0.33</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.013</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the clearance is <b>not</b> within specifications, check for foreign material or a piece of gasket between the thrust plate and the block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/if400ta.png\" alt=\"if400ta.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><p>Make sure the index marks on the camshafts are in the 12 o&#x27;clock position and crankshaft gear and the idler gears are in alignment with the timing marks.</p><p>Install the left-bank camshaft compound idler gear.</p><ul><li>Measure the gear train backlash. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-055\">Refer to Procedure 001-055 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Install the cam follower assembly on the cylinder that previously had the injector removed. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-004-001-tr\">Refer to Procedure 004-001 in Section 4.</a></li><li>Measure the injection timing. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-006-025-tr\">Refer to Procedure 006-025 in Section 6.</a></li><li>Install the remaining cam follower assemblies and related components. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-004-001-tr\">Refer to Procedure 004-001 in Section 4.</a></li><li>Install the gear cover and related components. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-031 in Section 1.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600086.png\" alt=\"01600086.png\"></figure>","56-001-010-shopas":"<h3>Install</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Prior to installing the bushing, ensure there are no burrs around the edge of the camshaft bushing bores.</p><p>If found, use an appropriate tool to remove any burrs.</p><p>Clean the bushing bores thoroughly and dry with compressed air. Refer to Procedure 001-026 in Section 1.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600624.png\" alt=\"01600624.png\"></figure><p>Align the oil holes in the bushing with the oil drilling in the block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600090.png\" alt=\"01600090.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not damage the bushing during installation. If damage occurs serious engine damage can result.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of engine damage, make sure that the front camshaft bushings are below the surface of the block.</p></div></div><p>Install the bushing until the oil holes are aligned.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600092.png\" alt=\"01600092.png\"></figure><p>Check the alignment of the bushing oil holes.</p><p>Use a 7-mm [1/4-in] Allen wrench. If the Allen wrench will <b>not</b> fit into the oil drilling, the camshaft bushing <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>There are three holes in each bushing.</p><p>All holes <b>must</b> be aligned, except on the front bushing.</p><p>There are no drillings to align with the upper holes on the front camshaft bushing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600093.png\" alt=\"01600093.png\"></figure>","56-001-010-shopds":"<h3>Remove</h3><p>Use the camshaft bushing tool hydraulic actuator kit, Part Number 3823621, and camshaft bushing installation/removal kit, Part Number 3163015, to remove the camshaft bushings.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ka3bswa.png\" alt=\"ka3bswa.png\"></figure><p>Remove the camshaft bushings.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22800450.png\" alt=\"22800450.png\"></figure>","56-001-010-tr":"<h3>Inspect</h3><p>Inspect the outside surfaces of the cylinder block and inside the cylinder block around the camshaft bores for discoloration.</p><p>Discoloration from high temperature indicates the need for a thorough inspection. Repair the camshaft bore if it is deemed necessary. Reference the machine section below.</p><p>The minimum hardness for the cylinder block is 205HB.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When a hardness test is performed, be sure to use a maximum of 5 dents per test area. An excessive number of dents will result in irreparable block damage.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600587.png\" alt=\"01600587.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Remove the camshaft from the cylinder block. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-008-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-008 in Section 1.</a></p><p>Use solvent to clean the camshaft bushing.</p><p>Check the amount of copper exposure on the camshaft bushing. If it extends more than 120 degrees around the inside diameter of the camshaft bushing, the bushing <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600588.png\" alt=\"01600588.png\"></figure><p>Measure the camshaft bushing inside diameter in four equally spaced locations.</p><p>Camshaft bushing specifications:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft Bushing Inside Diameter</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>105.114</td><td>MIN</td><td>4.138</td></tr><tr><td>105.177</td><td>MAX</td><td>4.141</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the camshaft bushing is out of specification, the camshaft bushing <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>Inspect the camshaft bushing bore while removing the camshaft bushing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600089.png\" alt=\"01600089.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><p>Use the camshaft bushing tool hydraulic actuator kit, Part Number 3823621, and the camshaft bushing installation/removal kit, Part Number 3163015, to remove the camshaft bushings.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ka3bswa.png\" alt=\"ka3bswa.png\"></figure><p>Remove the camshaft bushings.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg6bsma.png\" alt=\"cg6bsma.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use solvent to clean the camshaft bores.</p><p>Use an emery cloth to remove any burrs and sharp edges from the bore.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck6brsi.png\" alt=\"ck6brsi.png\"></figure><p>Use crack detection kit, part Number 3375432, or equivalent, to check the camshaft bores for cracks.</p><p>Bores which have excessive and multiple cracks can <b>not</b> be repaired. Reference the guidelines below.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600590.png\" alt=\"01600590.png\"></figure><p>Guidelines for unacceptable cracks:</p><ol><li>Cracks entering oil hole</li><li>Cracks in the radii of the structural webs</li><li>Cracks that break over the side of the camshaft bearing bore.</li></ol><p>If any camshaft bearing bores contain any of these cracks, the block can <b>not</b> be repaired and <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600595.png\" alt=\"01600595.png\"></figure><p>Measure the camshaft bushing bore inside diameter in four equally spaced locations.</p><p>Camshaft bushing bore specifications:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft Bushing Bore Diameter</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>111.975</td><td>MIN</td><td>4.409</td></tr><tr><td>112.025</td><td>MAX</td><td>4.410</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the camshaft bushing bore is <b>not</b> within specifications, the bore <b>must</b> be machined and a repair sleeve inserted. Reference the repair section below for information on salvaging the camshaft bushing bores.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600089.png\" alt=\"01600089.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Prior to installing the bushing, ensure there are no burrs around the edge of the camshaft bushing bores.</p><p>If found, use an appropriate tool to remove any burrs.</p><p>Clean the bushing bores thoroughly and dry with compressed air. Refer to Procedure 001-026 in Section 1.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600624.png\" alt=\"01600624.png\"></figure><p>Align the oil holes in the bushing with the oil drilling in the block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600090.png\" alt=\"01600090.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not damage the bushing during installation. If damage occurs serious engine damage can result.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of engine damage, make sure that the front camshaft bushings are below the surface of the block.</p></div></div><p>Install the bushing until the oil holes are aligned. Use the camshaft bushing tool hydraulic actuator kit, Part Number 3823621, and the camshaft bushing installation/removal kit, Part Number 3163015, to install the camshaft bushing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600092.png\" alt=\"01600092.png\"></figure><p>Check the alignment of the bushing oil holes.</p><p>Use a 7-mm [1/4-in] Allen wrench. If the Allen wrench will <b>not</b> fit into the oil drilling, the camshaft bushing <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>There are three holes in each bushing.</p><p>All holes <b>must</b> be aligned, except on the front bushing.</p><p>There are no drillings to align with the upper holes on the front camshaft bushing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600093.png\" alt=\"01600093.png\"></figure><h3>Repair</h3><p>If any of the camshaft bores need repair, the size of the bore <b>must</b> be increased so that a repair sleeve can be installed.</p><p>There are two repair sleeves available. Reference the Camshaft Bore Repair Sleeves tool in Section 11 of the Service Products Catalog, Bulletin 3377710, for the part numbers for the repair sleeves.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The difference between the repair sleeves is width. Be sure to select the correct repair sleeve for the camshaft bore being repaired.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600591.png\" alt=\"01600591.png\"></figure><p>Measure the outside diameter of the repair bushing in 4 equally spaced places.</p><p>Use this measurement to determine how much material is to be removed during the machining process.</p><p>The repair sleeve <b>must</b> have an interference fit of 0.063 to 0.139 mm [0.0025 to 0.0055 in]. If the repair sleeve does <b>not</b> have an interference fit within this range, the final assembly can <b>not</b> be performed.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks900no.png\" alt=\"ks900no.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Put the cylinder block on a vibration-resistant work surface.</p><p>The block <b>must</b> sit flat on the surface.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600534.png\" alt=\"01600534.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Position the cylinder block to permit the use of a steady rest during the machining operation.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600606.png\" alt=\"01600606.png\"></figure><p>Use a dial indicator to align the center line of the camshaft bore with the center line of the boring bar.</p><p>The most accurate alignment is achieved from the camshaft bores that are not damaged and are at the ends of the cylinder block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600592.png\" alt=\"01600592.png\"></figure><p>Use the average outside diameter measurement value of the camshaft repair sleeve to determine how much material <b>must</b> be removed from the camshaft bore.</p><p>The camshaft bore repair diameter <b>must</b> be cut correctly for the repair assembly or repair sleeve to fit correctly.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600544.png\" alt=\"01600544.png\"></figure><p>Operate the cutter at 150 to 275 rpm.</p><p>If the cutting tool tip wears quickly or breaks, reduce the speed of the cutter.</p><p>After cutting the first time, approximately 1.52 mm [0.060 in] of material can be removed from the diameter each additional time the bore is cut.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600545.png\" alt=\"01600545.png\"></figure><p>The amount of material that can be removed depends on the harness of the block, the type of boring machine, and the surface finish requirements of the bore.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600593.png\" alt=\"01600593.png\"></figure><p>The surface finish of the camshaft bore should be 2.03 µmm [80 µin] or less.</p><p>Reduce the depth of the cut and reduce the cutter speed, or feed if the surface finish is <b>not</b> 2.03 µmm [80 µin] or less.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600625.png\" alt=\"01600625.png\"></figure><p>After making the first cut, check the accuracy of the cutting tool setting by comparing the cut diameter of the repair camshaft bore with the set diameter of the cutter.</p><p>The difference, if any, is the amount that <b>must</b> be taken into consideration when making the final cut. This will allow the bore to be cut to the correct finish.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600594.png\" alt=\"01600594.png\"></figure><p>Continue to cut the block until the inside diameter of the camshaft bore is 0.13 mm [0.005 in] smaller than the required bore size.</p><p>Reference the measured camshaft bushing repair sleeve outer diameter.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600596.png\" alt=\"01600596.png\"></figure><p>Remove the remaining 0.13 mm [0.005 in] of material from the camshaft bore using reduced depth of cutting operations.</p><p>Check the cut diameter to be sure it provides the correct press fit and surface finish.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600597.png\" alt=\"01600597.png\"></figure><p>Complete the cutting operation on each camshaft bore before proceeding to the next bore(s). This lessens the potential for misalignment between adjacent camshaft bores.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600598.png\" alt=\"01600598.png\"></figure><p>After the cutting operation is complete, use an appropriate tool to remove burrs from around the edges of the camshaft bores.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600624.png\" alt=\"01600624.png\"></figure><p>After the cutting operation is complete, use a rigid or flexible hone to remove any burrs from each camshaft bore.</p><p>Remove all burrs from the oil supply hole drilling. The surface finish of the camshaft bore after honing <b>must</b> be 2.03 µmm [80 µin] or less.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600550.png\" alt=\"01600550.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the enlarged camshaft bore for any fault indication that was <b>not</b> discovered during the initial inspection before proceeding.</p><p>This is especially critical in instances where the bore was distressed by heat or impact loading.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600599.png\" alt=\"01600599.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If the repair exceeds these dimensions, the cylinder block can not be used as there are no larger repair sleeves available.</p></div></div><p>Check each camshaft bore to be sure that it is the correct size for the required press fit on the camshaft bushing repair assembly, or repair sleeve.</p><p>Measure each bore in four equally spaced directions.</p><p>Reference the beginning of the camshaft bore machine section for press fit specifications.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600600.png\" alt=\"01600600.png\"></figure><p>The block <b>must</b> be thoroughly cleaned and free of all machining debris.</p><p>Be sure to brush the oil supply holes in the cylinder block with a nonmetallic brush to remove all machining debris.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600578.png\" alt=\"01600578.png\"></figure><p>Prepare the bore for installation of the repair sleeve.</p><p>Clean the bore with spray cleaner, Part Number 3375433 or ST-1272-13.</p><p>Allow 2 minutes for the excess cleaner to evaporate.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600601.png\" alt=\"01600601.png\"></figure><p>Clean the outside diameter of the repair sleeve.</p><p>Use spray cleaner, Part Number 3375433 or ST-1272-13, to remove any oils, greases, or preservative coating.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600602.png\" alt=\"01600602.png\"></figure><p>Use liquid nitrogen to freeze the repair sleeve.</p><p>Apply a 0.8 mm [1/35 in] wide bead of Loctite™ 601 or equivalent to the leading edge of the repair sleeve.</p><p>Allow the bead to extend completely around the outside diameter of the repair assembly.</p><p>Each bead should be the full length of the repair assembly.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck200eq.png\" alt=\"ck200eq.png\"></figure><p>Turn the repair sleeve until the oil holes in the repair sleeve are correctly oriented with the oil supply drillings in the cylinder block camshaft repair bore.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600603.png\" alt=\"01600603.png\"></figure><p>Press or drive the repair sleeve into the repair bore of the cylinder block.</p><p>Use installer camshaft bore insert kit, Part Number 3823621, to install the repair sleeve.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600586.png\" alt=\"01600586.png\"></figure><p>Check the location and position of the oil supply holes.</p><p>Be sure a 7-mm [1/4-in] Allen wrench will pass through the repair assembly oil holes and into the oil supply drillings in the cylinder block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600589.png\" alt=\"01600589.png\"></figure><p>Allow the sealant to dry for 10 minutes.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/bp900vg.png\" alt=\"bp900vg.png\"></figure><p>Verify the camshaft bore in four equally spaced locations and compare with the camshaft bore specifications.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600597.png\" alt=\"01600597.png\"></figure><p>Install the camshaft bushing. Reference the Install section of this procedure.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600092.png\" alt=\"01600092.png\"></figure><p>If there is any resistance when installing the camshaft or when the camshaft is rotated, the camshaft bores are out of alignment. Engine damage will occur if a camshaft block with out-of-alignment bores is used.</p><p>Reference the following procedure to install the camshaft. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-008-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-008 in Section 1.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg6shha.png\" alt=\"cg6shha.png\"></figure>","56-001-012":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this component.</p></div></div><ul><li>Remove the gear cover and all related components. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-031 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Remove the left-bank camshaft or right-bank idler gear. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-037</a> or <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-038-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-038 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Remove the accessory idler gear.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Initial Check</h3><ul><li>Make sure the target notches are free of debris or metal burrs.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600638.png\" alt=\"01600638.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><p>Remove the two capscrews from the camshaft thrust bearing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600084.png\" alt=\"01600084.png\"></figure><p>Mechanical Gear Remover</p><p>Assemble the Mechanical Gear Remover, Part Number 3162895.</p><p>Apply anti-seize or heavy duty grease onto the threads of the remover screw (3).</p><p>Install the remover screw (3) into the remover plate assembly (2).</p><p>Lubricate the thrust washer (17) with anti-seize or heavy duty grease.</p><p>Assemble the thrust washer (17) and remover screw adapter (14) to the remover screw (3), and secure it with the socket setscrew (15).</p><p>Install plate (11) on the remover plate assembly (2) with one capscrew (8) and tighten capscrew.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400097.png\" alt=\"22400097.png\"></figure><p>Install the remover jaw (13) onto the end of the stud (7). The end of the stud <b>must</b> be flush with the bottom of the jaw.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400093.png\" alt=\"22400093.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The round blanking holes in the camshaft gear must be aligned in the 1:00 and 7:00 positions to insert the remover jaw assembly.</p></div></div><p>Tilt the remover jaw and stud assembly through a round blanking hole, and maneuver it sideways until the remover jaw is inserted.</p><p>Install the other remover jaw and stud assembly in the opposite round blanking hole.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400094.png\" alt=\"22400094.png\"></figure><p>Position the flat face of the retainer flange (12) toward the camshaft.</p><p>Slide the retainer (12) down the studs until it is positioned into the camshaft gear blanking hole and engages with the remover jaw.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400095.png\" alt=\"22400095.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make certain that the flat face of the retainer flange sits against the radius of the camshaft gear hub. This will locate the remover jaw correctly at the back of the camshaft gear.</p></div></div><p>Adjust the retainer if necessary, and uniformly hand tighten the nuts (1) onto the studs.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400096.png\" alt=\"22400096.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The remover is heavy and the gear can come loose suddenly causing the gear and gear remover assembly to fall. To reduce the possibility of personal injury and component damage, use a hoist or other lifting device when using the gear remover.</p></div></div><p>Using a lifting device, slide the remover plate (2) over the studs and position it close to the camshaft gear.</p><p>Make sure the pilot of the old remover screw adapter is properly engaged with the camshaft.</p><p>Install the washers (16) and nuts (1) onto the studs.</p><p>Uniformly hand tighten the nuts.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400100.png\" alt=\"22400100.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not attempt to alter the camshaft gear remover assembly for use with any kind of impact wrench. Do not exceed 890 N [200 lb] of force on the end of the handle. The threads on the remover can gall and seize.</p></div></div><p>Make sure anti-sieze or heavy duty grease is applied to the remover screw threads (3).</p><p>Install the holding handle (6) into the remover plate assembly (2) and secure it with one capscrew (8).</p><p>Using handles (4) and (5), and holding handle (6), turn the remover screw (3) <b>clockwise</b> to remove the camshaft gear from the camshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400101.png\" alt=\"22400101.png\"></figure><p>Hydraulic Gear Remover</p><p>These items are used with the hydraulic gear remover kit, Part Number 3164375, and one or more of the engine-specific kits.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Part Number</th><th>Description</th><th>Quantity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>3823624</td><td>Hydraulic hose</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3823622</td><td>Air/hydraulic pump</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>A minimum of 621 kPa [90 psi] of clean, dry shop air supply is required for use of this tool.</p><p>Check the fluid level in the air/hydraulic pump.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22a00139.png\" alt=\"22a00139.png\"></figure><p>As an alternative to kit, Part Number 3164378, four studs and four nuts can be purchased individually, if <b>only</b> the capability of removing the camshaft gear is required.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Part Number</th><th>Description</th><th>Quantity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>3279355</td><td>Nut, M16 x 2</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3163558</td><td>Stud, M16 x 2 (2 shown)</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600152.png\" alt=\"22600152.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Use spacer base (1) where necessary.</p></div></div><p>Place the spacer base (1), Part Number 3163766, into the center of the 30-ton hydraulic cylinder, Part Number 3163551. Secure it with two socket head capscrews.</p><p>Attach spacer (3), Part Number 3164201, to the spacer base with the socket head capscrew, Part Number 3163446.</p><p>Spacer (3) is used for other engine applications.</p><p>Check the hydraulic cylinder for leaks and any signs of damage.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22400119.png\" alt=\"22400119.png\"></figure><p>The remover plate is designed to be used on several different engine applications. The mounting holes in the remover plate, Part Number 3163553, have been marked for identification.</p><ol><li>L10, M11, ISM, and QSM11</li><li>K19, K38, and K50</li><li>QST30 and QSK19</li><li>QSK45 and QSK60</li><li>QSK23.</li></ol><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22200102.png\" alt=\"22200102.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When installing the studs, make certain that the end of the stud is flush with the back of the gear.</p></div></div><p>Install two studs into the threaded holes of the camshaft gear as illustrated.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600202.png\" alt=\"01600202.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The spacer, Part Number 3164201, and the socket head capscrew, Part Number 3163446, <b>must</b> be removed from the 30-ton hydraulic cylinder.</p></div></div><p>Place the 30-ton hydraulic cylinder over the two studs.</p><p>Install the remaining two studs into the camshaft gear.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600203.png\" alt=\"01600203.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make certain that the 30-ton hydraulic cylinder is located in the counterbore provided in the remover plate.</p></div></div><p>Install the remover plate over the four studs and against the 30-ton hydraulic cylinder. Make certain that the 30-ton hydraulic cylinder assembly is centered on the camshaft and seated in the counterbore of the remover plate.</p><p>Install and uniformly hand-tighten the four nuts onto the studs.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600204.png\" alt=\"01600204.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The gear remover is heavy and the gear can come loose suddenly, causing the gear and gear remover assembly to fall. To reduce the possibility of personal injury and component damage, use a hoist or other lifting device when using the gear remover.</p></div></div><p>Install the eyebolt into the remover plate.</p><p>Attach a lifting device to the eyebolt. Lift the camshaft gear remover kit slightly, if necessary, to align it with the camshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600117.png\" alt=\"22600117.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of personal injury, remain clear of pressurized hoses, which can rupture suddenly or break free.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Connect the air hose to the input side of the air/hydraulic pump. Connect the hydraulic hose to the output side of the pump.</p><p>Connect the other end of the hydraulic hose to the 30-ton hydraulic cylinder.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22200068.png\" alt=\"22200068.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make certain that the 30-ton hydraulic cylinder is located in the counterbore of the remover plate and the piston is centered on the camshaft when it makes contact. Failure to comply can damage the gear, camshaft, or camshaft gear remover kit.</p></div></div><p>Slowly operate the air/hydraulic pump until the gear is removed.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600120.png\" alt=\"22600120.png\"></figure><p>Remove the hydraulic camshaft gear remover kit and the camshaft gear as one unit.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of damage to the 30-ton hydraulic cylinder, release the hydraulic pressure. This will retract the piston.</p></div></div><p>Remove the hydraulic hose.</p><p>Disassemble the hydraulic camshaft gear remover from the camshaft gear.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600122.png\" alt=\"22600122.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Engines with electronically actuated injectors do <b>not</b> use offset keys.</p></div></div><p>Check and record the direction of the key offset when compared to the camshaft gear rotation (same or opposite).</p><p>Remove the key.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg4kema.png\" alt=\"cg4kema.png\"></figure><p>Mark the position of the camshaft thrust bearing before removing it.</p><p>Remove the camshaft thrust bearing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg800ha.png\" alt=\"cg800ha.png\"></figure><h3>Magnetic Crack Inspect</h3><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Use a copper braid contact that has neoprene covers to reduce the possibility of burning the teeth of the gear.</p></div></div><p>If the gear contains a keyway, position the gear so that the keyway is pointing toward one of the contacts.</p><p>Use a magnetic particle testing machine.</p><p>Use the residual method and apply head shot amperage.</p><p>Adjust the amperage to the value specified in the table.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Amperage for Gear Sizes</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gear Outside Diameter</td><td>Direct Current Amperage</td></tr><tr><td>Less than 101 mm [4 in]</td><td>1000</td></tr><tr><td>101 to 203 mm [4 to 8 in]</td><td>1500</td></tr><tr><td>Greater than 203 mm [8 in]</td><td>2000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Check the camshaft gear for cracks.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400340.png\" alt=\"01400340.png\"></figure><p>If the gear contains a keyway, position the gear so that the keyway is pointing toward the coil.</p><p>Use the residual method and apply coil shot amperage.</p><p>Adjust the amperage to the value specified in the table.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Amperage for Gear Sizes</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gear Outside Diameter</td><td>Ampere Turns</td></tr><tr><td>Less than 101 mm [4 in]</td><td>4000</td></tr><tr><td>101 to 203 mm [4 to 8 in]</td><td>6000</td></tr><tr><td>Greater than 203 mm [8 in]</td><td>8000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Ampere turn is an electrical current of one ampere flowing through the coil, multiplied by the number of turns in the coil.</p><p>Check the camshaft gear for cracks.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8gesd.png\" alt=\"cg8gesd.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The gear must be demagnetized completely and cleaned thoroughly. Any small particles will cause engine damage.</p></div></div><p>An open indication is visible after the wetting operation has been completed. An indication below the surface is <b>not</b> visible after the wetting operation has been completed. An indication below the surface is visible with the use of the ultraviolet light.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> use the gear if:</p><h4>Limits of Acceptance - Machined Surfaces</h4><ul><li>There is an open indication.</li><li>There is an indication below the surface that is in the shaded area, shown in the graphic.</li><li>There is an indication below the surface that is longer than 6 mm [0.250 in].</li></ul><h4>Limits of Acceptance - Forged Surfaces</h4><ul><li>There is a open indication that is in a circumferential direction.</li><li>There is an open indication that is longer than 9.5 mm [0.375 in].</li><li>There is an indication below the surface that is in the shaded area shown in the graphic.</li></ul><p>An indication below the surface in a radial direction is acceptable if it is in the area that is <b>not</b> shaded.</p><p>Demagnetize the gear.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8gesk.png\" alt=\"cg8gesk.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Clean the camshaft and gear with solvent and dry with compressed air.</p><p>Check the camshaft for fretting damage. The camshaft <b>must</b> be replaced if the fretting damage is more than 3 mm [0.125 in] wide.</p><p>Measure the outside diameter of the camshaft.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft Outside Diameter (Gear Location)</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>86.90</td><td>MIN</td><td>3.421</td></tr><tr><td>86.99</td><td>MAX</td><td>3.425</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the camshaft is <b>not</b> within specifications. The camshaft <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg400ta.png\" alt=\"cg400ta.png\"></figure><p>Check the keyway of the camshaft gear for burrs.</p><p>Remove any burrs with a fine emery cloth.</p><p>If the burrs can <b>not</b> be removed with a fine emery cloth or, the keyway is damaged the camshaft gear <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8gesb.png\" alt=\"cg8gesb.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the bore of the gear for frets or burrs.</p><p>If fretting is in excess of 3 mm [0.125 in] wide, the camshaft gear <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>If the fretting or burrs can <b>not</b> be removed with emery cloth, the camshaft gear <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>Measure the inside diameter of the camshaft gear.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft Gear Inside Diameter</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>86.88</td><td>MIN</td><td>3.420</td></tr><tr><td>86.90</td><td>MAX</td><td>3.421</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the camshaft gear is <b>not</b> within specifications, it <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8gesa.png\" alt=\"cg8gesa.png\"></figure><p>Measure the camshaft thrust bearing thickness.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft Thrust Bearing Thickness</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>13.95</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.549</td></tr><tr><td>14.05</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.553</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the camshaft thrust bearing is <b>not</b> within specifications, it <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600096.png\" alt=\"01600096.png\"></figure><p>with Electronically Actuated Injector</p><p>Inspect the backside of the gear for cracks, chipped, or broken bosses that the cam position sensor reads. The gear <b>must</b> be replaced if the bosses are damaged.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400619.png\" alt=\"01400619.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><p>The gear housing <b>must not</b> prevent the thrust plate from being flat against the block.</p><p>Use Lubriplate™ 105, Part Number 3163086 to lubricate the outside diameter of the camshaft at the gear location.</p><p>Install the thrust plate with the grooves in the thrust plate positioned toward the camshaft gear.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg800ha.png\" alt=\"cg800ha.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Engines with electronically actuated injectors do <b>not</b> use offset keys.</p></div></div><p>Camshaft keys are available in different sizes (amount of offset). The injection timing is controlled by:</p><ul><li>The selection of the camshaft key</li><li>The direction of the key offset when compared to the camshaft gear rotation</li><li>The amount of offset.</li></ul><p>Install the same part number key in the same orientation as the key that was removed. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-006-025-tr\">Refer to Procedure 006-025 in Section 6</a>.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck4kema.png\" alt=\"ck4kema.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not exceed the specified time or temperature. Damage to the gear and the gear teeth will result.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of damage to the camshaft gear, do not attempt to install the gear without using heat.</p></div></div><p>Use an oven and adjust the heat to 205°C [400°F]. Heat the gear for a minimum of 40 minutes and a maximum of 1 hour. The inside diameter of the gear will become larger and simplify installation.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600160.png\" alt=\"01600160.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of severe burns, wear protective gloves when installing the heated camshaft gear.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The camshaft must be held in its most forward position when the camshaft gear is being installed. Failure to hold the camshaft in this position can result in improper location of the camshaft gear on the camshaft.</p></div></div><p>Remove the gear from the oven, and install it on the camshaft.</p><p>The keyway in the gear <b>must</b> be aligned with the key in the camshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600086.png\" alt=\"01600086.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Allow the gear to cool slowly. Do not use water or oil to reduce the cooling time. This can cause the gear to crack.</p></div></div><p>The timing mark on the camshaft gear <b>must</b> be visible from the front of the gear after it is installed on the camshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600086.png\" alt=\"01600086.png\"></figure><p>If necessary, rotate the crankshaft so that the holes in the camshaft gear allow access to the capscrew holes in the thrust plate.</p><p>Install the two thrust plate mounting capscrews.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg4csha.png\" alt=\"cg4csha.png\"></figure><p>Use a dial indicator, Part Number 3376050 or equivalent, to measure the camshaft end clearance.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Camshaft End Clearance</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.15</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.006</td></tr><tr><td>0.33</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.013</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the camshaft end clearance is <b>not</b> within specification, check for foreign material between the thrust plate and the block, and proper location of the gear on the camshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/if400ta.png\" alt=\"if400ta.png\"></figure><p>If the camshaft gear was replaced, check the injection timing; machine tolerances can cause timing to be out of specifications. Refer to Procedure 006-025 in Section 6.</p><p>Install the camshaft idler gear(s). Make sure all timing marks are correctly matched.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/it400gc.png\" alt=\"it400gc.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><ul><li>Install the left-bank camshaft or right-bank idler gear. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-037</a> or <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-038-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-038 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Install the accessory idler gear.</li><li>Install the front gear cover and related components. Refer to Procedure 001-031 in Section 1.</li><li>Operate the engine and check for leaks.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-001-013-tr":"<h3>Disassemble</h3><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not use a heating torch to remove the camshaft gear. If a heating torch is used to remove the gear, the gear must be replaced. The heat of the torch will damage the heat treatment of the gear.</p></div></div><p>Use a hydraulic press to push the camshaft through the gear.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg4gema.png\" alt=\"cg4gema.png\"></figure><p>Camshaft keys are available in different sizes (amount of offset). The injection timing is controlled by:</p><ul><li>The selection of the camshaft key</li><li>The direction of the key offset when compared to the camshaft gear rotation</li><li>The amount of offset.</li></ul><p>Check and record the direction of the key offset when compared to the camshaft gear rotation (same or opposite).</p><p>Remove the key.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Engines with electronically actuated injectors do <b>not</b> use offset keys.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck4kema.png\" alt=\"ck4kema.png\"></figure><h3>Magnetic Crack Inspect</h3><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Use a copper braid contact that has neoprene covers to reduce the possibility of burning the teeth of the gear.</p></div></div><p>If the gear contains a keyway, position the gear so that the keyway is pointing toward one of the contacts.</p><p>Use a magnetic particle testing machine.</p><p>Use the residual method and apply head shot amperage.</p><p>Adjust the amperage to the value specified in the table.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Amperage for Gear Sizes</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gear Outside Diameter</td><td>Direct Current Amperage</td></tr><tr><td>Less than 101 mm [4 in]</td><td>1000</td></tr><tr><td>101 to 203 mm [4 to 8 in]</td><td>1500</td></tr><tr><td>Greater than 203 mm [8 in]</td><td>2000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Check the camshaft gear for cracks.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400340.png\" alt=\"01400340.png\"></figure><p>If the gear contains a keyway, position the gear so that the keyway is pointing toward the coil.</p><p>Use the residual method and apply coil shot amperage.</p><p>Adjust the amperage to the value specified in the table.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Amperage for Gear Sizes</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gear Outside Diameter</td><td>Ampere Turns</td></tr><tr><td>Less than 101 mm [4 in]</td><td>4000</td></tr><tr><td>101 to 203 mm [4 to 8 in]</td><td>6000</td></tr><tr><td>Greater than 203 mm [8 in]</td><td>8000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Ampere turn is an electrical current of one ampere flowing through the coil, multiplied by the number of turns in the coil.</p><p>Check the camshaft gear fro cracks.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8gesd.png\" alt=\"cg8gesd.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The gear must be demagnetized completely and cleaned thoroughly. Any small particles will cause engine damage.</p></div></div><p>An open indication is visible after the wetting operation has been completed. An indication below the surface is <b>not</b> visible after the wetting operation has been completed. An indication below the surface is visible with the use of the ultraviolet light.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> use the gear if:</p><ul><li>There is an open indication.</li><li>There is an indication below the surface that is in the shaded area, shown in the graphic.</li><li>There is an indication below the surface that is longer than 6 mm [0.250 in].</li></ul><ul><li>There is a open indication that is in a circumferential direction.</li><li>There is an open indication that is longer than 9.5 mm [0.375 in].</li><li>There is an indication below the surface that is in the shaded area shown in the graphic.</li></ul><p>An indication below the surface in a radial direction is acceptable if it is in the area that is <b>not</b> shaded.</p><p>Demagnetize the gear.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8gesk.png\" alt=\"cg8gesk.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Clean the camshaft and gear with solvent and dry with compressed air.</p><p>Check the camshaft for fretting damage. The camshaft <b>must</b> be replaced if the fretting damage is more than 3 mm [0.125 in] wide.</p><p>Measure the outside diameter of the camshaft.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>mm</th><th></th><th>in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>86.90</td><td>MIN</td><td>3.421</td></tr><tr><td>86.99</td><td>MAX</td><td>3.425</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the camshaft is <b>not</b> within specifications. The camshaft <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg400ta.png\" alt=\"cg400ta.png\"></figure><p>Check the keyway of the camshaft gear for burrs.</p><p>Remove any burrs with a fine emery cloth.</p><p>If the burrs can <b>not</b> be removed with a fine emery cloth or the keyway is damaged the camshaft gear <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8gesb.png\" alt=\"cg8gesb.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the bore of the gear for frets or burrs.</p><p>If fretting is in excess of 3 mm [0.125 in] wide the camshaft gear <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>If the fretting or burrs can <b>not</b> be removed with emery cloth, the camshaft gear <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>Measure the inside diameter of the camshaft gear.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>mm</th><th></th><th>in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>86.88</td><td>MIN</td><td>3.420</td></tr><tr><td>86.90</td><td>MAX</td><td>3.421</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the camshaft gear is <b>not</b> within specifications. The camshaft gear <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg8gesa.png\" alt=\"cg8gesa.png\"></figure><p>Measure the camshaft thrust bearing thickness.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>mm</th><th></th><th>in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>13.95</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.549</td></tr><tr><td>14.05</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.553</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the camshaft thrust bearing is <b>not</b> within specifications, the camshaft thrust bearing <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600096.png\" alt=\"01600096.png\"></figure><p>with Electronically Actuated Injector</p><p>Inspect the backside of the gear for cracks, chipped, or broken bosses that the cam position sensor reads. The gear <b>must</b> be replaced if the bosses are damaged.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400619.png\" alt=\"01400619.png\"></figure><h3>Assemble</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Engines with electronically actuated injectors do <b>not</b> use offset keys.</p></div></div><p>The camshaft gear <b>must</b> be removed to adjust the injection timing. If the camshaft is replaced, do <b>not</b> install the camshaft gear until the injection timing has been adjusted using a slip fit gear.</p><p>The QSK Timing Key Offsets table identifies the recommended camshaft key for each timing code. Machining tolerances on the camshaft and the gear can cause the injection timing <b>not</b> to be within specifications.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QSK Timing Key Offsets</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Key Part Number</td><td>Key Offset</td><td>Change in Push Rod Travel</td></tr><tr><td>216294</td><td>0.089 mm [0.004 in]</td><td>0.040 mm [0.002 in]</td></tr><tr><td>200711</td><td>0.178 mm [0.007 in]</td><td>0.079 mm [0.003 in]</td></tr><tr><td>3626781</td><td>0.229 mm [0.009 in]</td><td>0.102 mm [0.004 in]</td></tr><tr><td>216782</td><td>0.279 mm [0.011 in]</td><td>0.125 mm [0.005 in]</td></tr><tr><td>3626782</td><td>0.305 mm [0.012 in]</td><td>0.136 mm [0.006 in]</td></tr><tr><td>200709</td><td>0.381 mm [0.015 in]</td><td>0.170 mm [0.007 in]</td></tr><tr><td>3626783</td><td>0.432 mm [0.017 in]</td><td>0.192 mm [0.008 in]</td></tr><tr><td>200704</td><td>0.500 mm [0.020 in]</td><td>0.223 mm [0.009 in]</td></tr><tr><td>3626784</td><td>0.546 mm [0.021 in]</td><td>0.243 mm [0.010 in]</td></tr><tr><td>200708</td><td>0.584 mm [0.023 in]</td><td>0.260 mm [0.011 in]</td></tr><tr><td>3000491</td><td>0.686 mm [0.027 in]</td><td>0.306 mm [0.012 in]</td></tr><tr><td>200706</td><td>0.833 mm [0.033 in]</td><td>0.371 mm [0.015 in]</td></tr><tr><td>3000492</td><td>0.914 mm [0.036 in]</td><td>0.408 mm [0.016 in]</td></tr><tr><td>200714</td><td>0.991 mm [0.039 in]</td><td>0.441 mm [0.017 in]</td></tr><tr><td>3000493</td><td>1.092 mm [0.043 in]</td><td>0.487 mm [0.019 in]</td></tr><tr><td>3000494</td><td>1.194 mm [0.047 in]</td><td>0.532 mm [0.021 in]</td></tr><tr><td>3000495</td><td>1.295 mm [0.051 in]</td><td>0.577 mm [0.023 in]</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg4kema.png\" alt=\"cg4kema.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not exceed the specified time or temperature. Damage to the gear and the gear teeth will result.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of gear damage, do not attempt to install the gear without using heat.</p></div></div><p>Use an oven with the temperature adjusted to 205°C [400°F]. Heat the gear in the oven for a <b>minimum</b> of 40 minutes but <b>not</b> more than a <b>maximum</b> of one hour. The inner diameter of the gear will become larger and will simplify the installation of the gear on the camshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600160.png\" alt=\"01600160.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of severe burns, wear protective gloves when installing the heated camshaft gear.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Allow the air to cool the gear. Do not use water or oil to reduce the cooling time. It can cause the gear to crack.</p></div></div><p>The timing marks on the camshaft gear <b>must</b> be visible from the front of the camshaft after the gear is installed. The keyway <b>must</b> be aligned with the key in the gear.</p><p>Install the thrust bearing.</p><p>Remove the gear from the oven.</p><p>Install the camshaft gear onto the camshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cg4geha.png\" alt=\"cg4geha.png\"></figure>","56-001-014":"<h3>General Information</h3><p>The QSK45 and QSK60 engines utilize two connecting rod designs. They are a straight split connecting rod (1) and an angle split connecting rod (2).</p><p>To identify a connecting rod installed in an engine, check the connecting rod capscrew. The straight split connecting rod capscrew (1) has a double hexagonal, 12 point, head (3). The angle split connecting rod capscrew (2) has a single hexagonal, 6 point, head (4).</p><p>Engines that contain the straight split connecting rod require the connecting rod, piston, and liner to be removed as a complete assembly. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-045-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-045 in Section 1.</a> Use the following procedure for removal of the angle split connecting rods. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-054-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-054 in Section 1.</a></p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Angle split connecting rods from fracturing rigs, excavators, loaders and mechanically driven haul trucks, <b>must not</b> be reused at rebuild or repaired, regardless of hours. Angle split connecting rods installed in QSK45/60 engines in electrically driven haul trucks, power generation, marine or other applications <b>must only</b> be reused at rebuild or repair if the connecting rods have less than 10,000 hours and pass the reuse guidelines. If a connecting rod does <b>not</b> meet the reuse guidelines, it <b>must not</b> be reused, regardless of hours. Straight split connecting rods from any application can be reused regardless of the hours, provided they pass the reuse guidelines.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Angle split and straight split connecting rods can <b>not</b> be mixed within an engine. All connecting rods <b>must</b> be the same design. Straight split connecting rods can <b>not</b> be installed into engines built prior to Engine Serial Number (ESN) 33172060, unless they have had a cylinder block upgrade.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600436.png\" alt=\"01600436.png\"></figure><h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><ul><li>Remove the piston from the connecting rod. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-054-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-054 in Section 1.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The number on the connecting rod must be the same as the number on the cap. NEVER assemble a new cap to an old rod or an old cap to a new rod.</p></div></div><p>Remove the capscrews and the cap from the connecting rod.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx400ga.png\" alt=\"cx400ga.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using a steam cleaner, wear safety glasses or a face shield, as well as protective clothing. Hot steam can cause serious personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use solvent or steam to clean the parts.</p><p>Dry with compressed air.</p><p>Use a soft bristle brush to clean the oil drilling.</p><p>Dry the rod with compressed air.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8bdea.png\" alt=\"cx8bdea.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the rod and the cap for fretting damage.</p><p>The rod and cap <b>must</b> be replaced, as an assembly, if fretting damage is visible on either piece.</p><p>Inspect for cracks and serration around the oil drilling.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The straight split connecting rod does <b>not</b> have a serrated joint, as seen on the angle split connecting rod.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600246.png\" alt=\"01600246.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the rods and caps for damage.</p><p>Replace the rod and cap, if either the I beam or cap is nicked or otherwise damaged.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx1bdsb.png\" alt=\"cx1bdsb.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the rod pin bore bushing for damage or misalignment of the oil hole passage and bushing.</p><p>If the bushing is damaged, the rod <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx1bssb.png\" alt=\"cx1bssb.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the bearing surface for nicks or burrs. If it is <b>not</b> possible to remove any nicks or burrs with a fine crocus cloth, the rod <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8behf.png\" alt=\"cx8behf.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Prevent damage to the capscrews. Nicks in the body of the capscrew can cause an area of stress that can fail during engine operation. Damage to the threads will cause torque values to be incorrect and will damage the mating parts.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/bp8csba.png\" alt=\"bp8csba.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Repair of rolled threads by the use of a thread die is <b>not</b> recommended. The thread die can create a sharp corner on the minor diameter (root) of the threads. This sharp corner can cause an area of increased stress.</p></div></div><p>Inspect the capscrew.</p><p>The capscrew <b>must</b> be replaced if:</p><ul><li>The threads are damaged</li><li>Rust or corrosion has caused pitting in the body</li><li>The body is nicked, galled, bent, or stretched.</li></ul><p>Perform a magnetic crack inspection of the connecting rod capscrews. Connecting rod capscrews <b>must</b> be magnetically inspected for cracks. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-017-001-tr\">Refer to Procedure 017-001 in Section 17.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/bp8cssa.png\" alt=\"bp8cssa.png\"></figure><h3>Measure</h3><p>Measurement of the connecting rod bores requires measuring equipment with a high level of precision and <b>must only</b> be taken after the connecting rods temperatures have stabilized for 24 hours at a stable temperature between 21 to 24°C [70 to 75°F].</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600635.png\" alt=\"01600635.png\"></figure><p>Measure the connecting rod bushing inside diameter.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Connecting Rod Bushing Inside Diameter - New</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>65.035</td><td>MIN</td><td>2.5604</td></tr><tr><td>65.047</td><td>MAX</td><td>2.5609</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Connecting Rod Bushing Inside Diameter - Used</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>65.025</td><td>MIN</td><td>2.5600</td></tr><tr><td>65.060</td><td>MAX</td><td>2.5614</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The connecting rod bushing deforms during operation and may become out of round, resulting in the difference in new and used dimensions.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The bushing is <b>not</b> replaceable. If the bushing is <b>not</b> within specification, the connecting rod <b>must</b> be replaced.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8bdnb.png\" alt=\"cx8bdnb.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Use a vise with brass jaws to hold the connecting rod. Notches, scratches, or dents in the I-beam area can lead to engine failure.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The number on the connecting rod must be the same number as the number on the rod cap. NEVER assemble a new cap to an old rod or an old cap to a new rod.</p></div></div><p>Lubricate the capscrew head flange with clean gear oil (SAE W140).</p><p>Lubricate the capscrew threads with clean engine oil (SAE 15W40).</p><p>Assemble the connecting rod, cap, and capscrews.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx5csua.png\" alt=\"cx5csua.png\"></figure><p>Tighten the capscrews alternately and evenly to pull the cap over the dowel pins. Use the following steps and sequence to tighten the capscrews.</p><p>Angle Split Connecting Rod Torque Sequence:</p><p>Torque Value:</p><p>Straight Split Connecting Rod Torque Sequence:</p><p>Torque Value:</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600133.png\" alt=\"01600133.png\"></figure><p>Use a dial bore indicator. Measure the inside diameter using the measuring positions shown.</p><p>Connecting Rod Bearing Bore Inside Diameter</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Angle Split Connecting Rods</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>127.032</td><td>MIN</td><td>5.0013</td></tr><tr><td>127.083</td><td>MAX</td><td>5.0032</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Straight Split Connecting Rods</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>127.032</td><td>MIN</td><td>5.0013</td></tr><tr><td>127.072</td><td>MAX</td><td>5.0028</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If the measurements are <b>not</b> within specification, the connecting rod <b>must</b> be replaced.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx4brtb.png\" alt=\"cx4brtb.png\"></figure><h3>Bend and Twist Inspect</h3><p>Required tools:</p><ul><li>Part Number ST-561 Connecting Rod Checking Fixture</li><li>Part Number 3163700 Connecting Rod Location Mandrel (for crank pin end of rod)</li><li>Part Number 3163701 Connecting Rod Locating Mandrel (for piston rod end with bushing installed)</li></ul><p>Bulletin 3377541, Service Tool Instructions - Connecting Rod Checking, is also available.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8togd.png\" alt=\"cx8togd.png\"></figure><p>Calibration Procedure</p><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The rod must be installed and torqued to specification or the measurement will be incorrect.</p></div></div><p>A connecting rod of known length, bend, and twist, called a master rod, is required to calibrate the fixture. A new connecting rod with a known distance from the center of the crank pin to the center of the piston pin end (rod length), can also be used.</p><p>Install the appropriate mandrel in the piston pin end of the master connecting rod.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Be sure that the locating pin in the mandrel for the crank pin end is touching the connecting rod cap directly opposite the beam of the connecting rod.</p></div></div><p>Install the mandrel in the crank pin bore of the master rod.</p><p>Tighten the mandrel so that it is centered in the bore correctly.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8toha.png\" alt=\"cx8toha.png\"></figure><p>Install the master connecting rod in the cranking fixture.</p><p>Loosen the knob and move the indicator bracket until both indicators touch the top of the piston pin end mandrel. Move the bracket toward the mandrel until the indicator needles have moved approximately 0.25 mm (0.010 in]. Turn the knob to tighten the bracket.</p><p>Adjust the indicator needles to &quot;0&quot;. Move the master connecting rod in and out to confirm the &quot;0&quot; setting.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8tova.png\" alt=\"cx8tova.png\"></figure><p>Remove the master connecting rod from the fixture.</p><p>Rotate the connecting rod 180 degrees horizontally and install it in the checking fixture.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx800ke.png\" alt=\"cx800ke.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not adjust the indicators during this step of the procedure, or the measurement will be incorrect.</p></div></div><p>Be sure the indicators are at the &quot;0&quot; setting.</p><p>If the indicator needles do <b>not</b> return to the &quot;0&quot;, adjust the indicator so that the &quot;0&quot; moves ½ of the indicated difference from the needle to the &quot;0&quot; established during the previous step.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If the needle is more than 0.10 mm [0.004 in] from the &quot;0&quot; established during the previous step, check for dirt or burrs on the mandrels and fixture. If the &quot;0&quot; is still <b>not</b> within specification, check to be sure that the master connecting rod is <b>not</b> damaged.</p></div></div><p>After completing the calibration of the fixture, remove the mandrels from the master rod.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx800kf.png\" alt=\"cx800kf.png\"></figure><p>Repeat the same steps to install the mandrels in the connecting rod to be measured, as you did for the master rod.</p><p>Install the rod in the fixture.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8tohb.png\" alt=\"cx8tohb.png\"></figure><p>Record the indicator reading. The difference of the calibrated &quot;0&quot; of the indicator <b>must</b> be added or subtracted from the known length of the master rod to determine the length of the connecting rod being measured.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Connecting Rod Length</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>320.937</td><td>MIN</td><td>12.635</td></tr><tr><td>320.987</td><td>MAX</td><td>12.637</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the connecting rod length is <b>not</b> within specification, the connecting rod <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx800nc.png\" alt=\"cx800nc.png\"></figure><p>Make a note of the indicator readings.</p><p>Remove the rod from the fixture. Turn the rod 180 degrees horizontally.</p><p>Compare the indicator readings with those noted in the previous step. The difference between the indicator readings is the amount of bend in the connecting rod.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx800nd.png\" alt=\"cx800nd.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Never attempt to staighten a connecting rod with the use of heat or force. The connecting rod will eventually break and cause extensive engine damage.</p></div></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Maximum Connecting Rod Bend (Bushing Installed)</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.10</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.004</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the connecting rod bend is <b>not</b> within specification, the connecting rod <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/nobox.png\" alt=\"nobox.png\"></figure><p>Check the fixture and mandrel in the piston pin end for a gap between the two. If there is any twist in the connecting rod, the mandrel will <b>only</b> touch one side of the fixture.</p><p>Hold the end of the mandrel that is touching the fixture firmly against the fixture.</p><p>Use a feeler gauge to measure the gap between the mandrel and the fixture. The amount of gap between the mandrel and the fixture is the amount of connecting rod twist.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx800nd.png\" alt=\"cx800nd.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Never attempt to straighten a connecting rod with the use of heat or force. The connecting rod will eventually break and cause extensive engine damage.</p></div></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Maximum Connecting Rod Twist (Bushing Installed)</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.25</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.010</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the connecting rod twist is <b>not</b> within specification, the connecting rod <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/nobox.png\" alt=\"nobox.png\"></figure><h3>Magnetic Crack Inspect</h3><p>Use a magnetic particle testing machine.</p><p>The connecting rod and cap <b>must</b> be assembled during this check.</p><p>Use the residual method. Apply head shot amperage. Adjust the amperage to 1500 ampere D.C. or rectified A.C.</p><p>Check for cracks.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8bdsc.png\" alt=\"cx8bdsc.png\"></figure><p>Use the residual method. Apply coil shot amperage. Check for cracks.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Amperage (Ampere Turns)</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>MIN</td><td>2600 D.C. or Rectified A.C.</td></tr><tr><td>MAX</td><td>2800 D.C. or Rectified A.C.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Ampere turn is an electrical current of one ampere flowing through the coil, multiplied by the number of turns in the coil.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8bdsd.png\" alt=\"cx8bdsd.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The rod must be demagnetized completely and cleaned thoroughly. Any small metal particles will cause engine damage.</p></div></div><p>The connecting rod <b>must</b> be replaced if any indications are visible in the critical (shaded) areas.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx8bdse.png\" alt=\"cx8bdse.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using a steam cleaner, wear safety glasses or a face shield, as well as protective clothing. Hot steam can cause serious personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Demagnetize the connecting rod.</p><p>Use solvent or steam to clean the part.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cx800kd.png\" alt=\"cx800kd.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><ul><li>Install the piston onto the connecting rod. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-054-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-054 in Section 1.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-001-016-shopas":"<h3>Install</h3><p>The upper bearings contain an oil hole. The lower bearings do <b>not</b> have an oil hole.</p><p>Both bearings are marked on the back side indicating location (UPPER or LOWER) and the size (STANDARD [STD] or OVERSIZE [OS]). If the bearing is oversize, the amount of oversize is indicated in U.S. customary inches.</p><p>If the crankshaft was <b>not</b> ground, use the same size bearing that was removed [STD, 0.010, 0.020, or 0.030].</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400146.png\" alt=\"01400146.png\"></figure><p>The crankshaft will be stamped on the end of the number 1 counterweight to indicate if it has been ground under size. Thrust bearing size is stamped on a crankshaft counterweight adjacent to the thrust location.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800ga.png\" alt=\"ck800ga.png\"></figure><p>The location of the main bearing caps, beginning from the front of the engine block, are number 1 through number 7 for the QSK45, and number 1 through number 9 for the QSK60.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400122.png\" alt=\"01400122.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Prevent dirt from mixing with the lubricant. Dirty lubricant can cause low hour failures.</p></div></div><p>Use a lint-free cloth to clean the main bearings and main bearing mounting surfaces.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> lubricate the backs of the main bearings.</p><p>Align the tang in the main bearing with the slot in the engine block. Install the bearings. The end of the bearing <b>must</b> be even with the mounting surface for the main bearing cap.</p><p>Lubricate the bearings with Lubriplate™ 105, or equivalent.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb6beha.png\" alt=\"mb6beha.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Use a lint-free cloth to clean the crankshaft bearing journals.</p><p>Install the crankshaft with the gear at the front of the engine block.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The QSK45 tungsten counterweighted crankshaft <b>must only</b> be installed in engines intended for use in certain applications. Make sure the intended engine application is appropriate for use with this crankshaft.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600647.png\" alt=\"01600647.png\"></figure>","56-001-016-shopds":"<h3>Remove</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Use a nylon sling and a hoist to remove the crankshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600647.png\" alt=\"01600647.png\"></figure><p>Remove and mark the upper main bearings. Mark the location of the bearing on the tang.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb6beha.png\" alt=\"mb6beha.png\"></figure>","56-001-016-tr":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Acid is extremely dangerous and can damage the machinery and can also cause serious burns. Always provide a tank of strong soda water as a neutralizing agent when servicing the batteries. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of serious personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Disconnect the batteries. See equipment manufacturer service information.</li><li>Drain the lubricating engine oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-037 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the full flow filters. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-013-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-013 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the engine and place on an engine stand. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-000-001\">Refer to Procedure 000-001 in Section 0.</a></li><li>Remove the lubricating oil pan. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-025-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-025 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the oil pan adapter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-027-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-027 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the lubricating oil suction tube. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-035 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Remove the flexplate, if installed. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-016-004-tr\">Refer to Procedure 016-004 in Section 16.</a></li><li>Remove the flywheel, if installed. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-016-005-tr\">Refer to Procedure 016-005 in Section 16.</a></li><li>Remove the flywheel housing. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-016-006-tr\">Refer to Procedure 016-006 in Section 16.</a></li><li>Remove the front gear cover. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-031 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Remove the piston and connecting rod assembly. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-054-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-054 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Remove the main bearings caps. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-006\">Refer to Procedure 001-006 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Remove the thrust bearings. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-007-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-007 in Section 1.</a></li></ul><h3>Remove</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Use a nylon sling and a hoist to remove the crankshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600647.png\" alt=\"01600647.png\"></figure><p>Remove and mark the upper main bearings. Mark the location of the bearing on the tang.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb6beha.png\" alt=\"mb6beha.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Clean the crankshaft with solvent and dry with compressed air.</p><p>Inspect the crankshaft for nicks or scratches. If a mark can <b>not</b> be felt with the fingernail, there is no value in polishing the crankshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bdec.png\" alt=\"ks8bdec.png\"></figure><p>Use a Scotch-Brite™ 7448 abrasive pad, Part Number 3823258, or equivalent, to remove discoloration or light scratches from the machined surfaces.</p><p>The crankshaft <b>must</b> be cleaned again if this polishing is performed.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bded.png\" alt=\"ks8bded.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not use a thread chaser to clean the capscrew threads in the crankshaft. Severe engine damage can result.</p></div></div><p>Both the QSK45 and the QSK60 engines have rolled capscrew threads in the nose of the crankshaft.</p><p>Use solvent to clean the rolled capscrew threads and dry with compressed air.</p><p>Place tape over the threaded capscrew holes.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600278.png\" alt=\"01600278.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use a bristle brush and solvent to clean all the crankshaft oil drillings.</p><p>Use a light preservative oil to lubricate the crankshaft to prevent the formation of rust.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks6sheb.png\" alt=\"ks6sheb.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>New crankshafts are coated with a heavy preservative. Use solvent to thoroughly remove the coating. Brush or flush the packing debris from the oil drillings before installing the crankshaft into the engine.</p></div></div><p>Use a honing stone to polish the outside diameter of the front and rear oil seal locations, the flywheel mounting location, and the vibration damper location. Remove all small scratches and grooves.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks6shea.png\" alt=\"ks6shea.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The QSK45 and QSK60 engines use rolled threads in the crankshaft nose. Do not use a thread cutting tap to chase or clean the threads. Damage or failure will result.</p></div></div><p>Thread salvage inserts are <b>not</b> permitted in the crankshaft nose.</p><p>Check the threads in the capscrew holes for damage at both ends of the crankshaft.</p><p>Check the roll pins for damage. Replace the pins if they are damaged.</p><p>The roll pins <b>must</b> be installed.</p><p>The roll pins align the vibration damper and the flywheel with the crankshaft.</p><p>The vibration damper and the flywheel contain the index marks required for proper adjustment of the valves and injectors.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks600va.png\" alt=\"ks600va.png\"></figure><p>Check the main bearing journals and the rod bearing journals for damage or excessive wear. Minor scratches are acceptable.</p><p>If a fingernail is caught in the scratch, the crankshaft <b>must</b> be replaced or machined. Reference the Alternative Repair Manual, Bulletin 3379035.</p><p>Measure the connecting rod and main bearing crankshaft journal outside diameter.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Crankshaft Main Bearing Journal Outside Diameter</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>Standard</td><td>184.10</td><td>MIN</td><td>7.248</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>184.15</td><td>MAX</td><td>7.250</td></tr><tr><td>Undersize 0.25 mm [0.010 in]</td><td>183.85</td><td>MIN</td><td>7.238</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>183.90</td><td>MAX</td><td>7.240</td></tr><tr><td>Undersize 0.50 mm [0.020 in]</td><td>183.60</td><td>MIN</td><td>7.228</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>183.65</td><td>MAX</td><td>7.230</td></tr><tr><td>Undersize 0.75 mm [0.030 in]</td><td>183.35</td><td>MIN</td><td>7.218</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>183.40</td><td>MAX</td><td>7.220</td></tr><tr><td>Undersize 1.016 mm [0.040 in]</td><td>183.10</td><td>MIN</td><td>7.208</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>183.15</td><td>MAX</td><td>7.210</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Crankshaft Connecting Rod Journal Outside Diameter</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>Standard</td><td>120.57</td><td>MIN</td><td>4.747</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>120.65</td><td>MAX</td><td>4.750</td></tr><tr><td>Undersize 0.25 mm [0.010 in]</td><td>120.32</td><td>MIN</td><td>4.737</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>120.40</td><td>MAX</td><td>4.740</td></tr><tr><td>Undersize 0.50 mm [0.020 in]</td><td>120.07</td><td>MIN</td><td>4.727</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>120.15</td><td>MAX</td><td>4.730</td></tr><tr><td>Undersize 0.75 mm [0.030 in]</td><td>119.82</td><td>MIN</td><td>4.717</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>119.90</td><td>MAX</td><td>4.720</td></tr><tr><td>Undersize 1.016 mm [0.040 in]</td><td>119.57</td><td>MIN</td><td>4.707</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>119.65</td><td>MAX</td><td>4.710</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The crankshaft can be machined undersize if the outside diameter is <b>not</b> within specifications. <b>Always</b> grind all of the journals when one is <b>not</b> within specifications.</p><p>Oversize rod bearings and main bearings are available. Reference the Alternative Repair Manual, Bulletin 3379035, for grinding specifications and instructions.</p><p>Oversize thrust bearings are available if the thrust distance is <b>not</b> within specifications. Bearings that are 0.25 mm [0.010 in], 0.51 mm [0.020 in], 0.76 mm [0.030 in], and 1.016 mm [0.040 in] thicker than standard are available. If the crankshaft <b>must</b> be machined for an oversize thrust bearing, refer to the Alternative Repair Manual, Bulletin 3379035.</p><p>Use a light preservative oil to lubricate the crankshaft to prevent the formation of rust. If the crankshaft is <b>not</b> going to be installed immediately, use a heavy preservative oil.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks6shsa.png\" alt=\"ks6shsa.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The illustration shows the QSK60 crankshaft, which contains 16 webs. The QSK45 crankshaft contains 12 webs.</p></div></div><p>The webs of the crankshaft are numbered from the front of the crankshaft. The number is steel stamped on the web.</p><p>In the illustration, the numbers (1) through (16) indicate the location of the stamps.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600648.png\" alt=\"01600648.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If the counterweights are removed, they must be installed in the correct position on the crankshaft from which they were removed. If they are installed in the wrong position, the crankshaft will fail.</p></div></div><p>The QSK45 and QSK60 crankshafts contain counterweights that are attached with capscrews. The counterweights have the same number stamped on them as the web to which they are attached, as illustrated (1) through (16).</p><p>If the counterweight is replaced, the crankshaft <b>must</b> be balanced. Reference the Alternative Repair Manual, Bulletin 3379035.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600649.png\" alt=\"01600649.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Steel and tungsten counterweights must never be mixed on a crankshaft or engine damage can occur.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The QSK60 has both fully and partially counterweighted crankshafts. The fully counterweighted crankshaft has sixteen counterweights with one on each crankshaft web. The partially counterweighted crankshaft has eight counterweights.</p></div></div><p>QSK60 engines use steel (1) counterweights, while QSK45 engines may use steel (1) or tungsten (2) counterweights. The steel and tungsten counterweights can be identified by their difference in shape. The steel counterweight has extensions (3) while the tungsten (2) counterweight has a flat base (4).</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600664.png\" alt=\"01600664.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make sure the tungsten counterweight is installed using the 12.9 capscrew and the appropriate torque value. If the incorrect capscrew or torque value is used, engine damage can occur.</p></div></div><p>Due to the difference in weight between the two counterweight materials, different counterweight capscrews and capscrew torque values are used. The correct counterweight capscrew can be identified by the steel properties marking on the top of the capscrew head. The steel counterweight capscrew is marked with the number 10.9 (1) while the tungsten counterweight capscrew is marked 12.9 (2).</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600665.png\" alt=\"01600665.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Note any loose capscrews. The capscrews must be tight or the counterweight can fall, causing severe damage to the engine. Any loose capscrews must be replaced with new capscrews.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Capscrews can not be used again and must be replaced with new capscrews.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Check new capscrews for any visible damage or wear. Discard the capscrew if there is any visible damage or wear to the thread, neck, or capscrew head.</p></div></div><p>Each counterweight contains two capscrews.</p><p>Use a torque wrench to check the torque of the counterweight capscrews.</p><p>Check which capscrew is installed. Use a torque wrench to check the torque of the counterweight capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>10.9 Capscrews 240 n•m [177 ft-lb]</p></div></div><p>Torque Value:</p><p>12.9 Capscrews</p><p>Mark any counterweights that have a loose capscrew.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600650.png\" alt=\"01600650.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The following steps apply <b>only</b> to the counterweights that contain a loose capscrew.</p></div></div><p>Remove the capscrews and discard.</p><p>Remove the counterweight.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600655.png\" alt=\"01600655.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Fully counterweighted crankshafts can not be repaired at the number 14 and 15 counterweight locations. If fretting occurs in these locations, the crankshaft must be replaced. Repair of crankshafts at these locations may result in engine damage.</p></div></div><p>Check the counterweight and crankshaft for fretting or damage between the mating surfaces. If the counterweight is damaged, the counterweight <b>must</b> be replaced and the crankshaft <b>must</b> be balanced. If the crankshaft is damaged, the crankshaft <b>must</b> be replaced or the counterweight replaced and the crankshaft repaired.</p><p><b>Not</b> more than 0.51 mm [0.020 in] can be removed from the crankshaft mounting pad to repair fretting.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600656.png\" alt=\"01600656.png\"></figure><p>Before installing the counterweight to the crankshaft, make sure there is sufficient clearance between the crankshaft, counterweight, and dowel.</p><p>Measure the depth of the dowel bore in both the counterweight (A) and the crankshaft (C). Measure the height of the dowel (B).</p><p>The total depth of both the dowel bore in the counterweight (A) and the crankshaft (C), (A+C), <b>must</b> be greater than the height of the dowel (B). If the dowel height (B) is greater than this total depth (A+C) the counterweight will <b>not</b> sit correctly on the crankshaft and engine damage will occur.</p><p>If the dowel height (B) is greater than this total depth (A+C) a maximum of 0.51mm [0.020 in] of material can be removed from one end of the dowel. Remove any burrs created as a result of material removal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600657.png\" alt=\"01600657.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If the counterweight is removed, it must be installed with the chamfered edge (1) facing away from the main bearing journal (2). If the counterweight is not installed correctly, the weight can strike the connecting rod, causing extensive damage to the engine.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make sure the correct capscrew and torque value is used for the type counterweight installed.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Make sure the counterweight is returned to its original location. The counterweights have the same number stamped on them as the web to which they are attached.</p></div></div><p>Lubricate the capscrew head and threads with clean oil.</p><p>Install the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>10.9 Capscrews 240 n•m [177 ft-lb]</p></div></div><p>Torque Value:</p><p>12.9 Capscrews</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600658.png\" alt=\"01600658.png\"></figure><p>With the capscrews tightened, inspect the counterweight for an interference condition with the crank. There <b>must not</b> be an interference between the crankshaft and counterweight to the sides of the mounting pad.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600663.png\" alt=\"01600663.png\"></figure><p>Check the overhang of the counterweight to the main and connecting rod bearing journal side walls. The overhang <b>must not</b> exceed the maximum limits called out in the following table.</p><p>If the overhang exceeds either of these maximum limits, the counterweight <b>must</b> be replaced. If the overhang exceeds either of these maximum limits with a new counterweight, the crankshaft <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If a new counterweight is fitted, the crankshaft <b>must</b> be rebalanced.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600659.png\" alt=\"01600659.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Engine</th><th>Dimension</th><th>Counterweight/Web Location</th><th>Overhang</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td>inch</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>QSK45</td><td>A</td><td>All locations</td><td>4</td><td>0.157</td></tr><tr><td>QSK45</td><td>B</td><td>All locations</td><td>15</td><td>0.591</td></tr><tr><td>QSK60</td><td>A</td><td>1-13 and 16</td><td>4</td><td>0.157</td></tr><tr><td>QSK60</td><td>A</td><td>14 and 15</td><td>3</td><td>0.118</td></tr><tr><td>QSK60</td><td>B</td><td>All locations</td><td>15</td><td>0.591</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Magnetic Crack Inspect</h3><p>Use a magnetic particle testing machine for the test.</p><p>Perform the head shot and inspection procedure, then perform the coil shot and inspection procedure.</p><p>Adjust the testing machine to 1800 amperes direct current or rectified alternating current.</p><p>Use the continuous method. Wet <b>only</b> ⅓ of the crankshaft at a time.</p><p>Check the crankshaft for cracks.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bdsa.png\" alt=\"ks8bdsa.png\"></figure><p>Use the coil shot method. Use a coil that is a minimum of 514.0 mm [20.250 in] diameter.</p><p>Use the continuous method. Apply a coil shot.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Amperage (Ampere Turns)</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Minimum</td><td>Maximum</td></tr><tr><td>4500 direct current or rectified alternating current</td><td>5000 direct current or rectified alternating current</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Ampere turn is an electrical current of one ampere flowing through the coil, multiplied by the number of turns in the coil.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bdsb.png\" alt=\"ks8bdsb.png\"></figure><p>An open indication is visible after the wetting operation has been completed. An indication below the surface is <b>not</b> visible after the wetting operation has been completed. An indication below the surface can be seen with the use of the ultraviolet light.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> use the crankshaft if:</p><h4>Limits of Acceptance - Open Indications</h4><ul><li>There is an indication in the fillet or in the shaded area.</li><li>There is an indication that passes through the 45 degree diagonal from the oil hole or goes into the oil hole chamfer.</li><li>There is an indication that is longer than 3.0 mm [0.12 in] and must <b>not</b> enter the oil hole.</li><li>Total cumulative length of open longitudinal indications on any one big end or main journal does <b>not</b> exceed 15.0 mm [0.601 in].</li><li>Circumferential indications of any kind are <b>not</b> acceptable.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bdna.png\" alt=\"ks8bdna.png\"></figure><p>Do <b>not</b> use the crankshaft if:</p><h4>Limits of Acceptance - Indications Below the Surface</h4><ul><li>There is an indication in the fillet or in the shaded area that is in a circumferential direction.</li><li>There is an indication in a longitudinal direction that is longer than 3.0 mm [0.12 in].</li><li>There is an indication that is closer than 1.5 mm [0.063 in] to an oil hole chamfer.</li><li>There is an indication that passes through the 45 degree diagonal from the oil hole.</li><li>Circumferential indications of any kind are <b>not</b> acceptable.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bdnb.png\" alt=\"ks8bdnb.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using a steam cleaner, wear safety glasses or a face shield, as well as protective clothing. Hot steam can cause serious personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The crankshaft must be demagnetized completely and cleaned thoroughly. Small metal particles will cause engine damage.</p></div></div><p>Use steam to clean the crankshaft and oil drillings.</p><p>Use a light preservative oil to lubricate the crankshaft to prevent the formation of rust.</p><p>Use a heavy preservative oil if the crankshaft is <b>not</b> going to be installed immediately. Protect the part with a cover to prevent dirt from sticking to the oil.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks600gd.png\" alt=\"ks600gd.png\"></figure><h3>Bend and Twist Inspect</h3><p>The crankshaft straightness is determined by the amount of total indicator run out and adjacent journal runout.</p><p>Total indicator runout is measured at the middle bearing journal when the crankshaft is supported on the two end journals.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600651.png\" alt=\"01600651.png\"></figure><p>Journal runout is defined as the total indicator runout (total sweep of the needle) of the main bearing journals when the crankshaft is rotated one complete revolution (360 degrees).</p><p>Adjacent journal runout is defined as the relationship of the total indicator runout of a main bearing journal as it is rotated on a common axis to the total indicator runout of an adjacent journal.</p><p>Adjacent runout is often referred to as step runout, bearing-to-bearing runout, or journal-to-journal runout.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bdtb.png\" alt=\"ks8bdtb.png\"></figure><p>The clock position is defined as the location of the journal at the highest total indicator runout point. Compare its angular relationship with the number 1 crankshaft pin as viewed from the front of the crankshaft.</p><p>In the illustration, the crankshaft pin is at the 8 o&#x27;clock position. This is the clock position of the journal being measured.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bdtc.png\" alt=\"ks8bdtc.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Place two V-blocks on a flat surface.</p><p>Support the crankshaft on the V-blocks at the two end bearing journals.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bdtd.png\" alt=\"ks8bdtd.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The QSK45 crankshaft is shown in the illustration. The QSK60 has nine main bearing journals.</p></div></div><p>Position a dial indicator so the stem touches the center line of the main bearing journal.</p><p>The dial indicator <b>must</b> be positioned at the centerline of any journal that is measured, (1) through (7).</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bdte.png\" alt=\"ks8bdte.png\"></figure><p>Rotate the crankshaft and measure the total indicator runout at each bearing journal. Record the value and the clock position for each location.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bdtf.png\" alt=\"ks8bdtf.png\"></figure><p>All QSK45 and QSK60 crankshafts are fully fillet hardened.</p><p>A fully fillet hardened crankshaft <b>must</b> be discarded if the bow is <b>not</b> within specifications.</p><p>Position the dial indicator stem to the center main bearing journal.</p><p>Rotate the crankshaft a complete revolution.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Crankshaft Run-out</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.230</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.009</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the crankshaft is <b>not</b> within specifications, it <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bdta.png\" alt=\"ks8bdta.png\"></figure><p>For each journal, plot the total indicator runout value at its clock position on a polar chart, as illustrated on the next page.</p><p>The end journals, supported by V-blocks, <b>must</b> be plotted at the center of the chart.</p><p>The graphic illustrates the plot points.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Journal</th><th>Total Indicator Runout</th><th>Clock Position</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>(1)</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>(2)</td><td>0.002</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>(3)</td><td>0.003</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>(4)</td><td>0.004</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Draw a straight line between the plotted points. From journal number 1 to journal number 2, from journal number 2 to journal number 3, until all journals are plotted on the chart.</p><p>To determine the adjacent journal runout, measure the length of the line from each journal to its corresponding journal point.</p><p>Record the adjacent journal runout for each main bearing journal.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Adjacent Journal Run-out</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.08</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.003</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the crankshaft is <b>not</b> within specifications, it <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8bdtg.png\" alt=\"ks8bdtg.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400348.png\" alt=\"01400348.png\"></figure><p>Polar Chart</p><p>Scale 1 inch = 0.001 inch and 1 mm = 0.001 mm</p><p>The small graduations are 0.1 of an inch = 0.0001 in.</p><p>A fixed central support should <b>never</b> be used to remove crankshaft bending or sag. A fixed central support will over-constrain the crankshaft and impart errors to the measured data as the crankshaft turns.</p><p>A central support that is free to float in the direction of the measurement may be used to mitigate crankshaft sag (deflection of the component under its own weight). If a floating central support is used, the support <b>must</b> be free to move with very little resistance in the direction perpendicular to the crankshaft, even when supporting the weight of the crankshaft.</p><p>The use of a floating central support requires a correlation study to validate its impact on crankshaft measurement. This study involves measuring total indicator runout using two setups: first, with the crankshaft supported <b>only</b> on the endmost journals; and second, with the crankshaft supported on the endmost journals as well as on the central journal using the floating central support. The study <b>must</b> demonstrate that the difference in total indicator runout between the two setups does <b>not</b> exceed 15 percent of the crankshaft&#x27;s runout specification.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Engine Configuration</th><th>Support Location</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>V16*</td><td>Front</td><td>Center</td><td>Rear</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>5</td><td>9</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>*A floating central support may <b>only</b> be used if measuring in the horizontal direction, and subject to the requirements above. A fixed central support should <b>not</b> be used.</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Install</h3><p>The upper bearings contain an oil hole. The lower bearings do <b>not</b> have an oil hole.</p><p>Both bearings are marked on the back side indicating location (UPPER or LOWER) and the size (STANDARD [STD] or OVERSIZE [OS]). If the bearing is oversize, the amount of oversize is indicated in U.S. customary inches.</p><p>If the crankshaft was <b>not</b> ground, use the same size bearing that was removed [STD, 0.010, 0.020, or 0.030].</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400146.png\" alt=\"01400146.png\"></figure><p>The crankshaft will be stamped on the end of the number 1 counterweight to indicate if it has been ground under size. Thrust bearing size is stamped on a crankshaft counterweight adjacent to the thrust location.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800ga.png\" alt=\"ck800ga.png\"></figure><p>The location of the main bearing caps, beginning from the front of the engine block, are number 1 through number 7 for the QSK45, and number 1 through number 9 for the QSK60.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400122.png\" alt=\"01400122.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Prevent dirt from mixing with the lubricant. Dirty lubricant can cause low hour failures.</p></div></div><p>Use a lint-free cloth to clean the main bearings and main bearing mounting surfaces.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> lubricate the backs of the main bearings.</p><p>Align the tang in the main bearing with the slot in the engine block. Install the bearings. The end of the bearing <b>must</b> be even with the mounting surface for the main bearing cap.</p><p>Lubricate the bearings with Lubriplate™ 105, or equivalent.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/mb6beha.png\" alt=\"mb6beha.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Use a lint-free cloth to clean the crankshaft bearing journals.</p><p>Install the crankshaft with the gear at the front of the engine block.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The QSK45 tungsten counterweighted crankshaft <b>must only</b> be installed in engines intended for use in certain applications. Make sure the intended engine application is appropriate for use with this crankshaft.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600647.png\" alt=\"01600647.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Acid is extremely dangerous and can damage the machinery and can also cause serious burns. Always provide a tank of strong soda water as a neutralizing agent when servicing the batteries. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of serious personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Install the thrust bearings. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-007-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-007 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Install the main bearings caps. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-006\">Refer to Procedure 001-006 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Install the piston and connecting rod assembly. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-054-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-054 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Install the front gear cover. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-031 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Install the flywheel housing. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-016-006-tr\">Refer to Procedure 016-006 in Section 16.</a></li><li>Install the flywheel, if removed. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-016-005-tr\">Refer to Procedure 016-005 in Section 16.</a></li><li>Install the flexplate, if removed. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-016-004-tr\">Refer to Procedure 016-004 in Section 16.</a></li><li>Remove the engine from the engine stand and install in the chassis. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-000-002\">Refer to Procedure 000-002 in Section 0.</a></li><li>Install the oil pan adapter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-027-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-027 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the lubricating oil suction tube. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-035 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the lubricating oil pan. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-025-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-025 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Install the full flow filters. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-013-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-013 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Fill the engine with lubricating oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-037 in Section 7.</a></li><li>Connect the batteries. See equipment manufacturer service information.</li><li>Operate the engine and check for leaks.</li></ul><h3>Rotation Check</h3><p>To rotate the engine crankshaft, push in on the engine barring device and rotate <b>counterclockwise</b>.</p><p>Rotate the crankshaft two complete revolutions.</p><p>If the engine does <b>not</b> turn freely, the equipment can have a malfunction. See equipment manufacturer service information.</p><p>The engine can have internal problems. See the correct procedure for inspection and replacement of internal engine components.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600097.png\" alt=\"01600097.png\"></figure>","56-001-017-shopas":"<h3>Install</h3><p>Install the roll pin into the crankshaft nose. This pin will align the crankshaft adapter to the crankshaft.</p><p>Measure the crankshaft adapter roll pin protrusion.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>mm</th><th></th><th>in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>21.0</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.83</td></tr><tr><td>23.0</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.91</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Make sure the roll pin is lined up with the hole in the crankshaft adapter.</p><p>Install the crankshaft adapter.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600185.png\" alt=\"01600185.png\"></figure><p>Lubricate the crankshaft adapter capscrew threads and flange surfaces with clean engine oil.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600186.png\" alt=\"01600186.png\"></figure><p>Install the crankshaft adapter capscrews.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews in the sequence shown.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th><b>Torque Value:</b></th><th>Step 1</th><th>200 n.m [148 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th></th><th>Step 2</th><th>380 n.m [280 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th></th><th>Step 3</th><th>685 n.m [505 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600187.png\" alt=\"01600187.png\"></figure>","56-001-017-shopds":"<h3>Remove</h3><p>Remove the crankshaft adapter capscrews and the crankshaft adaptor.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600185.png\" alt=\"01600185.png\"></figure>","56-001-017-tr":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this component.</p></div></div><p>Remove the vibration damper. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-052-tr\">001-052</a>.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/06400089.png\" alt=\"06400089.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><p>Remove the crankshaft adapter capscrews and the crankshaft adaptor.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600185.png\" alt=\"01600185.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><p>Install the roll pin into the crankshaft nose. This pin will align the crankshaft adapter to the crankshaft.</p><p>Measure the crankshaft adapter roll pin protrusion.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>mm</th><th></th><th>in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>21.0</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.83</td></tr><tr><td>23.0</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.91</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Make sure the roll pin is lined up with the hole in the crankshaft adapter.</p><p>Install the crankshaft adapter.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600185.png\" alt=\"01600185.png\"></figure><p>Lubricate the crankshaft adapter capscrew threads and flange surfaces with clean engine oil.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600186.png\" alt=\"01600186.png\"></figure><p>Install the crankshaft adapter capscrews.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews in the sequence shown.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th><b>Torque Value:</b></th><th>Step 1</th><th>200 n.m [148 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th></th><th>Step 2</th><th>380 n.m [280 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th></th><th>Step 3</th><th>685 n.m [505 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600187.png\" alt=\"01600187.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this component.</p></div></div><p>Install the vibration damper. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-052-tr\">001-052</a>.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600136.png\" alt=\"01600136.png\"></figure>","56-001-019-tr":"<h3>Disassemble</h3><p>Remove the crankshaft gear with the hydraulic gear remover, Part Number 3164375.</p><p>Remove the key from the keyway in the crankshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600094.png\" alt=\"22600094.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Clean the crankshaft gear with solvent and dry with compressed air.</p><p>Use a honing stone to polish the outside diameter of the crankshaft, at the location the gear is located.</p><p>Make sure any small scratches, burrs, or small grooves are removed.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8kema.png\" alt=\"ks8kema.png\"></figure><p>Measure the outside diameter of the crankshaft.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Crankshaft Outside Diameter (Front Gear Location)</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>184.12</td><td>MIN</td><td>7.249</td></tr><tr><td>184.16</td><td>MAX</td><td>7.251</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the crankshaft is <b>not</b> within specifications. The crankshaft <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks800ta.png\" alt=\"ks800ta.png\"></figure><p>Measure the inside diameter of the front crankshaft gear.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Front Crankshaft Gear Inside Diameter</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>183.97</td><td>MIN</td><td>7.243</td></tr><tr><td>184.10</td><td>MAX</td><td>7.248</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the crankshaft gear is <b>not</b> within specifications. The crankshaft gear <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8geta.png\" alt=\"ks8geta.png\"></figure><h3>Assemble</h3><p>Install a new key into the crankshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8keha.png\" alt=\"ks8keha.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of severe burns, wear protective gloves when installing the heated crankshaft gear.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When heating the crankshaft gear, do not exceed the specified time or temperature. Damage to the crankshaft gear and to the crankshaft gear teeth will result.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not attempt to install the crankshaft gear without heat. Damage to the crankshaft gear and to the crankshaft gear teeth will result.</p></div></div><p>Heat the crankshaft gear in an oven, at a maximum temperature of 210°C [410°F], for a minimum of 1/2 hour to a maximum of 1 hour. The inside diameter of the crankshaft gear will become larger and simplify the installation of the crankshaft gear onto the crankshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600291.png\" alt=\"01600291.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of severe burns, wear protective gloves when installing the heated crankshaft gear.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Allow the air to cool the crankshaft gear. The use of water or oil to reduce the cooling time can cause the crankshaft gear to crack.</p></div></div><p>Lubricate the outside diameter of the crankshaft, at the crankshaft gear location, with Lubriplate® 105 or equivalent.</p><p>Remove the crankshaft gear from the oven.</p><p>The timing marks on the crankshaft gear <b>must</b> be visible from the front of the crankshaft after the gear is installed.</p><p>Align the key way on the crankshaft gear with the key in the crankshaft and install the crankshaft gear.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks8geha.png\" alt=\"ks8geha.png\"></figure>","56-001-022-tr":"<h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using a steam cleaner, wear safety glasses or a face shield, as well as protective clothing. Hot steam can cause serious personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriated eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use solvent or steam to clean the pulley and dry with compressed air.</p><p>Check all mounting pilots and surfaces for damage from fretting.</p><p>If it is <b>not</b> possible to remove the damage with a 240-grit abrasive cloth, the crankshaft pulley <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600279.png\" alt=\"01600279.png\"></figure><p>Poly Vee pulley groove wear can be measured by placing a gauge ball or drill bit in the pulley groove and checking the protrusion with a straight edge. If the gauge ball or drill bit is below the pulley peaks, the pulley <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>All QSK45 and QSK60 engines use the L section pulley belt type.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Poly Vee - Pulley Reuse Guidelines</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Groove peak to peak dimension</td><td>Measuring tool dimension (B)</td></tr><tr><td>4.70 mm [0.185 in]</td><td>4 mm [0.16 in] gauge ball or a number 20 drill bit</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08600097.png\" alt=\"08600097.png\"></figure>","56-001-023-shopas":"<h3>Install</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not separate the crankshaft seal from the carrier during installation. This could cause damage to the seal faces and scrolls resulting in premature failure of the seal and oil leakage.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The use of a guide pin will make seal alignment more accurate.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not remove the seal from its packaging unless you are able to start and finish the installation in one action. Leaving the seal exposed out of its packaging can result in dirt ingress into the seal and result in premature failure of the seal and oil leakage.</p></div></div><p>Apply a light coating of clean engine oil to lubricate the rear rubber diameter of the seal.</p><p>Install the crankshaft seal carrier onto the crankshaft dry. Do <b>not</b> lubricate it.</p><p>Use hand pressure to push the rear crankshaft seal onto the crankshaft as far as possible.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600101.png\" alt=\"01600101.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not use a hammer on the tool. Damage to the threads will result. The tool can bind to the crankshaft because of the narrow tolerances.</p></div></div><p>Use the Front and Rear Crankshaft Seal Installation and Removal Tool Kit, Part Number 3163349, to install the front crankshaft seal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600102.png\" alt=\"01600102.png\"></figure><p>Install the five front crankshaft seal mounting capscrews.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews alternately and evenly.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>10 n•m [89 in-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600098.png\" alt=\"01600098.png\"></figure>","56-001-023-shopds":"<h3>Remove</h3><p>Remove the five front crankshaft seal mounting capscrews.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600098.png\" alt=\"01600098.png\"></figure><p>Remove and discard the front crankshaft seal from the front gear cover with the Front and Rear Crankshaft Seal Installation and Removal Tool Kit, Part Number 3163349.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600102.png\" alt=\"01600102.png\"></figure>","56-001-023-tr":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To reduce the possibility of serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Remove the fan and fan spacer(s). <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-040-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-040 in Section 8.</a></li><li>Remove the fan belt. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-002-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-002 in Section 8.</a></li><li>Remove the vibration damper(s) and fan drive pulley. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-052-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-052 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Remove the crankshaft adapter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-017-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-017 in Section 1.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><p>Remove the five front crankshaft seal mounting capscrews.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600098.png\" alt=\"01600098.png\"></figure><p>Remove and discard the front crankshaft seal from the front gear cover with the Front and Rear Crankshaft Seal Installation and Removal Tool Kit, Part Number 3163349.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600102.png\" alt=\"01600102.png\"></figure><h3>Clean</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Clean the crankshaft at the seal contact area. Use a clean cloth and solvent.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ks800sc.png\" alt=\"ks800sc.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not separate the crankshaft seal from the carrier during installation. This could cause damage to the seal faces and scrolls resulting in premature failure of the seal and oil leakage.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The use of a guide pin will make seal alignment more accurate.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not remove the seal from its packaging unless you are able to start and finish the installation in one action. Leaving the seal exposed out of its packaging can result in dirt ingress into the seal and result in premature failure of the seal and oil leakage.</p></div></div><p>Apply a light coating of clean engine oil to lubricate the rear rubber diameter of the seal.</p><p>Install the crankshaft seal carrier onto the crankshaft dry. Do <b>not</b> lubricate it.</p><p>Use hand pressure to push the rear crankshaft seal onto the crankshaft as far as possible.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600101.png\" alt=\"01600101.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not use a hammer on the tool. Damage to the threads will result. The tool can bind to the crankshaft because of the narrow tolerances.</p></div></div><p>Use the Front and Rear Crankshaft Seal Installation and Removal Tool Kit, Part Number 3163349, to install the front crankshaft seal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600102.png\" alt=\"01600102.png\"></figure><p>Install the five front crankshaft seal mounting capscrews.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews alternately and evenly.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>10 n•m [89 in-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600098.png\" alt=\"01600098.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To reduce the possibility of serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Install the crankshaft adapter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-017-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-017 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Install the vibration damper(s) and fan drive pulley. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-052-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-052 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Install the fan belt. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-002-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-002 in Section 8.</a></li><li>Install the fan spacer(s) and fan. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-040-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-040 in Section 8.</a></li><li>Operate the engine and check for leaks.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-001-024-shopas":"<h3>Install</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not separate the crankshaft seal from the carrier during installation. This could cause damage to the seal faces and scrolls resulting in premature failure of the seal and oil leakage.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The use of a guide pin will make seal alignment more accurate.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not remove the seal from its packaging unless you are able to start and finish the installation in one action. Leaving the seal exposed out of its packaging can result in dirt ingress into the seal and result in premature failure of the seal and oil leakage.</p></div></div><p>Apply a light coating of clean engine oil to lubricate the rear rubber diameter of the seal.</p><p>Install the crankshaft seal carrier onto the crankshaft dry. Do <b>not</b> lubricate it.</p><p>Use hand pressure to push the rear crankshaft seal onto the crankshaft as far as possible.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400069.png\" alt=\"01400069.png\"></figure><p>Install the new rear crankshaft seal into the flywheel housing. Use the Front and Rear Crankshaft Seal Installation and Removal Tool Kit, Part Number 3163349.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600139.png\" alt=\"01600139.png\"></figure><p>Install the four seal mounting capscrews.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>10 n•m [89 in-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400068.png\" alt=\"01400068.png\"></figure>","56-001-024-shopds":"<h3>Remove</h3><p>Remove the four rear crankshaft seal mounting capscrews.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400066.png\" alt=\"01400066.png\"></figure><p>Remove and discard the rear crankshaft seal from the flywheel housing. Use the Front and Rear Crankshaft Seal Installation and Removal Tool Kit, Part Number 3163349.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400069.png\" alt=\"01400069.png\"></figure>","56-001-024-tr":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To reduce the possibility of serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Remove the transmission, clutch, and all related components. See equipment manufacturer service information.</li><li>Remove the flywheel. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-016-005-tr\">Refer to Procedure 016-005 in Section 16.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><p>Remove the four rear crankshaft seal mounting capscrews.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400066.png\" alt=\"01400066.png\"></figure><p>Remove and discard the rear crankshaft seal from the flywheel housing. Use the Front and Rear Crankshaft Seal Installation and Removal Tool Kit, Part Number 3163349.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400069.png\" alt=\"01400069.png\"></figure><h3>Clean</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use a clean cloth and solvent to clean the crankshaft and seal mounting area.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400080.png\" alt=\"01400080.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not separate the crankshaft seal from the carrier during installation. This could cause damage to the seal faces and scrolls resulting in premature failure of the seal and oil leakage.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The use of a guide pin will make seal alignment more accurate.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not remove the seal from its packaging unless you are able to start and finish the installation in one action. Leaving the seal exposed out of its packaging can result in dirt ingress into the seal and result in premature failure of the seal and oil leakage.</p></div></div><p>Apply a light coating of clean engine oil to lubricate the rear rubber diameter of the seal.</p><p>Install the crankshaft seal carrier onto the crankshaft dry. Do <b>not</b> lubricate it.</p><p>Use hand pressure to push the rear crankshaft seal onto the crankshaft as far as possible.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400069.png\" alt=\"01400069.png\"></figure><p>Install the new rear crankshaft seal into the flywheel housing. Use the Front and Rear Crankshaft Seal Installation and Removal Tool Kit, Part Number 3163349.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600139.png\" alt=\"01600139.png\"></figure><p>Install the four seal mounting capscrews.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>10 n•m [89 in-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400068.png\" alt=\"01400068.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To reduce the possibility of serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Install the flywheel. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-016-005-tr\">Refer to Procedure 016-005 in Section 16.</a></li><li>Install the transmission, clutch, and all related components. See equipment manufacturer service information.</li><li>Operate the engine. Check for leaks.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-001-027":"<h3>General Information</h3><p>Definition of numerical callouts:</p><ol><li>Upper counterbore inside diameter</li><li>Counterbore depth</li><li>Lower counterbore inside diameter</li><li>Packing ring bore</li><li>Counterbore ledge</li><li>Counterbore radius.</li></ol><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600129.png\" alt=\"01600129.png\"></figure><h3>Inspect for Reuse</h3><p>Check the liner seat of the cylinder block for pitting.</p><p>Pitting on the liner seat is <b>not</b> acceptable.</p><p>If the cylinder bore is pitted, the counterbore <b>must</b> be machined before the cylinder block can be used.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck4slsa.png\" alt=\"ck4slsa.png\"></figure><p>Use crack detection kit, Part Number 3375432 or equivalent, to check the counterbore ledge for cracks.</p><p>Circumferential cracks of the counterbore ledge are acceptable if the cracks do <b>not</b> extend to, or over, the edge of the ledge, as shown in the illustration.</p><p>Circumferential cracks in the radius are acceptable if they do <b>not</b> extend more than 90 degrees around the circumference of the counterbore radius.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400311.png\" alt=\"01400311.png\"></figure><p>Metallurgical analysis of cross sections of counterbores having circumferential cracks has revealed that the cracks are surface initiated on the top of the counterbore ledge and normally do <b>not</b> propagate vertically through the counterbore ledge into the coolant passage around the cylinder liner.</p><p>Circumferential cracks in the radius are acceptable if they do <b>not</b> extend more than 90 degrees around the circumference of the counterbore radius.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400320.png\" alt=\"01400320.png\"></figure><p>Check the capscrew holes for cracks.</p><p>Cracks that extend from the counterbore wall to the capscrew hole are acceptable for use <b>only</b> if they do <b>not</b> extend into the threaded portion of the hole.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400313.png\" alt=\"01400313.png\"></figure><p>Cracks that extend into the threaded portion of the capscrew hole require repair with a blind-end thread insert.</p><p>Reference Section 11 (Alternative Repair Parts Group) of the Service Products Catalog, Bulletin 3377710, for a list of available thread inserts.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400314.png\" alt=\"01400314.png\"></figure><p>Check for cracks running horizontally around the vertical wall of the counterbore.</p><p>All cracked coolant passages closest to the bore <b>must</b> be repaired with coolant passage threaded inserts.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400316.png\" alt=\"01400316.png\"></figure><p>Check for cracks that run vertically to a coolant passage or a capscrew hole.</p><p>These passages <b>must</b> be repaired with coolant passage threaded inserts.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400317.png\" alt=\"01400317.png\"></figure><p>Cylinder blocks with vertical cracks that extend from a coolant passage down over the counterbore ledge can <b>not</b> be repaired.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400318.png\" alt=\"01400318.png\"></figure><p>Packing ring bores that have up to six shallow fractures, which have random origins, <b>must</b> be repaired.</p><p>Fractures that extend across the bore and are less than 4.585 mm [ 0.181 in ] deep <b>must</b> be repaired.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is the largest depth which can be repaired with the use of Cummins® repair sleeves.</p></div></div><p>Reference the Machine section below.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Any fractures that extend into the coolant passage can <b>not</b> be repaired.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600518.png\" alt=\"01600518.png\"></figure><h3>Measure</h3><p>Use a depth micrometer to measure the counterbore depth at four places 90 degrees apart, as illustrated.</p><p>The micrometer <b>must</b> contact the flat surface of the ledge and <b>must not</b> contact the radius.</p><p>If the counterbore depth does <b>not</b> meet specifications, a thicker or thinner seal ring was possibly used in a previous repair process. Measure and record the counterbore depth so that the liner protrusion can be determined.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Counterbore Depth</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>13.684</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.539</td></tr><tr><td>13.734</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.541</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The four measurements <b>must not</b> vary more than 0.055 mm [ 0.0021 in ]. If the measurements exceed the specifications, the counterbore ledge <b>must</b> be machined.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck4brta.png\" alt=\"ck4brta.png\"></figure><p>Use depth gauge assembly, Part Number 3823495, to measure the angle of the counterbore ledge at four places on the counterbore circumference.</p><p>The indicator <b>must not</b> contact the counterbore radius on a block that does <b>not</b> have a double undercut.</p><p>The measurement of the ledge depth <b>must</b> be as near to the counterbore radius as possible, and as near to the counterbore edge as possible.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck4brtb.png\" alt=\"ck4brtb.png\"></figure><p>The angle (20) of the counterbore ledge is acceptable if the measurement that is near the counterbore edge is the same or no more than 0.036-mm [0.001-in] shorter than the measurement near the counterbore radius.</p><p>If the measurement near the counterbore ledge is longer than the measurement near the counterbore radius, the ledge <b>must</b> be machined. Reference the Machine section below.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck8brna.png\" alt=\"ck8brna.png\"></figure><p>Measure the inside diameter of the upper counterbore (1).</p><p>The point of measurement <b>must</b> be within 2.54 mm [ 0.100 in ] of the top of the block.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Counterbore Diameter - Upper Press Fit Diameter</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>190.28</td><td>MIN</td><td>7.491</td></tr><tr><td>190.34</td><td>MAX</td><td>7.494</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The inside diameter of the upper counterbore <b>must</b> be completely round within 0.050 mm [ 0.002 in ]. If the measurement is <b>not</b> within specification, check to see if the block can be machined to use oversize liners.</p><p>The upper counterbore <b>must</b> be no more than 0.076 mm [ 0.003 in ] larger than the cylinder liner flange.</p><p>If the counterbore does <b>not</b> meet specifications, an oversize liner was possibly used in a previous machining bore process. Measure and record the measurement so that the proper press fit liner can be determined.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600130.png\" alt=\"01600130.png\"></figure><p>Measure the inside diameter of the lower counterbore (3).</p><p>The point of measurement <b>must</b> be within 2.54 mm [ 0.100 in ] of the top of the counterbore ledge.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Counterbore Diameter - Lower Press Fit Diameter</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>181.74</td><td>MIN</td><td>7.155</td></tr><tr><td>181.80</td><td>MAX</td><td>7.157</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The inside diameter of the lower counterbore <b>must</b> be completely round within 0.050 mm [0.002 in].</p><p>If the counterbore does <b>not</b> meet specifications, an oversize liner was possibly used in a previous machining bore process.</p><p>Measure and record the measurement so the proper press fit liner protrusion can be determined.</p><p>If the block is <b>not</b> within specifications, do <b>not</b> use the block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01k00059.png\" alt=\"01k00059.png\"></figure><p>Two sizes of oversize liners have been released: 0.25 mm [ 0.0984 in ] and 0.50 mm [ 0.0197 in ] along with oversize liner shims for the respective oversize liners. The oversize dimensional features of the liner apply to the upper press fit diameter, lower press fit diameter <b>only</b>.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The 0.25 mm [ 0.0098 in ] oversize liner has the upper press fit dimension increased by 0.25 mm [ 0.0098 in ] from its nominal dimensional value.</p></div></div><p>If an oversize liner is to be fitted, the engine block <b>must</b> be machined again for the respective oversize cylinder liner. The upper press fit (A) <b>must</b> be machined, or increased, to make sure of the correct fit of an oversize liner.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If a 0.25 mm [ 0.0098 in ] oversize liner is to be installed, the upper press fit dimension must be machined or increased by 0.25 mm [ 0.0098 in ] from its nominal dimensional value.</p></div></div><p>Any number of cylinder bores can be machined for oversize liners.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600397.png\" alt=\"01600397.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the chamfer at the top of the packing ring bore.</p><p>Excessive pitting <b>must</b> be repaired. Reference the Machine section below.</p><p>Measure the packing ring bore.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Packing Ring Bore</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>177.32</td><td>MIN</td><td>6.981</td></tr><tr><td>177.48</td><td>MAX</td><td>6.987</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600132.png\" alt=\"01600132.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Concentricity must be within specifications. Engine damage will result when the liner is not seated correctly in the bore.</p></div></div><p>Use the concentricity gauge, Part Number ST-1252, to check the cylinder bore concentricity after the counterbore ledge has been repaired.</p><p>The bore runout is half of the indicator reading.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Cylinder Block Counterbore Maximum Runout Value</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.13</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.005</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The bore <b>must</b> be repaired when consistent readings are <b>not</b> obtained. Reference the Machine section below.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck8gavd.png\" alt=\"ck8gavd.png\"></figure><p>Install a cylinder liner. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-028-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-028 in Section 1.</a></p><p>Measure the cylinder liner protrusion. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-064\">Refer to Procedure 001-064 in Section 1.</a></p><p>If the protrusion is <b>not</b> correct, remove the liner. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-028-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-028 in Section 1.</a></p><p>The protrusion can be adjusted with seal rings or by machining the counterbore ledge. Reference the Machine section below.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600184.png\" alt=\"01600184.png\"></figure><h3>Leak Test</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>To reduce the possibility of personal injury, avoid direct contact of hot oil with your skin.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Some state and federal agencies have determined that used engine oil can be carcinogenic and cause reproductive toxicity. Avoid inhalation of vapors, ingestion, and prolonged contact with used engine oil. If not reused, dispose of in accordance with local environmental regulations.</p></div></div><p>Drain the lubricating oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-037 in Section 7.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07600257.png\" alt=\"07600257.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [ 50 lb ]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Remove the lubricating oil pan. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-025-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-025 in Section 7.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07600320.png\" alt=\"07600320.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [ 50 lb ]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Remove the oil pan adapter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-027-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-027 in Section 7.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07600311.png\" alt=\"07600311.png\"></figure><p>Remove the suction and transfer tubes. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-035 in Section 7.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600064.png\" alt=\"01600064.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [ 50 lb ]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Remove the oil pump, if necessary. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-031 in Section 7.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07600382.png\" alt=\"07600382.png\"></figure><p>Pressurize the engine cooling system. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-018-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</a></p><p>Apply the air pressure 15 minutes before inspecting the cylinder liner seats. Make sure the system is holding air pressure before beginning inspection.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Measurements</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>kpa</td><td>psi</td></tr><tr><td>Air Pressure:</td><td>138</td><td>20</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800ka.png\" alt=\"ck800ka.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the outside diameter of the cylinder liners and the area below the cylinder liner seats in the cylinder block for coolant leaks.</p><p>If a leak is found, remove the cylinder liner(s).</p><p>Inspect the sealing ring and cylinder liner. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-028-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-028 in Section 1.</a></p><p>If a leak is found in the cylinder liner seat, reference the following procedure. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-028-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-028 in Section 1.</a></p><p>Inspect the cylinder block liner counterbore area.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cy8cysb.png\" alt=\"cy8cysb.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [ 50 lb ]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Install the oil pump, if removed. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-031 in Section 7.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07600382.png\" alt=\"07600382.png\"></figure><p>Install the oil suction and transfer tubes. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-035-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-035 in Section 7.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600064.png\" alt=\"01600064.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [ 50 lb ]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Install the oil pan adapter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-027-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-027 in Section 7.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07600311.png\" alt=\"07600311.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [ 50 lb ]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Install the lubricating oil pan. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-025-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-025 in Section 7.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07600320.png\" alt=\"07600320.png\"></figure><p>Fill the engine with clean engine oil. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-037 in Section 7.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07600526.png\" alt=\"07600526.png\"></figure><p>Operate the engine until it reaches a temperature of 80°C [ 176°F ].</p><p>Check for coolant and lubricating oil leaks.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07600232.png\" alt=\"07600232.png\"></figure><h3>Machine</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>If these repairs are done with the main bearing caps <b>NOT</b> installed correctly, the effectiveness of these repairs decreases.</p></div></div><p>To machine the cylinder bores, first attach the main bearing caps. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-016 in Section 1.</a></p><p>The cylinder block head deck <b>must</b> be machined before the cylinder bores if the head deck requires repair.</p><p>Use a capable machine shop to machine the cylinder bores.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600513.png\" alt=\"01600513.png\"></figure><p>Counterbore</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Below is the procedure for machining the upper counterbore.</p></div></div><p>Select the appropriate repair sleeve from the upper deck repair bushings and the available service tooling, if required. Reference Section 11 (Alternative Repair Parts Group) of the Service Products Catalog, Bulletin 3377710.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600500.png\" alt=\"01600500.png\"></figure><p>Measure and record the outer diameter or the repair sleeve.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck8smtb.png\" alt=\"ck8smtb.png\"></figure><p>Machine the top liner bore to give interference and depth according to the table below.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>“L” Shaped Sleeve Specifications (mm [ in ])</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interference Fit on Diameter</td><td>0.064 to 0.076 [ 0.0025 to 0.0030 ]</td></tr><tr><td>Depth</td><td>17.00 to 17.30 [ 0.669 to 0.681 ]</td></tr><tr><td>Corner Radius</td><td>1.87 to 2.13 [ 0.074 to 0.085 ]</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck6togc.png\" alt=\"ck6togc.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Use skin and eye protection when handling caustic solutions to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Thoroughly clean the outer diameter of the repair sleeve and cylinder block bore. Use cleaner/primer, Part Number 3824715.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600501.png\" alt=\"01600501.png\"></figure><p>Apply retaining compound, Part Number 3823718 or equivalent, to the corner of the cylinder block counterbore.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600502.png\" alt=\"01600502.png\"></figure><p>Use liquid nitrogen to shrink the repair sleeve.</p><p>Install the sleeve into the cylinder block. Make sure the repair sleeve bottoms in the counterbore.</p><p>Hold in position until the repair sleeve expands enough to remain in the correct position in the cylinder bore.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01e00087.png\" alt=\"01e00087.png\"></figure><p>Remove all traces of surplus retaining compound from the cylinder block.</p><p>Allow 3 to 4 hours for the retaining compound to cure.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600431.png\" alt=\"01600431.png\"></figure><p>Machine the sleeve to the correct specifications as indicated in the measure section above, replacing the undercut (6) with a 1.00 - 0.80 mm [.040 -.030 in] corner radius.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The sleeve will protrude above the head deck once installed and <b>must</b> be machined level with the deck head prior to machining the counterbore.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600129.png\" alt=\"01600129.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Below is the procedure for machining the packing ring bore.</p></div></div><p>Select a repair sleeve. Reference Lower Bore Repair Bushing/Tooling in Section 11 (Alternative Repair Parts Group) of the Service Products Catalog, Bulletin 3377710.</p><p>Cummins Inc. installation tooling is <b>not</b> available for this repair sleeve.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600522.png\" alt=\"01600522.png\"></figure><p>Measure the outside diameter of the repair sleeve in four equally spaced places.</p><p>Record these measurements.</p><p>This value will be used to determine the correct size to cut the cylinder block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600514.png\" alt=\"01600514.png\"></figure><p>Machine the entire length of the lower packing bore area (Y) to provide the specified interference fit between the outer diameter of the repair sleeve and the cylinder block.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Interference Fit on Diameter</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.084</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.0033</td></tr><tr><td>0.159</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.0063</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Removal of the liner catcher is required, as the sleeve will be installed from the bottom of the block.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600521.png\" alt=\"01600521.png\"></figure><p>Measure the finished bore size to verify the inside diameter and distance from the cylinder block head deck surface are sized correctly.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600515.png\" alt=\"01600515.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Thoroughly clean the bore surface area with spray cleaner, Part Number 3375433 or equivalent.</p><p>Dry with compressed air and wipe clean.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600516.png\" alt=\"01600516.png\"></figure><p>Clean the outside diameter of the repair sleeve with spray cleaner, Part Number 3375433 or equivalent.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600517.png\" alt=\"01600517.png\"></figure><p>Use liquid nitrogen to shrink the repair sleeve.</p><p>Apply a 0.8 mm [ 0.03 in ] wide band of retaining compound Loctite™ 675, or equivalent, to the machined bore.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01e00087.png\" alt=\"01e00087.png\"></figure><p>From the bottom of the engine, install the repair sleeve until the top edge is flush with the upper edge of the lower packing bore, as illustrated.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600520.png\" alt=\"01600520.png\"></figure><p>Wipe the excess Loctite™ compound from the cylinder block and upper portion of the cylinder sleeve.</p><p>Allow 3 to 4 hours for the retaining compound to cure.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600519.png\" alt=\"01600519.png\"></figure><p>Inspect all dimensions specified in the Measure section above.</p><p>Bore or hone the repair sleeve to the correct size, as required.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600515.png\" alt=\"01600515.png\"></figure><p>The cylinder block <b>must</b> be thoroughly cleaned prior to engine assembly.</p><p>For detailed cleaning instructions, reference the following procedure. Refer to Procedure 001-026 in Section 1.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600512.png\" alt=\"01600512.png\"></figure>","56-001-028-shopds":"<h3>General Information</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>There are two different piston and liner combinations available for this engine platform. The ferrous cast ductile (FCD) piston <b>must</b> be used in combination with a nitrided cylinder liner. The steel piston <b>must</b> be used in combination with a high boron liner. It is important that these parts are used in this combination stated and <b>never</b> mixed. An engine <b>must never</b> be run with a mixture of FCD and steel pistons. It <b>must</b> contain <b>only</b> a full set of FCD pistons or a full set of steel pistons. The liners can be distinguished from each other by appearance. The nitride liners will have a matte appearance on the outer circumference. The high boron liners are bright and shiny in appearance.</p></div></div><h3>Remove</h3><p>Use the cylinder liner puller, Part Number 3163745, and puller plate, Part Number 3162886, to remove the cylinder liner.</p><p>Wind down the threaded rod to extend the arm. Turn the arm to the side to enable passage through the liner.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01b00230.png\" alt=\"01b00230.png\"></figure><p>Install the cylinder liner puller, Part Number 3163745, in the cylinder liner. The puller feet <b>must not</b> touch the top of the liner. The puller arms <b>must</b> be positioned firmly on the bottom of the liner.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01b00231.png\" alt=\"01b00231.png\"></figure><p>Turn the puller screw until the liner loosens in the block.</p><p>Remove the tool and the liner.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01b00232.png\" alt=\"01b00232.png\"></figure><p>Use a liquid metal marker to mark the cylinder number and bank on each liner. Mark the cylinder liner on the camshaft side of the cylinder liner.</p><p>If sealing rings were used, use a tag to mark the cylinder number.</p><p>Measure in several places and record the thickness of the sealing rings used in each cylinder. The thickness of the sealing ring is one factor in determining liner protrusion. This information <b>must</b> be known when the liners are installed in the engine.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1cyla.png\" alt=\"ck1cyla.png\"></figure>","56-001-028-tr":"<h3>General Information</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>There are two different piston and liner combinations available for this engine platform. The ferrous cast ductile (FCD) piston <b>must</b> be used in combination with a nitrided cylinder liner. The steel piston <b>must</b> be used in combination with a high boron liner. It is important that these parts are used in this combination stated and <b>never</b> mixed. An engine <b>must never</b> be run with a mixture of FCD and steel pistons. It <b>must</b> contain <b>only</b> a full set of FCD pistons or a full set of steel pistons. The liners can be distinguished from each other by appearance. The nitride liners will have a matte appearance on the outer circumference. The high boron liners are bright and shiny in appearance.</p></div></div><h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Disconnect the batteries. Refer to the equipment manufacturer service information.</li><li>Remove the cylinder head. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-002-004-tr\">Refer to Procedure 002-004 in Section 2.</a></li><li>Remove the piston and connecting rod. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-054-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-054 in Section 1.</a></li></ul><h3>Remove</h3><p>Use the cylinder liner puller, Part Number 3163745, and puller plate, Part Number 3162886, to remove the cylinder liner.</p><p>Wind down the threaded rod to extend the arm. Turn the arm to the side to enable passage through the liner.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01b00230.png\" alt=\"01b00230.png\"></figure><p>Install the cylinder liner puller, Part Number 3163745, in the cylinder liner. The puller feet <b>must not</b> touch the top of the liner. The puller arms <b>must</b> be positioned firmly on the bottom of the liner.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01b00231.png\" alt=\"01b00231.png\"></figure><p>Turn the puller screw until the liner loosens in the block.</p><p>Remove the tool and the liner.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01b00232.png\" alt=\"01b00232.png\"></figure><p>Use a liquid metal marker to mark the cylinder number and bank on each liner. Mark the cylinder liner on the camshaft side of the cylinder liner.</p><p>If sealing rings were used, use a tag to mark the cylinder number.</p><p>Measure in several places and record the thickness of the sealing rings used in each cylinder. The thickness of the sealing ring is one factor in determining liner protrusion. This information <b>must</b> be known when the liners are installed in the engine.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1cyla.png\" alt=\"ck1cyla.png\"></figure><h3>Disassemble</h3><p>Remove and discard the two D-rings (2 and 3).</p><p>Remove and discard the crevice seal (1).</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01i00010.png\" alt=\"01i00010.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using a wire brush. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury. Make sure the wire brush is rated for the correct rpm if the brush is motor-driven.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not use a hone, aluminum oxide cloth, or sandpaper to clean the cylinder liner bores. Abrasives can damage the finish and the pattern and can contaminate the liner.</p></div></div><p>Use a high-quality steel wire brush to clean the liner flange seating area and the secondary press fit below the liner flange.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1cyeb.png\" alt=\"ck1cyeb.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using a steam cleaner, wear safety glasses or a face shield, as well as protective clothing. Hot steam can cause serious personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use a nonmetallic brush, detergent soap, and warm water to clean the inner diameter of the cylinder liner.</p><p>Clean the liners with solvent or steam.</p><p>Dry the cylinder liners with compressed air.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1cyec.png\" alt=\"ck1cyec.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline material for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Clean the bottom of the cylinder liner flange with safety solvent.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Inspect the cylinder block counterbore. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-027\">Refer to Procedure 001-027 in Section 1.</a></p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck8brea.png\" alt=\"ck8brea.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the liners for cracks on the inside and outside diameters.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1cysc.png\" alt=\"ck1cysc.png\"></figure><p>Inspect for cracks under the flange.</p><p>Cracks can also be detected by using either magnetic inspection or the dye method.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1cysd.png\" alt=\"ck1cysd.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the outside of the liner for excessive corrosion or pitting. Pits <b>must not</b> be more than 1.6 mm [0.063 in] deep.</p><p>Replace the liner if the pits are too deep or if the corrosion can <b>not</b> be removed with a fine emery cloth.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1cyse.png\" alt=\"ck1cyse.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the inside of the liner for vertical scratches deep enough to be felt with a fingernail.</p><p>If a fingernail catches in the scratch, the liner <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>Inspect the inside of the liner for scuffing or scoring.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1cysf.png\" alt=\"ck1cysf.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the inside of the cylinder liner for liner bore polishing.</p><p>A moderate polish produces a bright mirror finish in the worn area with traces of the original hone marks or an indication of etch patterns.</p><p>A heavy polish produces a bright mirror finish in the worn area, with no traces of hone marks or an etch pattern.</p><p>For further information on liner bore polishing, use the Parts Reuse Guidelines, Bulletin 3810303.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1cysg.png\" alt=\"ck1cysg.png\"></figure><p>Replace the cylinder liner if:</p><ul><li>A heavy polish is present over 20 percent of the piston ring travel area.</li><li>Thirty percent of the piston ring travel area has both moderate and heavy polish, with one-half of the 30 percent (15 percent) consisting of heavy polish.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1cysh.png\" alt=\"ck1cysh.png\"></figure><h3>Measure</h3><p>Use a dial bore gauge. Measure the inside diameter of the cylinder liner at the top, the bottom, and the middle of the piston ring travel area. Perform two measurements at each location. The measurements <b>must</b> be 90 degrees apart.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Cylinder Liner Inside Diameter</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>158.75</td><td>MIN</td><td>6.250</td></tr><tr><td>158.78</td><td>MAX</td><td>6.251</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The maximum liner ovality for all positions is 0.04 mm [0.0016 in].</p></div></div><p>If the cylinder liner is <b>not</b> within specifications, the cylinder liner <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/06400092.png\" alt=\"06400092.png\"></figure><p>Measure the cylinder liner flange outside diameter.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Upper Press Fit Cylinder Liner Flange Diameter</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>Standard</td><td>190.31</td><td>MIN</td><td>7.493</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>190.36</td><td>MAX</td><td>7.495</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the cylinder liner is <b>not</b> within specifications, it <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1brte.png\" alt=\"ck1brte.png\"></figure><p>The liner design incorporates a press fit between the upper liner bore and the area of the liner directly below the liner flange. This is referred to as the “lower press-fit” design.</p><p>Cylinder liners with standard and oversize press-fit diameters are available.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1brsw.png\" alt=\"ck1brsw.png\"></figure><p>Measure the lower press-fit outside diameter.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Lower Press-Fit Area Outside Diameter</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>Standard</td><td>181.82</td><td>MIN</td><td>7.158</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>181.86</td><td>MAX</td><td>7.160</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1brtd.png\" alt=\"ck1brtd.png\"></figure><p>Measure the cylinder liner flange thickness.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Cylinder Liner Flange Thickness</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>13.35</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.525</td></tr><tr><td>13.40</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.527</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck1cyth.png\" alt=\"ck1cyth.png\"></figure><p>Apply a thick film of clean engine oil to the bores of the liners for final cleaning. Leave the oil on for 5 to 10 minutes.</p><p>Use a clean, lint-free paper towel to wipe the oil from the bores until the black and gray deposits are removed.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> place the liners in an area where dirty airflow can contaminate the liners.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/oi1brwa.png\" alt=\"oi1brwa.png\"></figure><h3>Assemble</h3><p>The seal rings have three locating tabs on the inner diameter. The tabs have an interference fit to the liner lower press-fit diameter to hold the seal ring in place during liner installation.</p><p>Install the seal rings.</p><p>The seal ring <b>must</b> be straight on the liner upon installation. Use finger pressure to push the seal ring near the tabs to fit the seal ring down and over the lower press fit diameter during installation.</p><p>This practice during installation of the seal ring will prevent deformation that will result in the seal ring <b>not</b> fitting squarely on the bottom of the liner flange.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Cylinder Liner Seal Rings</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nominal Thickness</td><td>Number of Notches</td></tr><tr><td>0.45 mm [0.0180 in]</td><td>Two</td></tr><tr><td>0.52 mm [0.0205 in]</td><td>Two</td></tr><tr><td>0.55 mm [0.0220 in]</td><td>Two</td></tr><tr><td>0.66 mm [0.0240 in]</td><td>Two</td></tr><tr><td>0.78 mm [0.0310 in]</td><td>Two</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01800003.png\" alt=\"01800003.png\"></figure><p>Install the crevice seal. The beveled-edge of the crevice seal (2) <b>must</b> be positioned as shown.</p><p>Some o-rings have a &quot;D&quot; shape cross section. This type of o-ring <b>must</b> be installed with the flat side against the cylinder liner.</p><p>Install the o-rings in the position shown. Use the mold mark on the o-ring to check whether the o-ring is twisted.</p><ol><li>Liner, counterbore sealing ring</li><li>Crevice seal</li><li>Dark blue o-ring</li><li>Orange o-ring.</li></ol><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cy8orha.png\" alt=\"cy8orha.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><p>Apply a 2 mm [0.079 in] bead of gasket sealant, Part Number 4918771, to the corner of the cylinder block counterbore.</p><p>Make sure that the end of the bead overlaps the beginning of the bead, approximately 6 mm [0.236 in].</p><p>Install the cylinder liner within 15 minutes of applying the sealant.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01a00172.png\" alt=\"01a00172.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not use petroleum-based oil. This will cause swelling of the packing ring.</p></div></div><p>Use vegetable oil to lubricate the inside diameter of the packing ring bores.</p><p>Use hand pressure to push the cylinder liners into the block.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600109.png\" alt=\"01600109.png\"></figure><p>Use liner installation tool, Part Number 3163329, or equivalent, to install the cylinder liner. Install the bridge assembly. Install two cylinder head capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>68 n•m [50 ft-lb]</p></div></div><p>Install the push plate. Make sure it is aligned correctly in the liner. Turn the pusher screw until it touches the plate.</p><p>Use a wrench. Do <b>not</b> apply more than 135 n.m [100 ft-lb] of torque. Turn the pusher screw until the liner flange touches the counterbore ledge.</p><p>Remove the tool.</p><p>Check the liner protrusion. Use the following procedure for instructions on how to measure liner protrusion. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-064\">Refer to Procedure 001-064 in Section 1.</a></p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/cy400hc.png\" alt=\"cy400hc.png\"></figure><p>Use a dial bore gauge. Measure the inside diameter of the cylinder liner at the top, bottom, and middle of the piston ring travel area.</p><p>Perform two measurements at each location. The measurements <b>must</b> be 90 degrees apart.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>New Clinder Liner Inside Diameter</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>Positions 1, 2, and 3</td><td>158.74</td><td>MIN</td><td>6.250</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>158.78</td><td>MAX</td><td>6.251</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The maximum liner ovality for positions 1, 2, and 3 is 0.04 mm [0.0016 in].</p></div></div><p>If the cylinder liner is <b>not</b> within specifications the liner <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>Inspect for a twisted o-ring.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600303.png\" alt=\"01600303.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><ul><li>Install the piston and connecting rod assemblies. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-054-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-054 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Install the cylinder head and related components. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-002-004-tr\">Refer to Procedure 002-004 in Section 2.</a></li><li>Connect the batteries. See equipment manufacturer service information.</li><li>Operate the engine. Check for leaks.</li></ul>","56-001-030":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><ul><li>Disconnect the batteries. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-009\">Refer to Procedure 013-009 in Section 13.</a></li><li>Remove the front gear housing. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-033-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-033 in Section 1.</a></li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not allow the chisel to cut through the sleeve and damage the gear cover.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Determine the sleeve type prior to removal.</p></div></div><p>There are two gear cover trunion sleeve types:</p><ol><li>thin 3 mm [0.12 in]</li><li>thick 12 mm [0.47 in]</li></ol><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600508.png\" alt=\"01600508.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using a chisel and mallet. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>For the thin sleeve, the objective is to deform the sleeve, not to cut it into 2 pieces.</p></div></div><p>Steps for the thin gear cover trunion sleeve:</p><p>Use a chisel and mallet. Cut approximately 3/4 of the thickness of the sleeve at 2 or 3 points.</p><p>The sleeve will lose its shape and the press fit will be reduced.</p><p>Remove and discard the sleeve.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600509.png\" alt=\"01600509.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using a grinder, chisel, and mallet. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Steps for the thick gear cover trunion sleeve:</p><p>Use a suitable grinding tool to reduce an area of the sleeve to approximately 3 mm [0.12 in] thickness. Take care <b>not</b> to damage the gear cover.</p><p>Use a chisel and mallet to cut into the ground area.</p><p>The sleeve will split and the press fit will be reduced.</p><p>Remove and discard the sleeve.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600510.png\" alt=\"01600510.png\"></figure><h3>Inspect for Reuse</h3><p>Check the gear cover for cracks or other damage. If the gear cover is damaged, it <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>Use emery paper. Remove any nicks or burrs from the outside diameter of the trunion.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600511.png\" alt=\"01600511.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><p>Use Loctite® 609, or equivalent. Apply a smooth coating to the inside diameter of the sleeve.</p><p>The side of the sleeve with the widest 6.1 mm [0.24 inch] chamfer <b>must</b> be positioned toward the cover. Position the sleeve on the cover.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The thick sleeve has an identical chamfer on both sides and can be fitted in either orientation.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/gc6slha.png\" alt=\"gc6slha.png\"></figure><p>Use a hydraulic press. Support the gear cover as illustrated.</p><p>Use a flat steel plate (1). Push the sleeve (2) until the plate (1) touches the gear cover.</p><p>Check the sleeve for cracks or torn areas.</p><p>If the sleeve cracks or tears during installation, the sleeve <b>must</b> be replaced. Make sure there are no burrs on the cover. Make sure the sleeve is positioned straight with the cover before installing it with the plate and press.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/gc6slhb.png\" alt=\"gc6slhb.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><ul><li>Install the front gear housing <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-033-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-033 in Section 1.</a></li><li>Connect the batteries. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-009\">Refer to Procedure 013-009 in Section 13.</a></li><li>Operate the engine and check for proper operation.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-001-031-shopas":"<h3>Install</h3><p>with Mechanically Actuated Injector</p><p>This illustration shows the location for the six 16 mm capscrews. All of the other front cover capscrews are 12 mm.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600151.png\" alt=\"01600151.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this component.</p></div></div><p>Do <b>not</b> tighten the capscrews until the master dowel pin is installed.</p><p>The use of guide bolts will aid the assembly.</p><p>Install the front cover gasket, cover, and capscrews.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600082.png\" alt=\"01600082.png\"></figure><p>Tighten the 28 mounting capscrews in the sequence shown.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>M12 capscrews</th><th>80 n.m</th><th>[59 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>M16 capscrews</th><th>195 n.m</th><th>[144 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600152.png\" alt=\"01600152.png\"></figure><p>Install the five capscrews that attach to the bottom of the oil pan adapter.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600153.png\" alt=\"01600153.png\"></figure><p>Install the hydraulic pump drive.</p><p>Use clean engine oil to lubricate the bushing in the front gear cover.</p><p>Install the gasket, drive or cover, washers, and capscrews.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/09600041.png\" alt=\"09600041.png\"></figure><p>with Electronically Actuated Injector</p><p>This illustration shows the location for the six 16 mm capscrews. All of the other front cover capscrews are 12 mm.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600151.png\" alt=\"01600151.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this component.</p></div></div><p>Do <b>not</b> tighten the capscrews until the master dowel pin is installed.</p><p>The use of guide bolts will aid the assembly.</p><p>Install the front cover gasket, cover, and capscrews.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600082.png\" alt=\"01600082.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The number of capscrews that can be tightened at this time depends on the engine options. If the location is used to mount an accessory, it can <b>not</b> be installed at this time.</p></div></div><p>Tighten the front gear cover mounting capscrews in the sequence shown.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>M12 capscrews</th><th>80 n.m</th><th>[59 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>M16 capscrews</th><th>195 n.m</th><th>[144 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600362.png\" alt=\"01600362.png\"></figure><p>Install the five capscrews that attach to the bottom of the oil pan adapter.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600153.png\" alt=\"01600153.png\"></figure><p>Install the hydraulic pump drive.</p><p>Use clean engine oil to lubricate the bushing in the front gear cover.</p><p>Install the gasket, drive or cover, washers, and capscrews.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/09600041.png\" alt=\"09600041.png\"></figure>","56-001-031-shopds":"<h3>Remove</h3><p>with Mechanically Actuated Injector</p><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This assembly weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this assembly.</p></div></div><p>The front cover has capscrews that go up through the oil pan adapter and into the front gear cover.</p><p>Remove the 28 capscrews and washers.</p><p>Use the guide pins to support the front gear cover, slide it forward, and install the lifting eye into the threaded hole in the top center of the front gear cover.</p><p>Remove the front gear cover and gear cover gasket.</p><p>The front gear cover gasket is an edge-molded gasket. Inspect the gasket; if any damage is found, the gasket <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600082.png\" alt=\"01600082.png\"></figure><p>with Electronically Actuated Injector</p><p>Remove the five capscrews that go up through the oil pan adapter and into the front gear cover.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600153.png\" alt=\"01600153.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This assembly weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this assembly.</p></div></div><p>Remove the front gear cover capscrews and washers.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The number of capscrews depends on the engine options.</p></div></div><p>Use the guide pins to support the front gear cover, slide it forward, and install the lifting eye into the threaded hole in the top center of the front gear cover.</p><p>Remove the front gear cover and gear cover gasket.</p><p>The front gear cover gasket is an edge-molded gasket. Inspect the gasket; if any damage is found, the gasket <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600374.png\" alt=\"01600374.png\"></figure>","56-001-031-tr":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><p>with Mechanically Actuated Injector</p><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not remove the pressure cap from a hot engine. Wait until the coolant temperature is below 50°C [120°F] before removing the pressure cap. Heated coolant spray or steam can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Coolant is toxic. Keep away from children and pets. If not reused, dispose of in accordance with local environmental regulations.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This assembly weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Disconnect the batteries. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-009\">013-009</a>.</li><li>Disconnect the air starter to reduce the possibility of accidental starting. Refer to the OEM Service Manual.</li><li>Drain the cooling system. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-018-tr\">008-018</a>.</li><li>Remove the fan and fan spacer(s). Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-040-tr\">008-040</a>.</li><li>For engines that do <b>not</b> have a fan drive, remove the thermostat housing support. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-015-tr\">008-015.</a> Remove the LTA water pump. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-062-tr\">008-062</a>.</li><li>Remove the fan belt. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-002-tr\">008-002</a>.</li><li>Remove the alternator belt. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-005-tr\">013-005</a>.</li><li>Remove the alternator and bracket. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-001-tr\">013-001</a>.</li><li>Remove the fan hub. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-036-tr\">008-036</a>.</li><li>Remove the alternator and accessory drive pulleys, if equipped. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-009-004-tr\">009-004</a>.</li><li>Remove the vibration dampers. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-052-tr\">001-052</a>.</li><li>Remove the fan hub idler. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-029-tr\">008-029</a>.</li><li>Remove the front crankshaft seal. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-023-tr\">001-023</a>.</li><li>Remove the front engine support bracket. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-016-002-tr\">016-002</a>.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><p>with Electronically Actuated Injector</p><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Do not remove the pressure cap from a hot engine. Wait until the coolant temperature is below 50°C [120°F] before removing the pressure cap. Heated coolant spray or steam can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Coolant is toxic. Keep away from children and pets. If not reused, dispose of in accordance with local environmental regulations.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This assembly weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Disconnect the batteries. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-009\">013-009</a>.</li><li>Disconnect the air starter to reduce the possibility of accidental starting. Refer to the OEM Service Manual.</li><li>Remove the fan and fan spacer(s). Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-040-tr\">008-040</a>.</li><li>For engines that do <b>not</b> have a fan drive, remove the thermostat housing support. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-015-tr\">008-015.</a>.</li><li>Remove the fan belt. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-002-tr\">008-002</a>.</li><li>Remove the alternator belt. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-005-tr\">013-005</a>.</li><li>Remove the alternator and bracket. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-001-tr\">013-001</a>.</li><li>Remove the fan hub. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-036-tr\">008-036</a>.</li><li>Remove the alternator and accessory drive pulleys, if equipped. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-009-004-tr\">009-004</a>.</li><li>Remove the vibration dampers. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-052-tr\">001-052</a>.</li><li>Remove the fan hub idler. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-029-tr\">008-029</a>.</li><li>Remove the front crankshaft seal. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-023-tr\">001-023</a>.</li><li>Remove the front engine support bracket. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-016-002-tr\">016-002</a>.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><p>with Mechanically Actuated Injector</p><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This assembly weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this assembly.</p></div></div><p>The front cover has capscrews that go up through the oil pan adapter and into the front gear cover.</p><p>Remove the 28 capscrews and washers.</p><p>Use the guide pins to support the front gear cover, slide it forward, and install the lifting eye into the threaded hole in the top center of the front gear cover.</p><p>Remove the front gear cover and gear cover gasket.</p><p>The front gear cover gasket is an edge-molded gasket. Inspect the gasket; if any damage is found, the gasket <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600082.png\" alt=\"01600082.png\"></figure><p>with Electronically Actuated Injector</p><p>Remove the five capscrews that go up through the oil pan adapter and into the front gear cover.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600153.png\" alt=\"01600153.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This assembly weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this assembly.</p></div></div><p>Remove the front gear cover capscrews and washers.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The number of capscrews depends on the engine options.</p></div></div><p>Use the guide pins to support the front gear cover, slide it forward, and install the lifting eye into the threaded hole in the top center of the front gear cover.</p><p>Remove the front gear cover and gear cover gasket.</p><p>The front gear cover gasket is an edge-molded gasket. Inspect the gasket; if any damage is found, the gasket <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600374.png\" alt=\"01600374.png\"></figure><h3>Inspect for Reuse</h3><p>with Mechanically Actuated Injector</p><p>Measure the inside diameter of the water pump and accessory drive bushings.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>mm</th><th></th><th>in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>43.99</td><td>MIN</td><td>1.732</td></tr><tr><td>44.07</td><td>MAX</td><td>1.735</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the bushings are <b>not</b> within specifications. The bushings <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600355.png\" alt=\"01600355.png\"></figure><p>Measure the inside diameter of the hydraulic pump drive bushing inside diameter.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>mm</th><th></th><th>in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>43.99</td><td>MIN</td><td>1.732</td></tr><tr><td>44.07</td><td>MAX</td><td>1.735</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the bushing is <b>not</b> within specification. The bushing <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600356.png\" alt=\"01600356.png\"></figure><p>Check the gear cover for cracks or damage. If the gear cover is damaged, it <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>Use emery paper to remove any nicks or burrs from the outside diameter of the trunnion.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600229.png\" alt=\"01600229.png\"></figure><p>with Electronically Actuated Injector</p><p>There is no gear cover bushing for the water pump on engine equipped with electronically actuated injectors. A sleeve is installed in this location to block the oil passage.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600358.png\" alt=\"01600358.png\"></figure><p>Measure the inside diameter of the fuel pump drive bushings.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>mm</th><th></th><th>in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>43.99</td><td>MIN</td><td>1.732</td></tr><tr><td>44.07</td><td>MAX</td><td>1.735</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the bushing is <b>not</b> within specifications. The bushing <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600359.png\" alt=\"01600359.png\"></figure><p>Measure the inside diameter of the hydraulic pump drive bushing inside diameter.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>mm</th><th></th><th>in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>43.99</td><td>MIN</td><td>1.732</td></tr><tr><td>44.07</td><td>MAX</td><td>1.735</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>If the bushing is <b>not</b> within specification. The bushing <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600356.png\" alt=\"01600356.png\"></figure><p>Check the gear cover for cracks or damage. If the gear cover is damaged, it <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>Use emery paper to remove any nicks or burrs from the outside diameter of the trunnion.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600229.png\" alt=\"01600229.png\"></figure><h3>Disassemble</h3><p>The bushings can <b>only</b> be removed from the front gear cover after the gear cover has been removed.</p><p>The bushings can be removed from either the front or rear of the front gear cover.</p><p>Place the bushing remover against the bushing, and strike the tool with a hammer or a mallet until the bushing is removed.</p><p>Repeat the step for the remaining bushings.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600058.png\" alt=\"22600058.png\"></figure><h3>Assemble</h3><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Failure to align the bushing oil hole with the hole in the gear cover will prevent proper lubrication of the bushing.</p></div></div><p>Place the bushing into the bore and align the bushing oil hole with the oil hole inside of the bore.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600061.png\" alt=\"22600061.png\"></figure><p>Check the alignment of the bushing and the gear cover oil holes with a drill bit or a small piece of rod. If the holes are <b>not</b> aligned, remove the bushing and align the holes.</p><p>Strike the installation tool firmly with a mallet or a hammer. Continue to strike the tool until the bushing is installed. Repeat the procedure for remaining bushings.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/22600062.png\" alt=\"22600062.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><p>with Mechanically Actuated Injector</p><p>This illustration shows the location for the six 16 mm capscrews. All of the other front cover capscrews are 12 mm.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600151.png\" alt=\"01600151.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this component.</p></div></div><p>Do <b>not</b> tighten the capscrews until the master dowel pin is installed.</p><p>The use of guide bolts will aid the assembly.</p><p>Install the front cover gasket, cover, and capscrews.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600082.png\" alt=\"01600082.png\"></figure><p>Tighten the 28 mounting capscrews in the sequence shown.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>M12 capscrews</th><th>80 n.m</th><th>[59 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>M16 capscrews</th><th>195 n.m</th><th>[144 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600152.png\" alt=\"01600152.png\"></figure><p>Install the five capscrews that attach to the bottom of the oil pan adapter.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600153.png\" alt=\"01600153.png\"></figure><p>Install the hydraulic pump drive.</p><p>Use clean engine oil to lubricate the bushing in the front gear cover.</p><p>Install the gasket, drive or cover, washers, and capscrews.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/09600041.png\" alt=\"09600041.png\"></figure><p>with Electronically Actuated Injector</p><p>This illustration shows the location for the six 16 mm capscrews. All of the other front cover capscrews are 12 mm.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600151.png\" alt=\"01600151.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this component.</p></div></div><p>Do <b>not</b> tighten the capscrews until the master dowel pin is installed.</p><p>The use of guide bolts will aid the assembly.</p><p>Install the front cover gasket, cover, and capscrews.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600082.png\" alt=\"01600082.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The number of capscrews that can be tightened at this time depends on the engine options. If the location is used to mount an accessory, it can <b>not</b> be installed at this time.</p></div></div><p>Tighten the front gear cover mounting capscrews in the sequence shown.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>M12 capscrews</th><th>80 n.m</th><th>[59 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>M16 capscrews</th><th>195 n.m</th><th>[144 ft-lb]</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600362.png\" alt=\"01600362.png\"></figure><p>Install the five capscrews that attach to the bottom of the oil pan adapter.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600153.png\" alt=\"01600153.png\"></figure><p>Install the hydraulic pump drive.</p><p>Use clean engine oil to lubricate the bushing in the front gear cover.</p><p>Install the gasket, drive or cover, washers, and capscrews.</p><p>Tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/09600041.png\" alt=\"09600041.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><p>with Mechanically Actuated Injector</p><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This assembly weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this assembly.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><ul><li>Install the front crankshaft seal. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-023-tr\">001-023</a>.</li><li>Install the crankshaft adapter. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-017-tr\">001-017</a>.</li><li>Install the front engine support bracket. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-016-002-tr\">016-002</a>.</li><li>Install the vibration dampers. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-052-tr\">001-052</a>.</li><li>Install the accessory drive and alternator drive seal (if applicable). Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-003-tr\">001-003</a>.</li><li>Install the alternator and accessory drive pulleys, if equipped. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-009-004-tr\">009-004</a>.</li><li>Install the LTA water pump. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-062-tr\">008-062</a>.</li><li>Install the fan hub idler. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-029-tr\">008-029</a>.</li><li>Install the fan hub. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-036-tr\">008-036</a>.</li><li>Install the alternator and bracket. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-001-tr\">013-001</a>.</li><li>Install the alternator belt. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-005-tr\">013-005</a>.</li><li>Install the fan belt. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-002-tr\">008-002</a>.</li><li>Install the fan and fan spacer(s). Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-040-tr\">008-040</a>.</li><li>Install new full-flow oil filters. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-013-tr\">007-013</a>.</li><li>Connect the batteries. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-009\">013-009</a>.</li><li>Connect the air starter to reduce the possibility of accidental starting. Refer to the OEM Service Manual.</li><li>Fill the cooling system. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-018-tr\">008-018</a>.</li><li>Operate the engine and check for leaks.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><p>with Electronically Actuated Injector</p><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This assembly weighs 23 kg [50 lb] or more. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, use a hoist or get assistance to lift this assembly.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Batteries can emit explosive gases. To reduce the possibility of personal injury, always ventilate the compartment before servicing the batteries. To reduce the possibility of arcing, remove the negative (-) battery cable first and attach the negative (-) battery cable last.</p></div></div><ul><li>Install the front crankshaft seal. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-023-tr\">001-023</a>.</li><li>Install the crankshaft adapter. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-017-tr\">001-017</a>.</li><li>Install the front engine support bracket. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-016-002-tr\">016-002</a>.</li><li>Install the vibration dampers. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-052-tr\">001-052</a>.</li><li>Install the accessory drive and alternator drive seal (if applicable). Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-003-tr\">001-003</a>.</li><li>Install the alternator and accessory drive pulleys, if equipped. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-009-004-tr\">009-004</a>.</li><li>Install the fan hub idler. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-029-tr\">008-029</a>.</li><li>Install the fan hub. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-036-tr\">008-036</a>.</li><li>Install the alternator and bracket. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-001-tr\">013-001</a>.</li><li>Install the alternator belt. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-005-tr\">013-005</a>.</li><li>Install the fan belt. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-002-tr\">008-002</a>.</li><li>Install the fan and fan spacer(s). Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-040-tr\">008-040</a>.</li><li>Connect the batteries. Refer to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-009\">013-009</a>.</li><li>Connect the air starter to reduce the possibility of accidental starting. Refer to the OEM Service Manual.</li><li>Operate the engine and check for leaks.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-001-033-shopas":"<h3>Install</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Locate the gear housing gasket and gear housing on the locating dowels.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Loctite™ 242, Part Number 3824040, or equivalent, <b>must</b> be applied to the capscrews during installation. Loctite™ 242 is <b>not</b> required if the capscrews being used are new capscrews with a Loctite™ patch applied to the capscrew threads.</p></div></div><p>Install the mounting capscrews.</p><p>Use the sequence shown in the illustration and tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>80 n•m [59 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600214.png\" alt=\"01600214.png\"></figure>","56-001-033-shopds":"<h3>Remove</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Remove the 19 front gear housing capscrews.</p><p>Remove the front gear housing and gasket.</p><p>Discard the gasket.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The dowel pins do <b>not</b> need to be removed unless they are damaged.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600214.png\" alt=\"01600214.png\"></figure>","56-001-033-tr":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The two camshaft idler gears, camshaft gears, and crankshaft gear have index marks that are aligned during assembly. Improper alignment will cause extensive engine damage.</p></div></div><ul><li>Remove the front gear cover. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-031 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Bar the engine over to align the index marks. Align the “V” on the idler gear with the “X” on the crankshaft gear. Align the “X” on the camshaft gear at the 12 o&#x27;clock position and with the dowel holes in the front gear housing.</li><li>Remove the water pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-062-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-062 in Section 8</a>.</li><li>Remove the fuel pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-005-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 005-016 in Section 5</a>.</li><li>Remove the left bank camshaft idler gear. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-037 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Remove the right bank camshaft idler gear. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-038-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-038 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Remove the hydraulic pump idler gear. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-039-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-039 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Remove the water pump idler gear. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-040-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-040 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Remove the left and right bank camshaft gears. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-012\">Refer to Procedure 001-012 in Section 1</a>.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Remove the 19 front gear housing capscrews.</p><p>Remove the front gear housing and gasket.</p><p>Discard the gasket.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The dowel pins do <b>not</b> need to be removed unless they are damaged.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600214.png\" alt=\"01600214.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Clean the front gear housing with solvent and dry with compressed air.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/gh6hsga.png\" alt=\"gh6hsga.png\"></figure><p>Make sure the mating surfaces of the front gear housing do <b>not</b> have nicks or cracks.</p><p>If the front gear housing is damaged, repair or replace the housing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/gc900sa.png\" alt=\"gc900sa.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><p>Locate the gear housing gasket and gear housing on the locating dowels.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Loctite™ 242, Part Number 3824040, or equivalent, <b>must</b> be applied to the capscrews during installation. Loctite™ 242 is <b>not</b> required if the capscrews being used are new capscrews with a Loctite™ patch applied to the capscrew threads.</p></div></div><p>Install the mounting capscrews.</p><p>Use the sequence shown in the illustration and tighten the capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>80 n•m [59 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600214.png\" alt=\"01600214.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This component or assembly weighs greater than 23 kg [50 lb]. To prevent serious personal injury, be sure to have assistance or use appropriate lifting equipment to lift this component or assembly.</p></div></div><ul><li>Install the left and right bank camshaft gears. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-012\">Refer to Procedure 001-012 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Install the water pump idler gear. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-040-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-040 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Install the hydraulic pump idler gear. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-039-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-039 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Install the right bank idler gear. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-038-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-038 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Install the left bank idler gear. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-037-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-037 in Section 1</a>.</li><li>Install the fuel pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-005-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 005-016 in Section 5</a>.</li><li>Install the water pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-062-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-062 in Section 8</a>.</li><li>Install the front gear cover. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-031-tr\">Refer to Procedure 001-031 in Section 1</a>.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-001-035-shopas":"<h3>Install</h3><p>Standard</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p><b>:</b> For Low NOx emissions capability products, the dipstick hand hole cover is reversed, with dipstick on the left, and filling point on the right. Ensure this is fitted, to prevent interference between the filling cap and Fuel Tubes.</p></div></div><p>Use the minimum amount of stretch and do <b>not</b> allow the o-ring to twist when installing in onto the hand hole cover.</p><p>Install a new o-ring into the groove of the hand hole cover.</p><p>Lubricate the o-ring seal with clean engine oil.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/03600022.png\" alt=\"03600022.png\"></figure><p>Do <b>not</b> pull the hand hole cover into the cylinder block by tightening the capscrews.</p><p>Place the hand hole cover into the cylinder block</p><p>Turn the hand hole cover until the location holes line up with the mounting holes on the block.</p><p>Apply firm pressure, pressing the hand hole cover into place.</p><p>Install and tighten capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600370.png\" alt=\"01600370.png\"></figure><p>Block Mounted Crankcase Breather</p><p>Use the minimum amount of stretch and do <b>not</b> allow the o-ring to twist when installing in onto the hand hole cover.</p><p>Install a new o-ring into the groove of the hand hole cover.</p><p>Lubricate the o-ring seal with clean engine oil.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600367.png\" alt=\"01600367.png\"></figure><p>Do <b>not</b> pull the hand hole cover into the cylinder block by tightening the capscrews.</p><p>Place the hand hole cover into the cylinder block.</p><p>Turn the hand hole cover until the location holes line up with the mounting holes on the block.</p><p>Apply firm pressure, pressing the hand hole cover into place.</p><p>Install and tighten capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600368.png\" alt=\"01600368.png\"></figure><p>Eliminator™</p><p>Use the minimum amount of stretch and do <b>not</b> allow the o-ring to twist when installing in onto the hand hole cover.</p><p>Install a new o-ring into the groove of the hand hole cover.</p><p>Lubricate the o-ring seal with clean engine oil.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600363.png\" alt=\"01600363.png\"></figure><p>Do <b>not</b> pull the hand hole cover into the cylinder block by tightening the capscrews.</p><p>Place the hand hole cover into the cylinder block.</p><p>Turn the hand hole cover until the location holes line up with the mounting holes on the block.</p><p>Apply firm pressure, pressing the hand hole cover into place.</p><p>Install and tighten capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600369.png\" alt=\"01600369.png\"></figure>","56-001-035-shopds":"<h3>Remove</h3><p>Standard</p><p>Remove the hand hole cover capscrews.</p><p>Remove the hand hole cover.</p><p>Remove and discard the o-ring.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/03600025.png\" alt=\"03600025.png\"></figure><p>Block Mounted Crankcase Breather</p><p>Disconnect the crankcase breather pipe.</p><p>Remove the hand hole cover capscrews.</p><p>Remove the hand hole cover.</p><p>Remove and discard the o-ring.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600367.png\" alt=\"01600367.png\"></figure><p>Eliminator™</p><p>Remove the hand hole cover capscrews.</p><p>Remove the Eliminator hand hole cover. Note the location where installed.</p><p>Remove and discard the o-ring.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600363.png\" alt=\"01600363.png\"></figure>","56-001-035-tr":"<h3>Preparatory Steps</h3><p>with Mechanically Actuated Injector</p><ul><li>Remove the Crankcase Breather. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-003-001-tr\">Refer to Procedure 003-001</a>.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><p>with Electronically Actuated Injector</p><ul><li>Remove the fuel pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-005-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 005-016</a>.</li><li>Disconnect the crankcase breather. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-003-001-tr\">Refer to Procedure 003-001</a>.</li><li>Remove the electronic control module (ECM) cooling plate. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-128\">Refer to Procedure 008-128</a>.</li><li>Remove the pre-lubricating oil pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-063-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-063</a>.</li><li>Remove the water pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-062-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-062</a>.</li><li>Remove the starter motors. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-020-tr\">Refer to Procedure 013-020</a>.</li><li>Remove the lubrication oil filters (Spin-On). <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-013-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-013</a>.</li><li>Remove the eliminator filter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-067-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-067</a>.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><h3>Remove</h3><p>Standard</p><p>Remove the hand hole cover capscrews.</p><p>Remove the hand hole cover.</p><p>Remove and discard the o-ring.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/03600025.png\" alt=\"03600025.png\"></figure><p>Block Mounted Crankcase Breather</p><p>Disconnect the crankcase breather pipe.</p><p>Remove the hand hole cover capscrews.</p><p>Remove the hand hole cover.</p><p>Remove and discard the o-ring.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600367.png\" alt=\"01600367.png\"></figure><p>Eliminator™</p><p>Remove the hand hole cover capscrews.</p><p>Remove the Eliminator hand hole cover. Note the location where installed.</p><p>Remove and discard the o-ring.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600363.png\" alt=\"01600363.png\"></figure><h3>Clean and Inspect for Reuse</h3><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When using solvents, acids, or alkaline materials for cleaning, follow the manufacturer&#x27;s recommendations for use. Wear goggles and protective clothing to reduce the possibility of personal injury.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout danger\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>WARNING · Опасно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Wear appropriate eye and face protection when using compressed air. Flying debris and dirt can cause personal injury.</p></div></div><p>Use solvent to clean the hand hole covers and capscrews.</p><p>Dry with compressed air.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600364.png\" alt=\"01600364.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the hand hole covers for damage, holes, and cracks.</p><p>Replace if damaged.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600365.png\" alt=\"01600365.png\"></figure><p>Inspect the capscrews for damage and stripped threads.</p><p>Replace if damaged.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600366.png\" alt=\"01600366.png\"></figure><h3>Install</h3><p>Standard</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p><b>:</b> For Low NOx emissions capability products, the dipstick hand hole cover is reversed, with dipstick on the left, and filling point on the right. Ensure this is fitted, to prevent interference between the filling cap and Fuel Tubes.</p></div></div><p>Use the minimum amount of stretch and do <b>not</b> allow the o-ring to twist when installing in onto the hand hole cover.</p><p>Install a new o-ring into the groove of the hand hole cover.</p><p>Lubricate the o-ring seal with clean engine oil.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/03600022.png\" alt=\"03600022.png\"></figure><p>Do <b>not</b> pull the hand hole cover into the cylinder block by tightening the capscrews.</p><p>Place the hand hole cover into the cylinder block</p><p>Turn the hand hole cover until the location holes line up with the mounting holes on the block.</p><p>Apply firm pressure, pressing the hand hole cover into place.</p><p>Install and tighten capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600370.png\" alt=\"01600370.png\"></figure><p>Block Mounted Crankcase Breather</p><p>Use the minimum amount of stretch and do <b>not</b> allow the o-ring to twist when installing in onto the hand hole cover.</p><p>Install a new o-ring into the groove of the hand hole cover.</p><p>Lubricate the o-ring seal with clean engine oil.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600367.png\" alt=\"01600367.png\"></figure><p>Do <b>not</b> pull the hand hole cover into the cylinder block by tightening the capscrews.</p><p>Place the hand hole cover into the cylinder block.</p><p>Turn the hand hole cover until the location holes line up with the mounting holes on the block.</p><p>Apply firm pressure, pressing the hand hole cover into place.</p><p>Install and tighten capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600368.png\" alt=\"01600368.png\"></figure><p>Eliminator™</p><p>Use the minimum amount of stretch and do <b>not</b> allow the o-ring to twist when installing in onto the hand hole cover.</p><p>Install a new o-ring into the groove of the hand hole cover.</p><p>Lubricate the o-ring seal with clean engine oil.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600363.png\" alt=\"01600363.png\"></figure><p>Do <b>not</b> pull the hand hole cover into the cylinder block by tightening the capscrews.</p><p>Place the hand hole cover into the cylinder block.</p><p>Turn the hand hole cover until the location holes line up with the mounting holes on the block.</p><p>Apply firm pressure, pressing the hand hole cover into place.</p><p>Install and tighten capscrews.</p><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>45 n•m [33 ft-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600369.png\" alt=\"01600369.png\"></figure><h3>Finishing Steps</h3><p>with Mechanically Actuated Injector</p><ul><li>Install the Crankcase Breather. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-003-001-tr\">Refer to Procedure 003-001</a>.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure><p>with Electronically Actuated Injector</p><ul><li>Install the eliminator filter. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-067-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-067</a>.</li><li>Install the lubrication oil filters (Spin-On). <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-013-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-013</a>.</li><li>Install the starter motors. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-013-020-tr\">Refer to Procedure 013-020</a>.</li><li>Install the water pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-062-tr\">Refer to Procedure 008-062</a>.</li><li>Install the pre-lubricating oil pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-007-063-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-063</a>.</li><li>Install the electronic control module (ECM) cooling plate. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-008-128\">Refer to Procedure 008-128</a>.</li><li>Connect the crankcase breather. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-003-001-tr\">Refer to Procedure 003-001</a>.</li><li>Install the fuel pump. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-005-016-tr\">Refer to Procedure 005-016</a>.</li><li>Operate the engine and check for leaks.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/ck800wa.png\" alt=\"ck800wa.png\"></figure>","56-001-037-shopas":"<h3>Install</h3><p>The grooves in the thrust washer <b>must</b> be positioned toward the gear.</p><p>The timing marks on the camshaft idler gear <b>must</b> be visible when the gear is installed.</p><p>Use Lubriplate™ 105, or equivalent to lubricate the gear bushing, shaft, and thrust washer.</p><p>Lubricate the capscrews with clean engine oil. Assemble the parts as illustrated.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600116.png\" alt=\"01600116.png\"></figure><p>Insert the crankshaft timing service tool, Part Number 5394520, into the position shown in the front gear housing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01b02385.png\" alt=\"01b02385.png\"></figure><p>Use the crankshaft timing service tool to set the crankshaft timing mark at the Top Dead Centre (TDC) position.</p><p>Rotate the crankshaft so that the &#x27;X&#x27; timing mark on the crankshaft gear aligns as closely as possible to the center line on the crankshaft timing tool.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The &#x27;X&#x27; timing mark on the crankshaft gear <b>must</b> fall between the two outer lines on the crankshaft timing tool.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01b02386.png\" alt=\"01b02386.png\"></figure><p>Align the “V” on the idler gear with the “X” on the crankshaft gear. Align the “X” on the camshaft gear at 12 o&#x27;clock and with the dowel holes in the front gear housing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600086.png\" alt=\"01600086.png\"></figure><p>Rotate the idler shaft as necessary to align the mounting capscrew holes.</p><p>The oil holes in the idler shaft <b>must</b> be placed in the vertical position.</p><p>Use the capscrews to pull the shaft into the bore.</p><p>Using the following steps, tighten the capscrews in the sequence shown.</p><p>Torque Value:</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600146.png\" alt=\"01600146.png\"></figure><p>Measure the camshaft idler gear end clearance.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Left Bank Camshaft Idler Gear End Clearance</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>mm</td><td></td><td>in</td></tr><tr><td>0.15</td><td>MIN</td><td>0.006</td></tr><tr><td>0.33</td><td>MAX</td><td>0.013</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/if400ta.png\" alt=\"if400ta.png\"></figure>"};
